hadiths[523]{hadithnumber,text}:
"397","Muhammad bin Bashar Bandar told us, Abd al-Wahhab told us, Ayoub told us, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, Malik bin al-Huwayrith told us, he said: We came to the Messenger of We were young people, may God bless him and grant him peace. We stayed for twenty nights, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was merciful and gentle. When he thought that we had missed our families, or were missing him, he asked about what we had left behind, so we told him, and he said: “Go back to your families. So stay among them, teach them and guide them,” and he mentioned things that I have memorized and things that I do not, “and pray as you have seen me praying, then Prayer has come, so let one of you call the call to prayer, and let the eldest of you lead.” Yahya bin Hakim narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab bin Abd al-Majid narrated to us, similar to the hadith of Bundar, and perhaps he differed from him in some wording."
"398","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim and Abu Hashim told us, they said: Ismail told us, Ayoub told us, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Malik bin Al-Huwayrith, and he mentioned The hadith in its entirety"
"399","It is narrated by Ismail bin Bishr bin Mansour Al-Sulaymi, on the authority of Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, who heard the Prophet pray May God bless him and grant him peace. A man was on his way, saying: God is great, God is great, and the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “On fitrah.” He said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. He said: “He came out of the Fire,” so he raced ahead of the people to the man. Suddenly, a shepherd attended prayer, so he stood up and called the call to prayer."
"400","We have Muhammad bin Abi Safwan Al-Ali, we have Bahz, meaning Ibn Asad, we have Hammad bin Salamah, Thabit told us, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He used to change his mind during the morning prayer. If he heard the call to prayer, he would stop. If not, he would feel jealous. One day he listened and heard a man saying: God He is the greatest, God is the greatest. He said: “On fitrah.” He said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. He said: “I came out of the Fire.” Abu Bakr said: If a person aspires to bear witness to the monotheism of God in the call to prayer, and he hopes that God will save him from the Fire By bearing witness to God and to the monotheism in His call to prayer, every believer should hasten to this virtue, hoping that God will save him from Hellfire, alone in his house or in a desert, village, or city, in pursuit of this virtue. The chapters on the call to prayer in travel were also included in Places other than this place, in the sleep of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, after the morning prayer until the sun rose, and his command, may God bless him and grant him peace, was with Bilal With the call to prayer for Fajr after the end of the time for that prayer, and these reports also contradict the statement of those who claimed that the call to prayer is not called after the end of at that time, but it is held for it without a call to prayer."
"401","Narrated by Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Ala’, narrated by Sufyan, who said: I heard al-Zuhri narrate something: Salem told me, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Bilala gives the call to prayer at night, so eat and drink until you hear the call to prayer of Ibn Umm Maktum.” Al-Makhzoumi narrated it, Sufyan narrated it, and he said in all of them: On the authority of, on the authority of"
"402","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Habib bin Al-Shahid narrated to us, Al-Mu`tamir narrated to us, saying: I heard my father, narrated by Abu Uthman, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Let not any of you prevent Bilal’s call to prayer from his suhoor meal, for he is giving the call to prayer or calling for your leader to return and pay attention.” Your sleeper, and he does not say thus and thus, rather he says thus and thus.” It was narrated to us by Yusuf bin Musa, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Suleiman, who is Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, with this"
"403","From Abdul Rahman bin Bishr bin Al-Hakam, from Yahya, meaning Ibn Saeed, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, may God Almighty be pleased On her authority, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Bilal gives the call to prayer at night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum gives the call to prayer,” and there was no one between them. Except the extent to which this one ascends and this one descends."
"404","Abu Hashem told us Ziyad bin Ayyub, Hisham told us, Mansour, who is Ibn Zazan, told us, on the authority of Khubayb bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his paternal aunt Unaysa bint Khubayb said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When Ibn Umm Maktum gives the call to prayer, then eat and drink, and when Bilal gives the call to prayer, So do not eat or drink.” If the woman is one of us and has some of her suhoor left, she should say to Bilal: Give some time until I finish my suhoor. Abu Bakr said: This is news about which there is disagreement, on the authority of Khubayb bin Abdul Rahman. Shu’bah narrated it on the authority of his aunt Anisa, and he said: Ibn Umm Maktum or Bilala calls out at night"
"405","It was narrated by Muhammad bin Bashar, it was narrated by Muhammad bin Jaafar, it was narrated by Shu’bah, on the authority of Khubayb, who is the son of Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his paternal aunt Anisa, who was On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Indeed, Ibn Umm Maktum or Bilal calls for the night, so eat and drink, until Bilal or Ibn Umm calls.” Maktoum,” and all that happened was for one of them to get down and the other to sit down, and she would take his garment and say: “As you are until I prepare for suhoor.” It was narrated by Ahmad ibn Miqdam al-Ijli, it was narrated by Yazid ibn Zuray’, Shu’bah narrated to us something similar. Abu Bakr said: The story of Anisa had a disagreement over this wording, but Al-Darawardi narrated, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Aisha, similar to the meaning of the news of Mansur bin Zazan in this word."
"406","On the authority of Muhammad ibn Yahya, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Hamza, on the authority of Abdul Aziz, meaning Ibn Muhammad, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, Ibn Umm Maktum gives the call to prayer at night, so eat and drink until Bilal gives the call to prayer, for Bilal does not give the call to prayer at night.” He calls the call to prayer until he sees the dawn.” Something similar to this meaning was narrated by Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha"
"407","Nahi, Ahmed bin Mansour Al-Ramadi, Abu Al-Mundhir, Yunus, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, Al-Aswad bin Yazid, he said: I said To Aisha: What time do you feel stressed? She said: “I will not perform the Witr prayer until they call the call to prayer, and they do not call the call to prayer until dawn comes.” She said: And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had two muezzins. And Amr bin Umm Maktoum, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When Amr gives the call to prayer, eat and drink, for he is a blind man. And when Bilal gives the call to prayer, raise your hands, for Bilal does not give the call to prayer until morning.”"
"408","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Sa‘īd al-Dārimī and Muḥammad ibn ‘Uthmān al-‘Ijlī:\n‘Ubaydullāh ibn Mūsā narrated to us, from Isrā’īl, from Abū Isḥāq, from al-Aswad, from ‘Ā’ishah (RA), who said:\n“The Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) had three mu’adhdhins: Bilāl, Abū Maḥdhurah, and ‘Amr ibn Umm Makṭūm. The Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) said:\n‘When ‘Amr gives the call to prayer, he is blind and his call should not deceive you. When Bilāl gives the call to prayer, let no one break his fast.’”\n\nAbū Bakr (ibn Abī Shaybah) said:\nAs for the report of Abū Isḥāq from al-Aswad from ‘Ā’ishah, it is worthy of scrutiny, for I have not been able to confirm that Abū Isḥāq heard this report directly from al-Aswad. However, the report of Hishām ibn ‘Urwah from his father is sound in its transmission. Moreover, this report does not contradict the report of Sālim from Ibn ‘Umar or the report of al-Qāsim from ‘Ā’ishah, for it is possible that the Prophet (ﷺ) had assigned the night-time calls to prayer alternately between Bilāl and Ibn Umm Makṭūm. Thus, on some nights he would command Bilāl to give the first call before dawn; when Bilāl descended, Ibn Umm Makṭūm would ascend and give the second call at daybreak. When it was Ibn Umm Makṭūm’s turn, he would give the first call at night, and when he descended, Bilāl would ascend and give the second call at daybreak.\n\nThe statement of the Prophet (ﷺ) means that Bilāl would give the first call at night during the time that Bilāl’s night-time call was due, and that Ibn Umm Makṭūm would give the first call at night during the time that Ibn Umm Makṭūm’s night-time call was due. The Prophet (ﷺ) thereby informed the people at both times that the first call was a night-time call, not a day-time one, and that it did not prevent those who wished to fast from eating or drinking. The second call, however, did prevent food and drink, for it was given at daybreak, not night.\n\nAs for the report of al-Aswad from ‘Ā’ishah—“they do not give the call to prayer until dawn breaks”—it has two possible meanings:\n1. Not all of them give the call until dawn breaks; it does not mean that none of them gives the call before dawn. Do you not see that the report states, “When ‘Amr gives the call, eat and drink”? If ‘Amr did not give the call until dawn broke, then eating and drinking after his call would be forbidden for the faster, which is not the case.\n2. ‘Ā’ishah meant that they would not give the call until the first dawn broke, at which point the first caller among them would give the call after the first dawn but before the second dawn. This is the time when food and drink are still lawful for those intending to fast, for the first dawn appears at night, not day. Then the next caller would give the call after the second dawn, which is daybreak, not night.\n\nThis, in my view, is the meaning of this report. And Allāh knows best.\n\n**CHAPTER:**"
"409","Harun bin Ishaq Al-Hamdani narrates, Ibn Fudayl narrates, on the authority of Husayn bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, on the authority of his father He said: We walked with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, one night, and some of the people said: If you had intercourse with us, O Messenger of God, he said: “I am afraid That you sleep and miss the prayer.” He mentioned the hadith in full, and said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, woke up, then he said: “O Bilal, get up and call the people to prayer.” \By prayer\"""""
"410","Muhammad bin Abi Safwan Al-Thaqafi told us, Bahz, meaning Ibn Asad, told us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, told us, Thabit Al-Bunani told us, that Abdullah bin Rabah spoke to the people in the Jami’ Mosque, and among the people was Imran bin Husayn. Imran said: Who is the boy? He said: A man from the Ansar, and Imran said: These people are more knowledgeable about their narration. Look at how you narrate it, for I am on the seventh of that night with the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Imran said: I did not see anyone who memorized this hadith except me. He said: I heard Abu Qatada say: We He was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey. He said: “Unless you reach water the next day you will be thirsty.” So the people quickly set off. Abu Qatada said: I stayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that night. He fell asleep and fell asleep, so I supported him. Then he fell asleep again, so he leaned over and I supported him. Then he fell asleep and leaned over again until He was about to startle, then he woke up and said: “Who is the man?” I said: Abu Qatada. He said: “How long has this been your journey?” I said: Since tonight, He said: “May God protect you as you protected His Prophet.” Then he said: “If we had a wedding.” He leaned toward a tree and I leaned with him. He said: “Do you see anyone?” I said: Yes, this is a rider, this is a rider, these are two riders, these are three, until we became seven, and he said: “Guard our prayers, and we will not sleep for a while.” Fajr prayer,” and he beat their ears until the heat of the sun woke them up, so they stood up and led a greeting, then they came down, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “Do you have any water?” I said: Yes, I have a basin with water in it. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Bring it.” So I brought it to him, and he said: “Touch some of it. “Touch some of it.” We performed ablution and there was a portion of it left. He said: “Take it, O Abu Qatada, for there is news about this.” So Bilal gave the call to prayer, so they prayed They performed the two dawn rak'ahs, then they prayed the dawn prayer, then they rode off, and some of them said to one another: We were negligent in our prayer, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: What do you say? If it is a matter of your world, then it is your business, and if it is a matter of your religion, then it is up to me.” We said: O Messenger of God, let us neglect our prayers. He said: “There is no negligence in sleep, but rather negligence in being awake, and if one of you neglects to pray, let him pray it when he remembers it, and from the next day.” Immediately.” He mentioned the length of the hadith."
"411","We are Amr bin Ali, we are Yahya bin Saeed, we are Malik, we are Al-Zuhri. H, Amr bin Ali, Othman bin Omar, Yunus bin Yazid Al-Ayli, narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri. H Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Malik bin Anas told us, and Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ata’ Ibn Yazid Al-Laythi, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When you hear the caller, say something like this.” \He says\"""""
"412","Abu Hashim told us Ziyad bin Ayyub, Hushaym told us, Abu Bishr told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Malih, on the authority of Abdullah bin Utba bin Abu Sufyan, on the authority of his paternal aunt, Umm Habibah bint Abu Sufyan, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was with her in On that day, he heard the muezzin giving the call to prayer, and he said as the muezzin says until he finished.”"
"413","On the authority of Bundar, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, on the authority of Bahz ibn Asad, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Abu al-Malih, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Utbah, on the authority of Umm Habibah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to say as the muezzin says, until the muezzin silenced.”"
"414","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi told us, Ibn Ulayya told us, on the authority of Hisham Al-Dastawai, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Issa bin Talha, said: We entered with Muawiyah, and the caller called for prayer, and said: God is great, God is great, so Muawiyah said: God is the greatest, God is the greatest, then he said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and Muawiyah said: I bear witness, then he said: I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger God, so Muawiyah said: And I bear witness, then he said: Hail to the prayer, so Muawiyah said: There is no power nor strength except in Allah, then he said: Hail to the farmer, Muawiyah said: There is no power nor strength except in God. Then he said: This is how I heard your Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, say."
"415","We are Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala, we are Harmala, meaning Ibn Abdul-Aziz, my father told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yusuf, the client of Othman bin Affan, he said: The muezzin called the call to prayer and said: God is the greatest, God is the greatest. Then Muawiyah bin Abi Sufyan said: God is the greatest. God is the greatest. So he said: I bear witness that no There is no god but Allah. Muawiyah said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. He said: I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. Muawiyah said: I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God. God, then Muawiyah said: This is how I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say."
"416","We are Bundar, we are Yahya bin Saeed, we are Muhammad bin Amr, my father told me, on the authority of my grandfather, he said: I was with Muawiyah bin Abi Sufyan. The muezzin said: “God is the greatest, God is the greatest.” Mu’awiyah said: God is the greatest, God is the greatest. Then he said: I bear witness that there is no god but God. So he said: Muawiyah: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. He said: I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. Muawiyah said: I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. He said: I live. On prayer, so Muawiyah said: There is no power nor strength except with God, so he said: Hail to the farmer, so Muawiyah said: There is no power nor strength except with God, so he said: God The greatest, God is the greatest, there is no god but God, so Muawiyah said: God is the greatest, God is the greatest, there is no god but God, then he said: This is how the Messenger of God was May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he says. Abu Bakr said: And the news of Omar bin Al-Khattab from this chapter as well, I mentioned it in another chapter. Abu Bakr said: The meaning of the news of a mother Habiba: He said as the muezzin says until he finishes, that is, except for his saying: Hail to prayer, hail to success, and likewise the meaning of the news of Abu Sa’id: So say As he says: That is, with the exception of his saying: He lives on the prayer, he lives on the farmer, and the news of Omar bin Al-Khattab and Muawiyah are interpreters of these two reports, and it has been explained in Omar and Muawiyah reported that whoever hears this herald calling for prayer is merely saying the same as what he says, except for his saying, “Haya to the prayer,” “Haya to the farmer,” And he says: When the muezzin says: Hail to the prayer, Hail to the success: There is no power nor strength except in God, the one who is praying, and the muezzin does not say there is no power nor strength. Except by God in His call to prayer. This statement from the listener of the muezzin is not what the muezzin says."
"417","On the authority of Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Jahdham, on the authority of Ismail ibn Jaafar, on the authority of Amara ibn Ghaziyah, on the authority of Khubayb ibn Abd Al-Rahman, on the authority of Hafs bin Asim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather Omar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If the muezzin says: God He is the greatest, God is the greatest, and one of you said: God is the greatest, God is the greatest, then he said: I bear witness that there is no god but God, so he said: I bear witness that there is no god but God God, then he said: I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, he said: I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, then he said: Live for prayer, he said: There is no power nor strength except By God, then he said: Hail to the farmer, he said: There is no power nor strength except by God, then he said: God is great, God is great, he said: God is great, God is great Akbar, then he said: There is no god but Allah. He said: There is no god but Allah from his heart, and he entered Paradise.”"
"418","On the authority of Muhammad ibn Aslam, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Muqri, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Abi Ayyub, on the authority of Ka`b ibn Alqamah, on the authority of Abdul Rahman ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said. H Abu Harun Musa ibn al-Nu`man told us about Fustat, Abu Abd al-Rahman, meaning the reciter, Haywa, Ka`b ibn Alqamah told me On the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Jubayr, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Amr saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “If You heard the muezzin, so say what he says, then pray for me, for whoever prays upon me, God will pray upon him ten times, then ask God for the means for me. And it is a degree in Paradise that is appropriate only for a servant of God, so whoever asks Me for a means, intercession will be permitted for him.” This is the wording of the hadith. Haywa, and in the news of Saeed bin Abi Ayoub, he said: “And I hope that I am him.”"
"419","Muhammad bin Yahya and Zakaria bin Yahya bin Aban told us, they said: Ibn Abi Maryam told us, Musa bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Hazim told me, Sahl bin Saad told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There are two things that are not rejected, or are rarely rejected: supplication at the time of the call, And in times of battle, when they join one another.”"
"420","Musa bin Sahl al-Ramli told us, Ali bin Ayyash told us, Shuaib bin Abi Hamza told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir bin Abd God, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever says when he hears the call: O God, Lord of this perfect call and the established prayer, come to Muhammad means and virtue, and raise him to the Praiseworthy Station which You promised him, unless intercession becomes permissible for him on the Day of Resurrection.”"
"421","We are Al-Rabi’ bin Suleiman Al-Muradi, we are Shuaib, meaning Ibn Al-Laith. H Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam narrated to us, Ubayy and Shuaib narrated to us, saying: Al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hakim bin Abdullah bin Qais. On the authority of Amer bin Saad bin Abi Waqqas, on the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: “Whoever said when The muezzin is heard: And I bear witness that there is no god but God alone, with no partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. I am satisfied with God as Lord, and with Muhammad Messenger, and with Islam as religion, his sins will be forgiven.”"
"422","On the authority of Zakaria ibn Yahya ibn Iyas, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Ufayr, on the authority of Yahya ibn Ayyub, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn al-Mughirah, on the authority of al-Hakim ibn Abdullah bin Qais, on the authority of Amer bin Saad bin Abi Waqqas, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever hears The muezzin was reciting the tashahhud, so he turned to face him and said: I bear witness that there is no god but God alone, with no partner, and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God. I am satisfied with God. usury, and with Islam as religion, he will be forgiven for his previous sins.”"
"423","From Muhammad bin Bashar, from Hisham bin Al-Walid, from Hammad, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala, on the authority of Mutarrif bin Abdullah, on the authority of Uthman Ibn Abi Al-Aas, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, teach me the Qur’an and make me the imam of my people. He said: So he said: “Imitate the weakest of them, and take a muezzin who does not He will receive a reward for his call to prayer.” It is narrated by Bundar, narrated by Abu Al-Numan, narrated by Hammad, narrated by Al-Jariri, on the authority of Yazid Abi Al-Ala, with this chain of transmission similar to it, and he did not say: Teach me the Qur’an. And he said: He said: “You are their imam, and follow the weakest of them.”"
"424","On the authority of Bundar, on the authority of Hammad ibn Masada, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Bilal gives the call to prayer.” At night, eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum gives the call to prayer.” Ubayd Allah said: I heard Al-Qasim narrating that, on the authority of Aisha, may God Almighty be pleased with her, who said: But there was only a matter of what came down between them. This, and this goes up"
"425","Ahmad bin Al-Miqdam Al-Ajli told us, Yazid told us, meaning Ibn Zuray’, we told Israel bin Yunus, on the authority of Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Burayd bin Abi Maryam, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The supplication between the call to prayer and the iqama is not rejected, so pray.”"
"426","Muhammad bin Khaled bin Khadash Al-Zahran told us, Sallam bin Qutayba told us, on the authority of Yunus bin Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Burayd bin Abi Maryam, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The supplication between the call to prayer and the iqama is not rejected.”"
"427","This is Ahmad bin Mansour al-Ramadi, Abu al-Mundhir narrates Ismail bin Omar al-Wasiti, Yunus narrates, Burayd bin Abi Maryam narrates us, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The supplication between the call to prayer and the iqamah is not rejected, so supplicate.” Abu Bakr said: He wants the invitation to be answered. Ahmad ibn Mani` narrated to us, Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Israel narrated to us, similar to the hadith of Yazid ibn Zuray’."
"428","From Abu Musa Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna, from Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Sufyan, Abu Ishaq told me, he said, I heard Al-Bara’, saying: “We prayed “We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, toward the Holy House for sixteen or seventeen months, then we turned toward the Kaaba.”"
"429","Narrated by Muhammad bin Isa, narrated by Salamah, meaning Ibn al-Fadl, narrated by Muhammad bin Ishaq, who said: Ma’bad bin Ka’b bin Malik narrated to me, and he was one of the The most knowledgeable of the Ansar, he told me, that his father Ka’b told him, and Ka’b bin Malik told me about the Ansar’s departure from Medina to Mecca in the pledge of allegiance. Aqaba, and it was mentioned in the report that Al-Baraa bin Ma’rour said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: I set out on this journey of mine and God has guided me. For Islam, so I decided not to leave this structure behind me, so I prayed to it, and my companions disagreed with me in that matter until I fell into a state of anxiety within myself. That is something, so what do you see? He said: “You could be facing the qiblah if you were patient with it.” He said: Al-Baraa returned to the qiblah of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and prayed with us until The Levant"
"430","Narrated to us Muhammad bin Abi Safwan Al-Thaqafi, narrated to us by Bahz, meaning Ibn Asad, narrated to us by Hammad bin Salamah, narrated by Thabit, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He and his companions were praying towards the Holy House, so when this verse was revealed {Then turn your face toward the Sacred Mosque} [Al-Baqarah: 144] A man from Banu Salamah passed by and called out to them while they were bowing in the Fajr prayer, but the qiblah had been turned towards the Kaaba, so they turned and bowed.”"
"431","Narrated to us Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad, my father told me, narrated to me Hammad, on the authority of Thabit,  on the authority of Anas, who said: They were praying towards the Holy House, so he mentioned Like it, and added it, and they repeated their previous prayers."
"432","Narrated to us by Muhammad Ibn Yahya, by Abd al-Razzaq, Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: Usama Ibn Zayd informed me, When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered the house, he supplicated in all its directions and did not pray in it until he left it. When he left, he bowed two rak’ahs in front of the house. The Kaaba, and he said: “This is the qiblah.”"
"433","Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Ata’, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas, saying: Usama bin told me Zaid, that when the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered the house, he prayed in all its parts, and did not pray in it until he left it, so when he left, he prayed two rak’ahs in it. He kissed the Kaaba, and said: “This is the qiblah.” And in the news of Al-Baraa bin Aazib: Then we turned towards the Kaaba. Israel said, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Baraa: Then he was directed to the Kaaba, and he liked to be directed to the Kaaba. Nah Salam bin Junada, Waki` told us, on the authority of Israel"
"434","Narrated by Abdullah bin Ishaq Al-Jawhari, Abu Asim told us, Othman bin Saad told us, Anas bin Malik told us, he said: “The Messenger of God prayed May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he spent several months in the direction of the Holy House. One day, while he was praying the noon prayer, he prayed two rak’ahs when he turned to the Kaaba. Then the foolish ones said: “What turned them away from the qiblah which they used to follow.” Surah Al-Baqarah, verse 142."
"435","Abdullah bin Ishaq Al-Jawhari told us, Abu Asim told us, Malik bin Anas told us, Abdullah bin Dinar told me, on the authority of Ibn Umar, The people of Quba were praying before the Holy House, and someone came to them and said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the Qur’an was revealed to him. And he headed towards the Kaaba, and they faced it, and they turned around as they were.” And in the news of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was directed to the Kaaba"
"436","And in the news of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: Then he was directed to the Kaaba. In the news of Thumama bin Abdullah, on the authority of Anas, a caller to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and said: “The qiblah has been turned to \The Kaaba.\"" I have included all these reports in the Great Book of Prayer. Abu Bakr said: All of these reports indicate that the qiblah is the Kaaba. In the report of Abu Hazim"
"437","Muhammad bin Yahya narrated, Ahmad bin Khalid al-Wahbi narrated, Sharik narrated us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Baraa, he said: “I prayed with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace “peace be upon him, towards the Holy House for sixteen months.” He mentioned the hadith and said: Al-Bara’ said: “And the part among us is before it.”"
"438","Narrated by Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Ala’, narrated by Sufyan, on the authority of Amr, who is Ibn Dinar, who said: Ibn Abbas recited: “Shall we bind you to it from within ourselves? On our own initiative.” I have included this section completely in the Book of Interpretation."
"439","On the authority of Imran bin Musa al-Qazzaz, on the authority of Abd al-Warith, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Abu al-Qasim said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “If one of you performs ablution in his house and then comes to the mosque, he will be in prayer until he returns, and he should not say like this, and he should intertwine between His fingers"
"440","On the authority of Abdullah bin Hashim, on the authority of Yahya, he is Ibn Sa’id, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He greeted and said to Ka’b ibn Ujrah: “If you perform ablution and then enter the mosque, do not clasp your fingers together.”"
"441","Abu Bakr said: This news was narrated by Dawud bin Qais Al-Farra’, on the authority of Saad bin Ishaq bin Ka’b bin Ujrah, on the authority of Abu Thumama, He is the tailor. Ka’b bin Ujrah told him on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: “If one of you performs ablution, then goes out to the mosque, so he should not interlace his fingers; For it is in prayer.” Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Dawud bin Qays told me"
"442","It was narrated by Anas bin Iyad, on the authority of Saad bin Ishaq bin Ka’b, on the authority of Abu Sa’id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Thumama, and Yunus bin Abd. The highest, Anas bin Iyadh told me, on the authority of Saad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Sa’id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Thumama, who said: I met Ka’b bin Ujrah I wanted to pray Friday prayer, and I had intertwined my fingers. When I approached, he struck my hand and separated my fingers, and said: “We have forbidden anyone from intertwining... His fingers while praying.” I said: I am not praying. He said: Didn’t you perform ablution when you wanted to perform Friday prayer? I said: Yes. He said: “Then you are in prayer.”"
"443","It was narrated by Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Maqbari, on the authority of a man from Banu Salim who told him on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Ka’b ibn Ujrah. Muhammad narrated it. Ibn Rafi’, Ibn Abi Fudaik told us, Ibn Dhib told us, Abu Bakr said: Sa’d bin Ishaq bin Ka’b is from Banu Salim"
"444","It was narrated by Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Ka’b. Abu Sa’id Al-Ashjaj narrated it, not Abu Khaled, on the authority of Ibn Two wheels. Khaled bin Hayyan Al-Raqqi brought a piece of paper, which he narrated on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, and Ja’far bin Muhammad Al-Thaalabi, Khaled told us, meaning Ibn Hayyan Al-Raqi."
"445","Abu Bakr said: It is not permissible for anyone to narrate this news from me except in this form. This is an inverted chain of transmission, so it is similar to what was narrated by Anas ibn Iyaad being authentic. Because Dawud bin Qais omitted from the chain of transmission Abu Sa`id al-Maqbari, so he said: On the authority of Saad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Thumama, and as for Ibn Ajlan misunderstood the chain of transmission and made mistakes in it. One time he said: On the authority of Abu Hurairah, and another time he sent it, and another time he said: On the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Ka’b. Ibn Abi Dhib explained that Al-Maqbari Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id only narrated it on the authority of a man from Banu Salem, and to me he is Sa’d bin Ishaq. However, he made a mistake about Saad bin Ishaq and said: On the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather Ka’b. Dawud bin Qais and Anas bin Iyaad all agreed that the news is only on the authority of Abu Thumamah."
"446","It was narrated by Muhammad bin Muslim Al-Taifi, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, who said: Al-Maqbari informed me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He, peace and blessings be upon him: “Whoever performs ablution and then goes out wanting to pray, then he is in prayer until he returns to his house, and he does not say: This means interlocking his fingers.” Nah Al-Fadl bin Yaqoub Al-Rakhami, Al-Haytham bin Jamil told us Muhammad bin Muslim, and it was narrated by Sharik, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Kitten"
"447","Imran bin Musa Al-Qazzaz told us, on the authority of Abdul-Warith, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “If one of you performs ablution in his house and then comes to the mosque, and he is in prayer until he returns, he should not say like this. And he interlaced his fingers.”"
"448","From Harun bin Ishaq Al-Hamdani, from Ibn Fudayl, from Husayn bin Abdul Rahman, from Habib bin Abi Thabit, from Muhammad bin Ali bin Abdullah bin Abbas, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, that he fell asleep with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Then the muezzin came to him, and he went out to pray, saying: “O God, put light in my heart, and place light in my tongue, and place light in my hearing, and place light in my sight.” Light, and make light behind me, and light before me, and make light above me, and light below me, O God, make light greater for me.” Abu Bakr said: There was something in the heart of this chain of transmission, for Habib ibn Abi Thabit is a deceiver, and I did not know whether Habib had heard this news. From Muhammad bin Ali or not, then I looked, and behold, Abu Awanah narrated it on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, he said: Muhammad bin narrated to me Ali"
"449","On the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya, on the authority of Abu Al-Walid, on the authority of Abu Awanah, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, that Muhammad bin Ali bin Abd Allah Ibn Abbas narrated to him, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I spent the night at my aunt Maimuna’s, so he mentioned the hadith."
"450","Ahmad ibn Abdah al-Dhabi informed us, Abbad, meaning Ibn Abbad al-Muhallabi, informed us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, He said: He was a man from the Ansar whose house was the furthest house in the city, and he never failed to pray with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I was sad for him. So I said: O so-and-so, if only you had bought a donkey that would protect you from the affliction, protect you from the scourges, and protect you from the vermin of the earth. So he said to him: By God, I do not like My house is surrounded by the house of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: So I carried a burden with it until I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I mentioned that to him. He said: So he summoned him, asked him, and mentioned something like that to him, so he mentioned that he hoped to follow him, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Indeed For what you expected.”"
"451","Imran bin Musa Al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Abdul-Warith narrated to us, Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Nadra, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: The areas around the mosque, so Banu Salamah wanted to be near the mosque, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was informed of that, and he said: “O Banu Salamah, Did you want to move near the mosque? They said: Yes. He said: O Banu Salamah, your homes write your tracks. He said it three times. I have completely excluded the chapter on walking to the mosques in the book on Imamate."
"452","We are Muhammad bin Bashar, we are Abu Bakr, meaning the Hanafi, we are al-Dahhak, who is Ibn Uthman, Sa`id al-Maqbari told me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you enters the mosque, let him greet the Prophet, and say: O God, open for me the doors of your mercy. And when he goes out, let him greet the Prophet and say: O God, protect me from the accursed Satan.”"
"453","On the authority of Ahmad bin Abdah, on the authority of Abdul Aziz, meaning Al-Darawardi, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Saleh, on the authority of Muhammad bin Muslim bin Aydh, on the authority of Amer Bin Saad bin Abi Waqqas, on the authority of his father Saad: A man came to pray, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was leading us in prayer, so he said when he finished Al-Saff: Oh God, give me the best of what You give Your righteous servants. When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, finished the prayer, he said: “Who was the speaker above?” The man said: I am, O Messenger of God. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Then you hamstring your horse and be martyred in the path of God.”"
"454","We are Al-Hassan bin Issa, we are Abdullah bin Numayr. H Al-Hasan bin Al-Junaid narrated to us, Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, saying: Ubayd Allah bin Omar narrated to us, Saeed Al-Maqbari narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, That a man entered the mosque and prayed, then he came and greeted the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he mentioned the hadith, and said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “When you stand up to pray, perform ablution completely, then face the Qiblah and say takbir,” and he mentioned the hadith in its entirety. This is the wording. Hadith of Ibn Numayr"
"455","Yahya bin Habib bin Adi Al-Harithi and Ahmad bin Abdah Al-Dhabi narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah bin Waqqas Al-Laythi, said: I heard Omar bin Al-Khattab saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He says: “Actions are but by intention.” Yahya bin Habib added: “And a person is only what he intended.”"
"456","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, Ibn Jurayj told us, Ibn Shihab told me, on the authority of Salim bin Abdullah, that Ibn Umar, He said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up to pray, he would raise his hands until they were at the level of his shoulders, and then he would say “Allahu Akbar.” So if he wanted to “When he kneels, he does the same thing, and when he rises from kneeling, he does the same thing, but he does not do it when he raises his head from prostration.”"
"457","Saeed bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Makhzoumi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Wael bin Hajar, he said: “I prayed with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his companions, and I saw them raising their hands in their raincoats.”"
"458","Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Ashjaj told us, dictating and reciting countless times, he said: Yahya bin Al-Yaman told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, On the authority of Saeed bin Samaan, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to “spread his fingers wide apart” in prayer. Abu Bakr said: Before our trip to Iraq, Muhammad bin Rafi’ had told us this hadith about him. He said: Abdullah told us Ibn Sa`id al-Ashjaj Abu Sa`id al-Kindi, except that he said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would spread his fingers out for prayer. Published"
"459","Yahya bin Hakim narrated to us, Abu Amir narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed bin Samaan, he said: Abu Hurairah entered a mosque over us. Bani Waraq, he said: “There are three things that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to do with them. People left them. When he stood up to pray, he said: Thus, Abu Amir pointed with his hand and did not spread his fingers, nor did he join them together, and said: This is what Ibn Abi Dhib showed us. Abu Bakr said: Yahya bin Hakim pointed to us and raised his hands, spreading his fingers wide apart, and he did not press them together. His fingers, without spacing them apart, raised his hands above his head, extending out, and he would stand for a while before reading, asking God Almighty for His bounty. He used to say “Allahu Akbar” during prayer whenever he prostrated and rose. Abu Bakr said: This network is a very thick network. I do not know who it is from, and this word Rather, it is: he raised his hands outstretched, there is no doubt or doubt about the praying person raising his hands above his head at the beginning of the prayer."
"460","From Bundar, from Yahya, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib. H Al-Bistami narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudaik narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Samaan, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, so he mentioned Hadith, they said: “He raised his hands and extended them but did not clasp them.” The story of Ibn Abi Dhib does not include in their hadith that he showed them the characteristic of spreading or clasping the fingers together."
"461","Muhammad bin Bashar Bundar, Ahmad bin Abdah, Yahya bin Hakim, and Abd al-Rahman bin Bishr bin al-Hakam told us: Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Omar, Saeed bin Abi Al-Maqbari narrated to me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He entered the mosque, and a man entered and prayed. Then he greeted the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he responded to him. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He said: “Go back and pray, for you have not prayed, until he did that three times.” Then the man said: “By the One who sent you with the truth, I do not know anything other than this,” so he said: “ When you stand up to pray, say “Allahu Akbar,” then recite whatever is easy for you from the Qur’an, then bow until you feel comfortable bowing, then rise until you are straight. Standing, then prostrate until you are at ease while prostrating, then rise until you are at ease sitting, and do that in all your prayers.” Abu Bakr said: This is the hadith of Bundar."
"462","It is narrated by Muhammad bin Yahya, narrated by Hajjaj bin Minhal, and Abu Salih Kateb, all of them, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Abi Salamah, on the authority of his uncle Al-Majishun. Ibn Abi Salamah, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Ubayd Allah Ibn Abi Rafi’, on the authority of Ali Ibn Abi Talib, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: That when he began the prayer, he would say “Allahu Akbar,” then he would say: “I turn my face to the One who created the heavens and the earth, upright, and I am not of the polytheists. My sacrifice, my life, and my death belong to God, Lord of the worlds, He has no partner, and with that I was commanded, and I am the first of the Muslims. O God, You are the King, there is no god but You. You are my Lord, and I am your servant. I wronged myself and confessed my sin, so forgive me all my sins. No one forgives sins except You, and guide me. To the best of morals, no one guides to the best of them except You, and turn away from me the bad of them, no one can turn away the bad of them except You. At Your command and my happiness, and all goodness. In your hands, and evil is not yours, I am through you and to you, you are blessed and exalted, I ask your forgiveness and I repent to you.” Abu Saleh said: There is no god for me but you."
"463","On the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya, on the authority of Ahmad bin Khalid al-Wahbi, on the authority of Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Abdullah bin al-Fadl, on the authority of his uncle Al-Majishun, on the authority of Al-Araj, with a similar chain of transmission. Muhammad bin Yahya said: One of them adds a letter or a word to its companion. Abu Bakr said: His saying: “And evil is not for you”: that is, it is not something by which one may draw close to you."
"464","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman and Bahr bin Nasr bin Sabiq Al-Khawlani told us, they said: Ibn Wahb told us, Ibn Abi Al-Zannad told me, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Fadl, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Al-Araj, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Rafi’, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, may God have mercy on him God Almighty, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that when he stood up for the obligatory prayer he would say “Allahu Akbar” and he would say “Allahu Akbar” when he began the prayer after Takbeer: “I turn my face to Him who created the heavens and the earth,” so he mentioned the hadith in its length, and said: “And I am of the Muslims.” And they did not mention: And guide me to the best of morals, no one guides me to the best of them except You, and do not turn away from me the bad of them, no one can turn away the bad of them except You."
"465","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi, Yusuf bin Musa, Ali bin Khashram, and others told us. Ali said: He told us, and the others said: Jarir told us. Ibn Abd al-Hamid, on the authority of Amara Ibn al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He said the takbeer during the prayer and was silent for a while, so I said: O Messenger of God, by my mother and father, what do you say in your silence between the takbeer and the recitation? He said: “I say: O God, distance me from my sins as You have distanced between the East and the West. O God, purify me from my sins as a garment is purified.” White from filth, O God, wash me from my sins with ice, water, and hail.”"
"466","Abu Musa Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, Abd al-Samad told us, Hammam told us, Qatada told us, on the authority of Anas. H Muhammad bin Abi Safwan Al-Thaqafi told us, Bahz, meaning Ibn Asad, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Thabit and Qatada told us, on the authority of Anas: That a man came and was moved by the breath, and he said: God is the greatest. Praise be to God, much, good and blessed praise be to Him. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed away Peace and blessings of God be upon him, he said: “Which of you is the one who speaks words?” So he looked at the people and said: “Which one of you speaks words, for he did not say anything wrong?” Then the man said: O Messenger of God, I came and he motivated me. So I said to them, and he said: “I saw twelve angels hastening to see which of them would raise it.” This is the hadith of Bahz bin Asad, and Abu Musa said in his hadith: A man entered the prayer and said: Praise be to God, a great, good and blessed praise. He also said: A man from among the people said: I said it, and I meant nothing but good by it, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “He began to say it twice.” Ten angels, and they did not know how to write it until they asked their Lord, and He said: Write it as My servant said.” Abu Bakr said: News has been narrated about the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, initiating the night prayer with invocations of different wording. I mentioned it in the chapters on the night prayer, as for what the common people used to open their prayers in Khorasan by saying: Glory be to You, O God, and with Your praise, Blessed be your name and exalted be your grandfather, and there is no god but you. We do not know of any reliable news about this matter from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, according to people of knowledge. With hadith, and the best chain of transmission we know of, the news of Abu al-Mutawakkil was narrated on the authority of Abu Sa`id."
"467","Narrated by Muhammad bin Musa Al-Harashi, narrated by Jaafar bin Sulaiman Al-Dhabi, narrated by Ali bin Ali Al-Rifai, on the authority of Abu Al-Mutawakkil Al-Naji, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, got up during the night to pray, he would say “Allahu Akbar” three times, then he would say: “Glory be to You, O God.” And with Your praise, blessed be your name, exalted is your grandfather, and there is no god but you.” Then he says: “There is no god but Allah” three times, then he says: “Allah is the greatest” three times, Then he says: “I seek refuge in God, the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing from Satan, the accursed, from his incitements, his blowing, and his spitting,” and then he recites. Abu Bakr said: This news was not heard in supplication, neither in ancient times nor in his hadith. This news was used in its context, and it was not narrated. It has been reported to us on the authority of some of the scholars whom we did not see that he used to say “Allahu Akbar” to open the prayer three times, then he would say: Glory be to You, O God, and with Your praise until His saying: There is no god but You, then he says Allah three times, then he says “Allahu Akbar” three times."
"468","It was narrated, on the authority of Jubayr bin Mutim, that when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, began the prayer, he would say: “Allahu Akbar, Great” three times. “Praise be to God very much” three times, “Glory be to God tomorrow and the evening” three times, then he seeks refuge similar to the refuge in Abu Sa’id’s narration, except They differed regarding the chain of transmission of the news of Jubayr bin Mutim. It was narrated by Shu'bah, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Asim Al-Anzi, on the authority of Ibn Jubayr bin Mut'im, on the authority of his father. No, Bundar, no, Muhammad ibn Jaafar, no, Shu’bah. H, Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Wahb bin Jarir told us, Shu’bah told us"
"469","It was narrated by Husayn bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, and he said: On the authority of Abbad bin Asim, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr bin Mut’im, on the authority of His father. It was narrated to us by Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Ashjaj, Ibn Idris. H. Harun bin Ishaq and Ibn Fudayl told us all, on the authority of Husayn bin Abdul Rahman. Abu Bakr said: Asim Al-Anazi and Abbad bin Asim are unknown, he does not know who they are, and he does not know what is correct, what was narrated by Husayn or Shu’bah."
"470","Haritha bin Muhammad and Asim Al-Anazi narrated, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha: When the Messenger of God began the prayer, he would raise his hands following the example of He raised his shoulders and said “Allahu Akbar”, then he said: “Glory be to You, O God, and with Your praise, and Blessed be Your name and exalted be your glory, and there is no god but You.” Mu’mal bin Hisham and Salam bin Junada told us, they said: Abu Muawiyah told us, Mu’mal said, he said: Harithah bin Muhammad told us, and he said Salam bin Junada: On the authority of Haritha bin Muhammad, except that Salam did not say: So he said “Allahu Akbar.” Abu Bakr said: Harithah bin Muhammad, may God have mercy on him, is not among those whose hadith the scholars of hadith use as evidence."
"471","This is true on the authority of Omar ibn al-Khattab, that he used to begin the prayer like the hadith of Haritha, not on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I do not dislike it. He opened by saying: Glory be to You, O God, and with Your praise for what has been proven on the authority of Al-Farouq, may God Almighty be pleased with him, that he used to begin the prayer, except that Opening with what was proven on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the news of Ali bin Abi Talib, Abu Hurairah, and others, through narration of justice, on the authority of Justice delivered to him, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, is more beloved to me and more deserving of use, as following the Sunnah of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, is better. And better than others"
"472","On the authority of Yusuf bin Issa Al-Maruzi, on the authority of Ibn Fudayl, on the authority of Ata’, who is Ibn Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: “O God, I seek refuge in You from the accursed Satan and his whispering, inciting, and breathing,” he said: And death shook him, and poetry suffused him, and pride suffocated him."
"473","From Bundar, from Yahya, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib. H Al-Hussein bin Issa Al-Bistami told us, Muhammad bin Ismail bin Abi Fudaik narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Samaan, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “There are three things that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to do. People abandoned them. When he stood up to pray, he would raise his hands outstretched. He used to stand for a while before reading, asking God for His bounty, and he used to say “Allahu Akbar” whenever he lowered or raised it. Bundar said in his hadith: There were three that he used to do, but people abandoned them. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would rise to pray, he would raise his hands. He extended, and he would stand for a while before reading, saying: “I ask God of His bounty,” and he would say “Allahu Akbar” whenever he bowed and lay down."
"474","We are Al-Fadl bin Yaqoub Al-Jazari, we are Abdul-Ala, we are Muhammad, who is Ibn Ishaq, Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id narrated to me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of my father Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led us in the noon prayer. When he said the salutation, he called a man who was at the end of the rows and said: “O so-and-so, don’t you fear God? Don't you see how you pray? Indeed, when one of you stands up to pray, he only stands in conversation with his Lord, so let him see how he speaks to Him. You see that I do not see you. “By God, I see behind my back as I see in front of my hands.”"
"475","It is narrated by Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-San’ani, it is narrated by Yazid, meaning Ibn Zuray’, it is narrated by Sa’id, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “What is the matter with people who raise their eyes to the sky in their prayer?” Then his statement intensified about that, until he said: “Let them stop.” About that, or their eyes will be snatched away.”"
"476","On the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah, meaning Al-Ansari, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Orouba, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, He told them, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, in a similar manner, except that he said: Then the saying of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on that matter became stronger."
"477","On the authority of Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Ibn Idris, on the authority of Asim ibn Kulayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Wa’il ibn Hajar, he said: I came to Medina, So I said: “To look at the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I saw that when he opened the prayer he said ‘Allahu Akbar’, then he raised his hands, and I saw his thumbs.” close to his ears, then he took his left hand with his right, then he recited.” Then he mentioned the hadith."
"478","Harun bin Ishaq Al-Hamdani narrated to us, he said: Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Wael bin Hajar, he said: “I was As for the one who came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, I said: Let us look at the prayer of the Messenger of God and how he prays, and I saw him when he said the takbir, raising his hands until they were close to his ears. Then he struck his right hand against his left and caught it.” Then he mentioned the hadith"
"479","Narrated by Abu Musa, narrated by Ma’mal, narrated by Sufyan, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Wa’il bin Hajar, who said: “I prayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace Peace be upon him, and he placed his right hand over his left hand on his chest.”"
"480","We are Muhammad bin Yahya, we are Muawiyah bin Amr, we are Zaida, we are Asim bin Kulayb Al-Jarmi, my father told me that Wael bin Hajar, He told him, he said: I said: “I will look at the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, how he prays.” He said: So I looked at him, he got up, said “Allahu Akbar” and raised his hands until They were in line with his ears, then he placed his right hand on the back of his left palm, wrist, and forearm.”"
"481","Ahmad bin Abdul Rahman bin Wahb told me, my uncle told me, Yunus told me, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: I heard Abu Al-Ahwas, the client of the Banu Layth, Saeed bin Al-Musayyab narrated that Abu Dharr said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Like it."
"482","Muhammad bin Yahya narrated to me, Abu Salih narrated to me, Al-Layth narrated to me, Yunus narrated to me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: I heard Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to Ibn Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Dharr, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God continues to approach the servant as long as he does not turn away. His face turned away from him.”"
"483","We are Abu Muhammad Fahd bin Sulaiman Al-Masry, we are Abu Tawba, meaning Al-Rabi’ bin Nafi’, we are Muawiyah bin Salam, on the authority of Zayd bin Salam, that Abu Salam told him, he said: Al-Harith Al-Ash’ari told me, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, told him: “God Almighty commanded Yahya ibn Zechariah said with five words that he would do them, and he would command the Children of Israel to do them, and he would advise the people. Then he said: “Indeed, God has commanded you to pray. So when you set your faces up, do not turn away, for God sets up His face toward the face of His servant when he prays for him, and He does not turn his face away from him until The servant will go away.”"
"484","Our Muhammad bin Othman Al-Ajli, our Ubaid Allah bin Musa, on the authority of Shayban. H Muhammad bin Othman also told us, Ubaid Allah bin Musa, about Israel. H Muhammad bin Amr bin Tammam Al-Masry, narrated to us Yusuf bin Adiy, narrated to us Abu Al-Ahwas, all of us, on the authority of Ash’ath, who is the son of Abi Al-Sha’atha’. On the authority of his father, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about turning around during prayer, and he said: “It is “It is a misappropriation by Satan of a servant’s prayer.” In the story of Abu Al-Ahwas: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about a man turning around during prayer."
"485","From us, Abu Ammar Al-Hussein bin Harith, from us Al-Fadl bin Musa, on the authority of Abdullah bin Saeed, who is the son of Abi Hind, on the authority of Thawr bin Zaid, On the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to turn right and left in his prayer, and would not twist his neck behind him.” \His back.\"" Abu Bakr said: His saying “he turns around during his prayer” means he looks with his eyes to the right and to the left."""
"486","On the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman, on the authority of Shuaib, meaning Ibn Al-Layth, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, that he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, complained Peace be upon him, so we prayed behind him while he was sitting, and Abu Bakr was saying “Allahu Akbar” and the people would hear him saying “Allahu Akbar.” He said: Then he turned to us and saw us standing. He pointed to us and we sat down, and when he greeted him, he said: “If you were just trying to do what the Persians and the Romans did, rising up against their kings while they were sitting, then do not Do so, follow your imams. If the imam prays standing, then pray standing, and if he prays sitting, then pray sitting.” And in the news of Sahl bin Al-Hanaliyah about the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sending Anas bin Abi Marthad to guard them, he said: So the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, appointed And he saluted, turning to the people, until when he had finished his prayer, he saluted, and said to me: Rejoice, for your knight has come to you."
"487","Nahi Muhammad bin Yahya, Nahi Muammar bin Yamar, Nahi Muawiyah bin Salam, Zaid, who is Ibn Salam, told me that he heard Abu Salam, he said: Abu Kabsha Al-Saluli narrated to me, that Sahl bin Al-Hanaliyah narrated to him. Fahd bin Sulaiman told us, he said: I read to Abu Tawbah Al-Rabi’ bin Nafi’, Muawiyah bin Salam told us, in a long hadith."
"488","It was narrated by Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Ala, it was narrated by Sufyan, al-Zuhri narrated to me. H Al-Hasan bin Muhammad, Ahmad bin Abdah, Saeed bin Abdul Rahman Al-Makhzoumi, and Muhammad bin Al-Walid Al-Qurashi told us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Mahmoud bin Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Ubadah bin Al-Samit, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “There is no prayer for one who does not He recites with the opening of the book.” This is the hadith of Al-Makhzoumi, and Al-Hasan bin Muhammad said: The Prophet conveys it, and Ahmad and Abdul-Jabbar said: On the authority of Ubadah bin Al-Samit, a narration, Muhammad ibn al-Walid said: There is no prayer except by reciting the Fatihah of the Book."
"489","On the authority of Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi, on the authority of Ibn Ulayya, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, Al-Ala’ bin Abdul Rahman bin Yaqoub told me that Abu Al-Sa'ib told him that he heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever prays a prayer in which he does not recite the Mother of the Qur’an, So it is prematurity, it is prematurity, it is incomplete prematurity.” So I said: O Abu Hurairah, I am sometimes behind the imam. He said: Then he touched my arm. And he said: O Persian, recite it to yourself."
"490","On the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya, on the authority of Wahb bin Jarir, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Ala’ ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “A prayer is not sufficient in which the Fatihah of the Book is not recited.” I said: “So I was behind the imam, and he took my hand and said:” Recite it to yourself, O Persian.”"
"491","On the authority of Bishr bin Muadh Al-Aqdi, on the authority of Abu Awanah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, Abu Bakr, and Omar, And Uthman used to “begin the recitation with: Praise be to God, Lord of the Worlds, Surah Al-Fatihah, verse 2.”"
"492","On the authority of Bundar, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ja’far, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr, Omar and Othman used to begin the recitation with: Praise be to God, Lord of the Worlds, Surah Al-Fatihah, verse 2."
"493","Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-San’ani informed us, Khalid ibn Khadash informed us, Amr ibn Harun informed us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Umm Salamah: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “recited during prayer, in the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, Surat Al-Fatiha, verse 1, so he considered it a verse, and praise be to God, Lord of the Worlds, Surat Al-Fatiha.” Verse 2: Two verses, and You alone do we seek help. Surah Al-Fatihah, Verse 5. He added five fingers."
"494","It is Bundar, it is Muhammad bin Jaafar, it is Shu’bah. He said: I heard Qatada speaking, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “ I prayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and with Abu Bakr and Omar, but I did not hear any of them reciting Surah Al-Fatiha, in the name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful. 1\. Abu Bakr said: I have mentioned the methods and wording of this report in the Book of Prayer"
"495","Narrated by Salam bin Junada al-Qurashi, narrated by Waki’, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, who said: “I prayed behind the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And Abu Bakr, Omar, and Othman, but they did not say out loud, “In the Name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.” Surah Al-Fatihah, verse 1."
"496","Narrated by Abu Saeed Al-Ashjaj, narrated by Ibn Idris, who said: I heard Saeed bin Abi Orouba, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “In the Name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, he did not recite out loud, Surah Al-Fatihah, verse 1, nor did Abu Bakr, nor Omar, nor Othman.”"
"497","Narrated to us Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-San’ani, narrated to us Abu Al-Jawab, narrated to us Ammar bin Ruzaiq, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, He said: “I prayed with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and with Abu Bakr and Omar, but they did not pray out loud in the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, Surat Al-Fatihah, verse 1.”"
"498","Ahmad bin Abi Shurayh Al-Razi narrated to us, Suwayd bin Abdul Aziz narrated to us, Imran Al-Qasir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was “pleased with In the Name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful,” Surah Al-Fatihah, verse 1, in prayer, and Abu Bakr and Omar. Abu Bakr said: This report states the opposite of what those who have not studied knowledge have imagined, and he claimed that Anas bin Malik meant when he said: “It was The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, Abu Bakr, and Omar begin the recitation with “Praise be to God, Lord of the Worlds,” Surah Al-Fatiha, verse 2, and by saying: “I did not hear None of them recited Surah Al-Fatiha, verse 1, in the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, because they did not recite in the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, Surah Al-Fatiha, verse 1, aloud or “hiddenly,” and this report makes it clear that he meant that they should be pleased with it, and not speak out about it, according to Anas Abu al-Jawab, who is Al-Ahwas ibn Answer"
"499","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, my father told us, and Shuaib, meaning Ibn Al-Layth, told us: Al-Layth informed us, we are Khaled. H Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Sa`id bin Abi Maryam told us, Al-Layth told us, Khaled bin Yazid told me, on the authority of Ibn Abi Hilal, on the authority of Naeem Al-Mujmar, said: I prayed behind Abu Hurairah, and he recited: “In the Name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful,” Surat Al-Fatihah, verse 1, then he recited the Mother of the Qur’an, until he reached Those who go astray, Surah Al-Fatihah, verse 7. And he said: Amen, and the people said: Amen. And he says whenever he prostrates: God is great, and when he gets up from sitting, he says: God is great, and he says When he greeted him: “By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I resemble the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to you, all of it with the same wording, except that Ibn Abd Al-Hakam, he said: And when he got up from sitting on Mondays, he said: “Allahu Akbar.” Abu Bakr said: “I have investigated a remembrance of In the Name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful.” Surah Al-Fatihah, verse 1 in the book Meanings of the Qur’an, and I explained in that book that it is from the Qur’an with a clear explanation that is not problematic for those who understand the industry. Knowledge, and ponder what I have explained in that book, and may God grant him understanding and guide him to realize the truth and guidance through His grace and grace."
"500","Muhammad bin Muammar bin Rabi’i al-Qaisi, Abu Usama Hammad bin Usama, Abd al-Hamid bin Ja’far al-Ansari, told us about Al-Alaa bin Abdul-Rahman bin Yaqoub Al-Harqi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Shall I not teach you a surah that has not been revealed in the Torah, nor in the Gospel, nor in the Qur’an like it?” I said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: “Perhaps you “Do not leave that door until I tell you about it.” So I stood up with him and he started talking to me, with my hand in his hand. I slowed down, for fear of him leaving. Before he told me about it, when I approached the door, I said: O Messenger of God, the surah that you promised me. He said: “How do you begin when you stand up to pray?” He said: So I recited the opening of the Book, and he said: “It is, it is, and it is the seven repeated verses of which God said: And We have given you seven of the repeated verses and the Great Qur’an, Surah Al-Hijr. Verse 87: “It is what I have been given.”"
"501","It was narrated to me by Hawthara bin Muhammad Abu Al-Azhar, narrated to me by Abu Osama, narrated to me by Abd al-Hamid bin Jaafar, narrated to me by Al-Alaa bin Abd al-Rahman bin Yaqoub. On the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God has not sent down in the Torah, nor in The Gospel, and there is nothing in the Qur’an like the Mother of the Book, which is the seven repeated verses.”"
"502","Utbah bin Abdullah Al-Hammadi told us, he said: I read to Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Abdul Rahman, that he heard Abu Al-Sa’ib The servant of Hisham bin Zahra, saying: I heard Abu Hurairah saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever prays a prayer does not recite “By the mother of the Qur’an, she is a prematurity, so she is a prematurity, so she is an incomplete prematurity.” So I said: O Abu Hurairah, I am sometimes behind the imam, so he touched my arm and said: Recite it, O Persian, to yourself, for I will be. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “God, Blessed and Most High, said: I divided the prayer between Me and My servant into two halves, so half of it is for Me.” And half of it is for my servant. The servant says: Praise be to God, Lord of the Worlds. Surah Al-Fatihah, verse 2. God says: My servant has praised Me. The servant says: The Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. Surah Al-Fatihah, verse 2. 1, God says: My servant has praised me, the servant says: Master of the Day of Judgment Surah Al-Fatihah, verse 4, God says: My servant has glorified me, and this verse is between me and My servant, the servant says: It is You we worship and You we seek help. Surah Al-Fatihah, verse 5, this is between Me and My servant, and My servant has whatever he asks. The servant says: Guide us. The straight path, the path of those whom You have bestowed, not upon whom is Anger, nor of those who go astray. Surah Al-Fatihah, verse 6-7. So it is My servant’s, and for My servant is what he asks.”"
"503","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi and Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, saying: Yazid bin Harun told us, Hammam told us, and Aban bin Yazid, all together, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was “ He recites in the two rak'ahs of noon and afternoon the opening of the book and a surah, and sometimes he makes us hear the verse, and he recites in the other two rak'ahs With the opening of the book.” Abu Bakr said: I thought for a long time that this news was about reciting the Fatihah of the Book in the other two rak’ahs of the noon prayer. And no one narrated it during the era except Aban bin Yazid and Hammam bin Yahya, as I used to hear our companions of antiquities say, so if Al-Awza’i and His Majesty mentioned this increase in his report."
"504","He said: Likewise, Muhammad bin Maymun Al-Makki narrated to us, Yahya bin Abi Kathir narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, on the authority of his father, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to lead us in the noon and afternoon prayers, and in the first two he would recite the Fatihah of the Book and a surah with it, and in The other two verses are with the opening of the book, and he used to lengthen the first one, and sometimes he would make us hear the verse.”"
"505","Muhammad bin Al-Ala bin Kurayb narrated to us, Abu Usama narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, Amara bin Umair narrated to us. H. Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala’ narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Al-A’mash narrated to us. H Ahmed bin Abdah and Saeed bin Abdul Rahman Al Makhzoumi told us, saying: Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash. H. Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Amara bin Umair, on the authority of Abu Muammar, he said: We asked Khabbab said, “Did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recite during the noon and afternoon prayers?” He said: “Yes.” We said: What did you learn about? He said: “With confusion.” “His beard.” Al-Dawraqi, Al-Makhzoumi, and Abu Kurayb said: “Because of the disorder in his beard.”"
"506","Ya'qub al-Dawrqi and Salam ibn Junada told us, they said: Waki` told us, al-Dawrqi said, he said: al-A'mash told us, and Salam said: on the authority of al-Amash, With this chain of transmission, the same, and he said: “With the disorder of his beard.” We are Bishr bin Khaled Al-Askari, we are Muhammad, meaning Ibn Jafar, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Suleiman, he said: I heard Amara bin Umair about this. The chain of transmission is the same, and he said: his beard."
"507","Ali bin Sahl Al-Ramli told me, Al-Walid, meaning Ibn Muslim, told me Abu Amr, and he is Al-Awza’i, Yahya bin Abi Kathir told me. H, Bahr bin Nasr Al-Khawlani told us, Bishr bin Bakr told us, Al-Awza’i told me, Yahya bin Abi Kathir told me, Abdullah told me Ibn Abi Qatada, my father told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite the Umm al-Qur’an, and two surahs with it in the two rak’ahs. The first two rak’ahs of the noon prayer and the afternoon prayer. He would sometimes recite the verse, and he would prolong the first rak’ah of the noon prayer.” Ali bin Sahl said, on the authority of his father, and he also said: “The first rak’ah of the noon prayer should be made long.”"
"508","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawrqi told us, Hushaym told us, Abd al-Malik bin Umair told us. H Saeed bin Abdul Rahman Al Makhzoumi told us, Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abdul Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra: The people of Kufa complained about Sa`d to Omar, and mentioned about his prayer, so Omar sent for him, and he came to him, and mentioned to him what they found fault with regarding the matter of prayer. He said to him: “I pray with them the prayer of the Messenger of God, so I do not neglect it. Rather, I stay with them in the first two prayers, and omit them in the last two.” So he said to him. Omar: That suspicion of you, Abu Ishaq. This is the hadith of Al-Dawraqi, and Al-Makhzoumi said: I reduce the other two."
"509","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawrqi, Abu Hashim Ziyad bin Ayyub, and Ahmad bin Mani’ told us, they said: Hushaym told us, he told us Mansour, who is Ibn Zazan, on the authority of Al-Walid Ibn Muslim, who is Abu Bishr, on the authority of Abu Al-Siddiq, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, who said: “We were Download prostration. He said: We estimated his standing in the last two days of the afternoon to be half of that. He said: We estimated his standing in the first two days of the afternoon to be half of that. . This is the wording of the hadith of Ziyad bin Ayyub"
"510","Yahya bin Hakim and Ya’qub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawrqi told us, they said: Abu Dawud, Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Samak bin Harb, he said: I heard Jabir bin Samurah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite at noon and afternoon prayers at night when it was overcast and the sun was \""
511"""
"511","Muhammad ibn Harb al-Wasiti narrated to us: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us: from Husayn ibn Waqid, the judge of Marw, who said: Abdullah ibn Buraydah al-Aslami informed me, from his father, that the Prophet ﷺ used to recite in the Zuhr prayer: ""When the heaven is split asunder"" (Surah al-Inshiqaq) and similar surahs."
"512","Muhammad bin Muammar bin Rabi’ al-Qaysi narrated to us, Ruh bin Ubadah narrated to us, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, Qatada, Thabit, and Hamid narrated to us, On the authority of Anas ibn Malik, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that they used to “hear from him the tone at noon, ‘Glorify the name of your Most High Lord,’” “Has the hadith of the cheater reached you?”"
"513","Muhammad bin Ziyad bin Ubaid Allah told us, Abdul-Warith informed us. H Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, narrated to us Abu Muammar, narrated to us Abd al-Warith, narrated to us Hanzalah al-Sadusi, he said: I said to Ikrimah: Perhaps I recited in prayer Morocco B Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of creation, and say, I seek refuge in the Lord of people, and some people blame me for that. He said: Glory be to God, and what’s wrong with that? Recite them, for they are from the Qur’an. Then he said: Ibn Abbas told me that the Messenger of God “came and prayed two rak’ahs in which he only recited With the Mother of the Book.” This is the hadith of Muhammad bin Yahya, and Muhammad bin Ziyad said: And some people criticize, but he did not say: What is the harm in that? He said: Ibn Abbas told me that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, stood up and prayed two rak’ahs in which only the Fatihah of the Book was recited, nothing more than \That's something\"""""
"514","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala told us, Sufyan told us, he said: I heard Al-Zuhri, saying: Muhammad bin Jubayr bin Mut’im told me, on the authority of his father, He heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “reciting Al-Tur in Morocco.” Ali bin Khashram and Saeed bin Abdul Rahman Al Makhzoumi told us, saying: Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Muhammad bin Jubayr bin Mut'im, on the authority of his father. H, Bundar narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, Al-Zuhri narrated to me, on the authority of Ibn Jubayr bin Mut’im, on the authority of his father, like him."
"515","On the authority of Bundar, on the authority of Abu Asim, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, on the authority of Marwan ibn al-Hakam, on the authority of Zaid Ibn Thabit said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to recite in the Maghrib prayer two long verses.”"
"516","Narrated by Muhammad bin Muammar Al-Qaisi, narrated by Ruh bin Ubadah, on the authority of Ibn Juraij. H Al-Hussein bin Mahdi told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, Ibn Jurayj told us, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Abi Mulaika, saying: Urwa bin Al-Zubayr told me, Marwan bin Al-Hakam told me, he said: Zayd bin Thabit said: Why do you read so short in Morocco? Al-Mufassal?” The Messenger of God used to recite in Morocco at two lengths of length. He said: I said: What is the length of two lengths? He said: “Al-A’raf”, so I asked Ibn Abi Mulaika: What are the two lengths? He said, according to his opinion: “Al-An’am and Al-A’raf.” This is the wording of the hadith of Abdul Razzaq. And in the news of a soul, he said: Ibn Abi Mulaika told me, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, Marwan bin Al-Hakam said: Zaid bin Thabit told me. He said: I heard Ahmad bin Nasr, the reciter, saying: “I would like to recite Al-A’raf once in Morocco.”"
"517","Narrated by Muhammad bin Yahya, narrated by a lecturer, narrated by Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to “recite in Maghrib reciting Surah Al-A’raf in both rak’ahs.” Abu Bakr said: I do not know of anyone who followed Muhadhir ibn al-Muwari’ with this chain of narration. Hisham’s companions said in this chain of narration, on the authority of Zayd ibn Thabit, Or on the authority of Abu Ayyub, Hisham doubted"
"518","It is narrated by Muhammad bin Al-Alaa bin Kurayb, on the authority of Abu Usama, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, that Abu Ayyub, or Zayd bin Thabit, reported that Hisham doubted, He said to Marwan, who was the governor of the city: “You are afraid to recite the two rak’ahs of sunset, for by God the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was And he recited the salaam therein, reciting Surah Al-A’raf in both rak’ahs.” So I said to my father: What was Marwan reciting about? He said: From the length of the joint. Thus it was narrated by Waki’ and Shuaib bin Ishaq, on the authority of Hisham, and they said: On the authority of Zaid, or on the authority of Abu Ayyub."
"519","On the authority of Salam ibn Junada, on the authority of Waki’, on the authority of Abu Kurayb, on the authority of Shuaib ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Abdul-Jabbar ibn Al-Ala’, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah told me. H. Saeed bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Makhzoumi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri. H. Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Zuhri told us, Sufyan told us, Al-Zuhri told us. H Ali bin Khashram told us, Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah. H. Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of his mother Umm al-Fadl bint al-Harith said that she heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “reciting the mursalat in Morocco.” This is the wording of the hadith of Al-Dawraqi, except that Abdul-Jabbar did not say: In Morocco."
"520","Bundar told us, Abu Bakr told us, meaning the Hanafi, I am Al-Dahhak, who is Ibn Uthman, Bukair bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj told me, Suleiman bin Yassar told us that he heard Abu Hurairah say: I have not seen anyone whose prayer was more similar to that of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, than so-and-so. To a prince who was in the city, Solomon said: “So I prayed behind him, and he used to make the first two prayers long, and the last two short, and he made the afternoon short, and he It is recited in the first two days of Maghrib with the short part of the Quran, in the first two days of the Isha prayer in the middle of the Quran, and in the first two days of the Isha’ prayer in the middle of the Quran, and in the first two days of the Isha’ prayer with the length of the Quran. Abu Bakr said: This difference in recitation in terms of what is permissible, it is permissible for the praying person to recite in Maghrib and in all the prayers that He will add to the opening of the book what he likes, and some surahs of the Qur’an. It is not forbidden for him to recite whatever surahs of the Qur’an he wants, except that If he is an imam, the choice is for him to recite slowly, and not to prolong the recitation with the people, lest he tempt them, as the Chosen One, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said. He greeted Muadh ibn Jabal: Do you want to be a perpetrator, and just as the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered the imams to shorten the prayer, and he said: “Who among you has prayed?” people, let him be light.” And I will present these reports, or some of them, in the Book of Imamate, for that book is the subject of these reports."
"521","Ahmad bin Abdah al-Dhabi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, and Abu al-Zubayr, we heard Jabir bin Abdullah, one of them adding to His companion said: Muadh used to pray with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, then he would return to his people and lead them in prayer, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, delayed He led the prayer one night, and Muadh returned to lead them, so he recited Surat Al-Baqarah. When a man from the people saw that, he turned to the side of The mosque, so he prayed alone, and they said: Have you hypocritically? He said: No. He said: And I will come to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I will inform him. And he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Muadh will pray with you. Then he returns and leads us in prayer, and you delayed the prayer yesterday, so he came and led us in prayer, and he recited Surat Al-Baqarah, and I delayed it, so I prayed alone, oh Messenger of God, and indeed we are companions of clarity, and we work with our own hands. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Muadh, are you more tempted? Read.” Surah: And the night when it covers, and glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and the sky full of constellations. Abu Bakr said: I have mentioned the methods of this report in the book of the Imamate."
"522","Ali bin Khashram told us, Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, and Muammar, we heard Adi bin Thabit, saying: I heard Al-Baraa bin Single, he says: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, reciting “with figs and olives at the evening meal of the afterlife, and I have never heard a better recitation than him.”"
"523","On the authority of Issa bin Ibrahim Al-Ghafiqi, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Malik, and Ibn Lahi’ah, on the authority of Ibn Al-Aswad, on the authority of Urwa ibn Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Zainab bint Umm Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, she said: I complained or complained, so I mentioned it to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him, and he said: “Round around, passing people while you were riding.” She said: So I rode on a camel, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was praying on the side of the House. So I heard him reciting in the last evening prayer while he was praying with the people and the mountain, and a written book.” Ibn Lahi’ah said, and Abu Al-Aswad said: He is reciting. He recites when he recites, except that Malik said: He prays at the side of the House."
"524","We are Bundar Muhammad bin Bashar, we are Muhammad, meaning Ibn Jafar, and Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Mahdi. They said: Shu`bah narrated to us, on the authority of Adi, and he is Ibn Thabit said: I heard Al-Baraa bin Aazib saying: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was on a journey, so he prayed the afterlife, so he recited in... One of the two rak’ahs with figs and olives.”"
"525","I am Abu Talib Zayd bin Akhzam Al-Tai, narrated by Muhammad bin Bakr, narrated by Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Al-Bara’, saying: “The Prophet prayed May God’s prayers and peace be upon him while on a journey, and he performed the final evening prayer, reciting figs and olives therein.”"
"526","Narrated by Abu Musa Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna, narrated by Zaida, on the authority of Simmak, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite in Fajr prayer with Qaf, and his prayer after that was shortened.”"
"527","Ahmad bin Abdah, Sufyan bin Uyaynah. H Ali bin Khashram told us, Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Ulaqah, on the authority of his uncle Qutbah bin Malik, I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace “He recites Surah Q in the morning, and I heard him reciting: And the palm trees are in fields, Surah Q, verse 10.”"
"528","Al-Saghani told me, Al-Mu`tamir told me, on the authority of his father, Abu Al-Minhal told me, on the authority of Abu Barza, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was It is recited in the morning prayer in the form of one hundred to sixty, or sixty to one hundred.” Abu Bakr said: Abu Al-Minhal is Sayyar bin Salamah Basri."
"529","Ahmed bin Abdah told us, Ziyad bin Abdullah told us, on the authority of Suleiman Al-Taymi. H, Bundar told us, Yazid told us, Suleiman Al-Taymi told us. H Ahmad bin Abdah told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Suleiman Al-Taymi. H Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Sulayman al-Taymi, with this chain of narration: the same, and they said, “Sixty to a hundred.”"
"530","Abu Ammar and Salam bin Junada told us, they said: Waki` told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu al-Minhal, on the authority of Abu Barza, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to recite in the morning anything between sixty and one hundred.”"
"531","On the authority of Yaqoub bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Khalaf bin al-Walid, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Simmak, on the authority of Jabir, who is Ibn Samurah, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was And peace be upon him, “He would pray like yours, but he would shorten the prayer. He would recite in the Fajr prayer Al-Waqi’ah and similar surahs.” Abu Bakr said: This news was narrated by someone whose art is not the hadith, so he came with a tamper. He narrated it on the authority of Sulaiman al-Taymi, and he said: On the authority of Anas bin Malik, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace"
"532","It was narrated by Ahmad bin Mani’, narrated by Yaqoub bin Ibrahim, narrated by Suleiman Al-Taymi, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with this. This is a gross error, and the news is only on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Abu Al-Minhal Sayyar Ibn Salamah, on the authority of Abu Barza. This is what was narrated by these memorizers whose craft is the hadith."
"533","Ali ibn Hajr al-Saadi told us, on the authority of a partner, on the authority of Makhoul ibn Rashid, on the authority of Muslim al-Bateen, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “would recite at dawn on Friday the Revelation, and has it come upon man?” Na Bandar, Na Muhammad, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Muslim Al-Bateen. H Al-Saghani told us, Khaled, meaning Ibn Al-Harith, I am Shu’bah, Makhoul told me, he said: I heard Muslim Al-Bateen, speaking, on the authority of Sa’id Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite on Friday in the morning prayer the revelation of the verse, and did he come “On mankind, and in the Friday prayer, Surat al-Jumu’ah, and the hypocrites.” Al-Fadl ibn Ya’qub al-Rakhami narrated to us a strange story. He said: Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite in the morning prayer On Friday, was the revelation not revealed, and did it come to mankind?"
"534","Abu Ammar and Ali bin Sahl al-Ramli told us, they said: Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir told me, he told me Al-Qasim Abu Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, said: I led the Messenger of God in one of those niqabs, and he said: “Will you not ride, O Uqaib?” So I was afraid to ride the boat of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then he said: “Won’t you ride, O Aqib?” I feared that it would be a sin. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, dismounted, and I rode for a while, then got off, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rode, and then he said: “O Aqib, Shall I not teach you two of the best surahs that people recite?” I said, “Yes, O Messenger of God,” so he recited to me, “Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of creation,” and “Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind.” Then the prayer was established, and he prayed and recited them, then he passed on. By me, he said: “How did you see, O Aqib? “Recite them every time you sleep and wake up.” Abu Al-Khattab narrated to us, Al-Walid narrated to us, with this and a similar chain of narration, and he said: On the authority of Al-Qasim. Abu Bakr said: This word: “Whenever you sleep and when you wake up,” is of the kind in which I learned that the Arabs assign the name of the sleeper to the one who is lying down, and they assign it to the transient sleeper. The mind, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, only meant when he said in this report: “Recite by them when you sleep,” that is, when you lie down, since the sleeper It is impossible for a person whose mind is fleeting to be addressed, and it is said to him: If he sleeps and his mind is gone, then recite the two Mu’awwidhatin. This is also what Ibn Buraidah reported, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn: “The prayer of a sleeper is equal to half the prayer of one sitting,” but by the sleeper in this position he meant the one who is lying down, not the sleeper whose mind is gone, since A sleeper whose mind has lost his mind is not called upon to pray. He cannot pray because his mind has lost his mind."
"535","Abdullah bin Hashem told us, Abdul Rahman told us, meaning Ibn Mahdi. H and us Abdah bin Abdullah Al-Khuza’i, Zaid, meaning Ibn al-Hubab, informed us, both of them on the authority of Muawiyah, and he was Ibn Salih. Abdah said, He said: Al-Alaa bin Al-Harith Al-Hadrami narrated to me, and Ibn Hashim said: On the authority of Al-Alaa bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Al-Qasim, the client of Muawiyah, on the authority of Uqba bin Amer, he said: I was leading the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey, and he said: “O Uqba, shall I not teach you the best of the two surahs ever recited?” I said: Yes, he said: “Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of creation, and say, I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind.” When he descended and led the morning prayer with them, he said: “How did you see, O Uqba?” This is the wording of the hadith of Abd al-Rahman, and Abdah did not say: On a journey, but he said: He did not see me impressed by them, so he led the people in the morning prayer, so he recited With them, then he said to me: “O Uqba, how did you see?”"
"536","Musa bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Masruqi and Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Fadl bin Al-Muwaffaq told us, they said: Abu Usama and Zayd bin Abi Al-Zarqa told us, Both on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Saleh, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Jubayr bin Nufayr al-Hadrami, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to “recite in the morning prayer: ‘Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of Al-Falaq,’ and ‘Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind.’” This is the wording of the hadith of Yazid bin Abi al-Zarqa, and in the hadith of Abu Usama, he said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about the two exorcists. Are they from the Qur’an? So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, believed in them during the dawn prayer. Abu Bakr said: Our companions say: Al-Thawri made a mistake in this hadith, and I say that it is not objectionable for Sufyan to narrate this on the authority of Muawiyah, and on the authority of others"
"537","Muhammad bin Yahya told us strange news. Ibrahim bin Hamza told us, Abdul Aziz, meaning Ibn Muhammad, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Thabit Al-Bunani, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, said: A man from the Ansar used to lead them in the Quba Mosque. He said: Whenever he opened a surah, he would recite With it in prayer, from what was recited with it, he opened with “Say, He is God, One” until he finished it, then he would recite another surah with it, and he used to do that. In every rak’ah, when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to them, they told him the news, and he said: “O so-and-so, what motivates you to recite this Surah regularly in every rak’ah? A rak’ah?” He said: “I love it.” Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Loving it will admit you to Paradise.”"
"538","Narrated by Muhammad bin Al-Ala bin Kurayb Al-Hamdani, by Abu Khaled, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, who said: Nahik bin Sinan came to Abdullah, He said: “How do you find this letter in water that is not stagnant or fragrant?” He said: “Has the entire Qur’an been counted except this?” He said: “I will recite Al-Mufassal in One rak’ah, and Abdullah said: This is like this poetry. There are people who recite the Qur’an with their tongues, it does not go beyond their throats, but when it enters A heart, in which benefit is established, and the last part of prayer is bowing and prostration, and I know the counterparts in which the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite He recited two surahs with them in one rak’ah, then he took Alqamah by the hand and entered and left and counted them over us.” Al-Amash said: It is twenty surahs written by Abdullah, the beginning of which is the Most Gracious and the last of them is Ad-Dakhan, the Most Compassionate, the Star, and the Offspring. And Al-Tur, these is the counterparts, and it came close, and Al-Haqqa, and Al-Waqi’ah, and N, and Al-Nazi’at, and a questioner asked, and Al-Muddathathir, and Al-Muzzammil, and Woe For the ones who turn away, and I frown and I do not swear, and did he come, and the messengers, and what do they wonder, and when the sun turned round, and the smoke. We are Abu Musa, we are Al-Amash. H Yusuf ibn Musa and Salam ibn Junada narrated to us, saying: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Al-A’mash narrated to us: They mentioned the hadith in its length, until his saying: So he entered Alqamah asked him, then he came out to us and said: Twenty surahs from the beginning of Al-Mufassal written by Abdullah. They did not add more than this."
"539","We are Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawrqi, we are Othman bin Omar, we are Khams. H. Salam bin Junada told us, I am Waki’, on the authority of Kahmas bin Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq Al-Uqaili, who said: I said to Aisha: Did Did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, combine the surahs in a rak’ah? She said: “Al-Mufassal.” This is a comprehensive hadith. Al-Dawrqi said in his hadith: I said to Aisha: Did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pray the noon prayer? She said: “When he came from his sunset?” I said: Was he reciting the surahs? She said: “Al-Mufassal.” I said: Did he pray sitting? She said: “After people destroyed it.”"
"540","It is narrated by Muhammad bin Al-Alaa bin Kurayb Al-Hamdani, on the authority of Abu Usama, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, that Abu Ayyub, or Zayd bin Thabit, So he mentioned the hadith"
"541","This is Ahmad bin Abd al-Rahman bin Wahb, I am my uncle, Amr bin al-Harith informed me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abd al-Rahman, that he heard Urwa Ibn Al-Zubayr, he says: Zayd Ibn Thabit said to Marwan Ibn Al-Hakam: O Abu Abdul-Malik, do you recite in the Maghrib the verse “Qul huwa Allahu Ahad,” and We have given you Al-Kawthar? He said: Yes, Zaid bin Thabit said: So mahlufah, I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “reciting and starting with the longest of the two long vowels, the sucking.” . Abu Bakr said: I dictated the information of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Zayd ibn Thabit, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite Maghrib With Surah Al-A’raf in both rak’ahs,” according to the news of Muhammad bin Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit, in his saying: It is read In both of them, he means performing both rak'ahs together"
"542","Narrated by Salam bin Junada, narrated by Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-A’mash. H, Mu'mal bin Hisham told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Al-Mustadawrid bin Al-Ahnaf, on the authority of a connection, On the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: I prayed with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, one night, so he began the recitation and recited until he reached one hundred, so I said: He bowed, then he continued until he reached two hundred, so I said: He bows, then he recited until he concluded it, so I said: He bowed, then he opened the women’s prayers, so he recited, then he bowed. So his bowing was like his standing, and he said in his bowing: “Glory be to my Lord the Great,” then he prostrated, and his prostration was like his bowing, so he said in his prostration: Glory be to my Lord, the Most High.” And whenever he came across a sign of mercy, he would ask, and when he came across a sign of punishment, he would seek refuge, and whenever he came across a sign of mercy, he would seek refuge in God. “Glory be to Him.” This is an implied word"
"543","We have Bundar, we have Yahya, we have Abdul-Rahman bin Mahdi, and Ibn Abi Adi, on the authority of Shu’bah. H. Abu Musa told us, Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us. Bishr bin Khalid Al-Askari told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Jaafar, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Al-Mustarid bin Al-Ahnaf, on the authority of Silah bin Zafar, on the authority of Hudhayfah, said: “I prayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, one night. “When he passed by a sign of mercy, he stopped at it and asked, and he did not pass by a sign of punishment except that he stopped at it and sought refuge.” This is the wording of the hadith of Abu Musa"
"544","This is Harun bin Ishaq Al-Hamdani, this is Muhammad, meaning Ibn Abdul Wahhab Al-Sukkari. H Saeed bin Abdul Rahman Al Makhzoumi, narrated to us Sufyan, all of us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ibrahim Al Saskiki, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi More fully, he said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: O Messenger of God, teach me something sufficient for me from the Qur’an, for I do not read. He said: “Say: Glory be to God, and praise be to God, and there is no god but God, and God is great, and there is no god but God, and there is no power but from God,” he said: The man held it with his hand and said: This is for my Lord, so what is mine? He said: “Say: O God, forgive me, have mercy on me, guide me, provide for me, and protect me.” He said: He embraced her with his other hand and stood up. This is the hadith of Al-Makhzoumi, and Harun said in his hadith: So he said: Teach me something that will suffice me from the Qur’an, and he did not say: Then the man cupped it with his hand. And he said at the end of the hadith, Mas’ar said: I was with Abraham while he was narrating, and I confirmed it from him."
"545","We are Ali bin Hajr Al-Saadi, we are Ismail, meaning Ibn Jafar, we are Yahya bin Ali bin Yahya bin Khallad bin Rafi’ al-Zarqi, on the authority of his father On the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Rifa’ah bin Rafi’, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was sitting in the mosque one day, Rifa’ah said: While we were with him, a man like a Bedouin came, and he prayed and shortened his prayer, then he left and greeted the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “And upon you, go back and pray, for you have not prayed.” So he went back and prayed, then he came and greeted the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he responded to him. And he said: “Go back and pray, for you have not prayed.” He did that two or three times, all of this until the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, greeted him. And he said: “And you must go back and pray, for you have not prayed.” The people were afraid and it was hard for them that someone whose prayers were lightest would not have prayed, so the man said at the end That is: Show me or teach me, for I am only human and I make mistakes. So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Yes, if you stand up to pray, So perform ablution as God commanded you, then recite the tashahhud and stand up, then say “Allahu Akbar.” If you have a Qur’an with you, recite it. Otherwise, thank God and say “Allahu Akbar.” And praise God, then bow down and be at ease in your bowing, then stand up straight, then prostrate and stand upright in prostration, then sit down and be at ease sitting, then stand up. If you do that, your prayer has been completed, and if you detract from it, it detracts from your prayer.” He said: This was easier for them than the first, because whoever detracts from that will detract from his prayer and will not perform all of it."
"546","We are Abd al-Rahman bin Bishr bin al-Hakam, we are Hajjaj, meaning Ibn Muhammad, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, he said: I heard Muhammad bin Abbad bin Jafar, saying: Abu Salamah bin Sufyan and Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Sa’ib, he said: “The Messenger of God prayed May God’s prayers and peace be upon him in Mecca in the morning, and Surat Al-Mu’minun was opened, until when the mention of Moses and Aaron came, or the mention of Jesus Muhammad ibn Servants who doubted or disagreed about it, a cough struck the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said, “So he bowed.” He said: Ibn al-Sa'ib was present at that. We are Abd al-Rahman, we are Abd al-Razzaq. Ibn Jurayj told us something similar, all in one word, except that he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed for us. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Then he omitted it and bowed, and did not mention what came after it. Abu Bakr said: He is not Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas Al-Sahmi."
"547","Narrated by Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala Al-Attar Abu Bakr, narrated by Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I heard Ata’, saying: I heard Abu Hurairah, He says: “In every prayer it is recited. Whatever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made us hear, we have made you hear, and whatever was hidden from us we have hidden from you.” Abu Bakr said: I have explained in the Book of Imamate all the prayers that the worshiper should announce by reading it, and what he should fear. With it, as the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to announce and fear."
"548","We are Ali bin Hajar Al-Saadi, we are Ismail, meaning Ibn Jafar, we are Sufyan bin Uyaynah. H, Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Sulayman bin Suhaim, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Ma’bad, and he is Ibn Abbas, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, revealed the curtain and the people were in rows behind Abu Bakr, and he said: O people, nothing remains of the glad tidings of prophecy except a good dream, which a Muslim sees, or it is seen for him. However, I am forbidden from reciting while bowing. Or prostrating, as for bowing, glorify the Lord therein, and as for prostration, strive diligently in supplication, for it is certain that it will be answered.” This is the hadith of Abdul-Jabbar"
"549","This is Yusuf bin Musa, I am Jarir. H and us Salam bin Junada, Abu Muawiyah told us all, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And he said: “When the son of Adam recites the prostration and prostrates, Satan withdraws, weeping, and says: Oh, woe to him! The son of Adam was commanded to prostrate, so he prostrated, so he has Paradise, and I was commanded to prostrate, but I refused, so Hell is mine.” In the hadith of Jarir, he said: So I disobeyed him"
"550","Narrated by Ahmad bin Abdah, on the authority of Hammad bin Zaid. Bishr bin Muadh Al-Aqdi told us, Hammad bin Zaid told us. H. Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala told us, Sufyan told us. H Muhammad bin Bashar and Yahya bin Hakim told us, saying: Abd al-Wahhab told us all, on the authority of Ayyub, and Abd al-Wahhab said, Ayoub, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he said: “PBUH is not one of the commandments of prostration, and I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prostrating “In it.” This is the wording of the hadith of Abdul Wahhab"
"551","We are Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Ashjaj, I am Hafs bin Ghayath, and Abu Khaled, meaning Suleiman bin Hayyan Al-Ahmar, on the authority of Al-Awwam bin Hawshab, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he was “prostrating in the prayer, and he was told, and he said: Those are the ones whom God has guided, so he guided them.” Surah Al-An’am, verse 90, and he said: David prostrated to it, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prostrated to it.”"
"552","Muhammad bin Al-Ala bin Kurayb and Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Ashjaj told us, they said: Abu Khalid told us, on the authority of the common people, on the authority of Al-Mujahid, he said: I said: To Ibn Abbas: Where did you get that prostration from? He said: “So he recited to me: And from his descendants are David, Solomon, and Job, until he reached his saying: Those are the ones whom God has guided, so by their guidance he led him, Surah Al-An’am, verse 84-90, he said: David prostrated in it, and for that reason the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prostrated. We are Al-Ashjaj, we are Ibn Abi Ghaniya, we are Al-Awwam bin Hawshab, with this"
"553","We are Bundar, we are Muhammad bin Jafar, I am Shu`bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Al-Aswad speaking, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. “He read the star and prostrated therein, and those who were with him prostrated, except that an old man took a handful of pebbles or dirt and raised it to the He touched his forehead and said: “This is enough for me.” Abdullah said: After that, I saw him killed as an infidel."
"554","It is from Abu Musa, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, from Sufyan, on the authority of Ayoub ibn Musa, from Ata’ ibn Mina, from Abu Hurairah. H. Salam bin Junada narrated to us, Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ayyub bin Musa, on the authority of Ibn Mina, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “ We prostrated with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the name of your Lord who created, and behold, the sky split open.”"
"555","We are Abd al-Rahman bin Bishr bin al-Hakam, we are Abd al-Razzaq, Ibn Jurayj told us, Ayoub bin Musa told me that Ata bin Mina He told him that he heard Abu Hurairah say: “I prostrated with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when the sky split open, and in it, recite in the name of your Lord who \He created.\"" Ayoub claimed that Ata bin Mina was one of the good people."""
"556","Muhammad bin Yahya brought strange news to us, Muhammad bin Uthman al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Thabit, on the authority of Nafi’, On the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “recited a prostration in the year of the conquest, and all the people prostrated, including the rider and the one prostrating on the ground. The rider even prostrates on his hand.”"
"557","We are Bundar, we are Yahya bin Saeed, we are Ubaid Allah, Nafi’ informed me, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: He was the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Qur’an will be recited to us, then he will recite the surah in which there is prostration, and he will prostrate, and we will prostrate with him, until none of us finds room for his forehead.”"
"558","Narrated by Muhammad bin Hisham, narrated by Ibn Idris, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: “We used to recite the prostration at The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, then he prostrates, and we prostrate with him until we crowd one another.”"
"559","Narrated by Al-Rabi’ bin Suleiman Al-Muradi, on the authority of Shuaib, meaning Ibn Al-Layth, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Bakr bin Abdullah, on the authority of Nu’aym bin Abdullah Al-Mujmar That he said: I prayed with Abu Hurairah above this mosque, so he recited: When the sky split open, he prostrated in it, and said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, prostrated therein.” I have mentioned the narrations of this report in the Book of Prayer, the Book of the Great, who said on the authority of Abu Hurairah: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, or I prostrated with him. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when the sky split open. Abu Bakr said: Abu Hurairah only came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he converted to Islam years after the Hijra. He said in the news of Arak bin Malik, on the authority of Abu Hurairah: I came to Medina and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was at Khaybar. He had appointed Siba’ ibn `Arfatah as successor to Medina, and Qays said Ibn Abi Hazim: I heard Abu Hurairah say: I accompanied the Prophet for three years, and he knew that he saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prostrate when The sky has split open, and recite in the name of your Lord who created, and I have taught in more than one place in our books that the informer and the witness who must be accepted His testimony and experience is the one who informs of the existence of a thing, and bears witness to seeing and hearing the thing, not the one who denies the existence of a thing and denies it, and who He said: So-and-so did not do such-and-such. He is neither an informant nor a witness. Rather, the witness is someone who bears witness, and says: I saw so-and-so doing such-and-such, and I heard him say Such and such, and this is not hidden from those who understand science and jurisprudence, and I have explained this issue in more than one place in our books. Some of those who were not versed in knowledge imagined that the news of Al-Harith bin Ubaid, on the authority of Matar, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, May God bless him and grant him peace. He has not prostrated in any part of the joint since he turned to Medina. The proof of those who claim that there is no prostration in the joint, and this is of the same type. What I know is that a witness is someone who testifies to seeing or hearing something, not someone who denies it or rejects it, and Abu Hurairah knew that he had seen The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prostrated when the sky split open, and he recited “In the name of your Lord who created” after he turned to Medina, as it was I accompanied him only after the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to Medina, not before."
"560","We have the news of Al-Harith bin Ubaid Muhammad bin Rafi’, we have Azhar bin Al-Qasim, we have Abu Qudamah, who is Al-Harith bin Ubaid. It was narrated by Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi, on the authority of al-Harith ibn Ubaid. He said: Matar al-Warraq told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, or someone else, on the authority of Ibn Abbas."
"561","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Al-Shahid, Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala Al-San’ani, and Abu Al-Ash’ath Ahmad bin Al-Miqdam Al-Ajli said: Al-Mu`tamir, Al-Shahidi said, he said: I heard my father, he said: And Bakr told me, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, he said: “I prayed the dark prayer with Abu Hurairah, He recited: When the sky split open, so he prostrated. I said to him: What is this prostration? He said: I prostrated with it behind Abu al-Qasim, may God bless him and grant him peace. Al-San’ani said: On the authority of his father, and he added at the end of the report: So I will continue to prostrate with it until I meet him. Abu Al-Ash'ath said, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Bakr bin Abdullah, he said: I prayed behind Abu Al-Qasim, and he prostrated with it, and I will continue to prostrate with it until... Abu Al-Qasim, may God bless him and grant him peace, delivered"
"562","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad narrated to us, Muhammad bin Yazid bin Khunnis narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told me, he said: Ibn Abbas narrated to me, a man came to the Messenger of God God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “O Messenger of God, this night I saw what the sleeper saw as if I was praying behind a tree, so I saw It is as if I recited a prostration and prostrated, and I saw the tree as if it was prostrating with my prostration, so I heard it prostrating, and it was saying: O God, write for me You have a reward for it, and keep it for me as a reserve for me, and relieve me of a burden for it, and accept it from me as you accepted it from your servant David. He said Ibn Abbas: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, reciting the prostration, then prostrated, so I heard him while he was prostrating, saying the same as what the man said. “about the words of the tree”"
"563","Ahmad bin Ja`far al-Halwani narrated to us, Muhammad bin Yazid bin Khunais narrated to us, he said: Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Ubaidullah bin Abi Yazid prayed with us. In this mosque, meaning the Sacred Mosque, in the month of Ramadan, he used to recite the prostration, then prostrate and prolong the prostration, and he was told about that, He said: Ibn Jurayj told me: Your grandfather Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Yazid told me, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: So he mentioned something similar, and said: “And spare me from it.” A burden, and he did not say: Accept it from me as you accepted it from your servant David.” Abu Bakr said: But I had neglected to dictate the report of Abu Al-Aliyah, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say in prostration The Qur’an at night: “My face prostrated itself before Him who created it, and His hearing and sight split, by His strength and power,” because between Khalid is the shoe and between Abu is the high An unnamed man. The man was not mentioned: Abdul Wahhab bin Abdul Majeed, and Khaled bin Abdullah Al-Wasiti."
"564","No, Bundar, I am Abdul Wahhab, I am Khaled and he is the shoe, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliya, on the authority of Aisha. H Abu Bishr al-Wasiti, our name is Khaled, meaning Ibn Abdullah, narrated to us on the authority of Khalid, which is the shoe, on the authority of Abu al-Aaliyah, on the authority of Aisha However, Abu Bishr did not say: at night, and added: He says that three times."
"565","On the authority of Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi, on the authority of Ibn Al-Aliyah, on the authority of Khalid Al-Hadha, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with him. It is similar to the hadith of Bundar, except that he said: He says “repeatedly in prostration.” Abu Bakr said: I only dictated this news and explained its reason at this time for fear that some students of knowledge would be tempted by the narration. Al-Thaqafi, and Khaled bin Abdullah, so it is imagined that the narration of Abdul-Wahhab and Khaled bin Abdullah is authentic."
"566","Yunus ibn Abd al-Ala al-Sadfi told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Abu Sakhr told us, on the authority of Ibn Qusayt, on the authority of Kharijah ibn Zayd ibn Thabit, on the authority of his father, said: “I showed the star to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, but none of us prostrated.” Abu Sakhr said: I prayed behind Omar bin Abdul Aziz and Abu Bakr bin Hazm, but they did not prostrate."
"567","Na.... Abu Bakr bin Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Othman bin Abdul Rahman Al-Taymi, on the authority of Rabia bin Abdullah bin Al-Hudair Al-Taymi, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Mulaika said: Rabi’ah was one of the best people among those who attended Omar ibn al-Khattab. Rabi’ah said: Omar ibn al-Khattab recited on the day Friday prayer on the pulpit, Surah An-Nahl, until when he came to prostrate, he said: “O people, we only pass by prostration, so whoever prostrates, he has attained And do good, and whoever does not prostrate, there is no sin on him, and he does not prostrate.”"
"568","We told Bundar, we told Yahya, Ibn Dhib told us. H. Bundar narrated to us once, Yahya narrated to us, and Uthman bin Omar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Qusayt, on the authority of Ata bin Yassar, on the authority of Zaid bin Thabit, said: “I recited to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, the star, but he did not prostrate.” Abu Bakr said: Abu Sakhr narrated this news, on the authority of Ibn Qusayt, on the authority of Kharijah bin Zayd, and Ata bin Yasar all of them told us. With them, Ahmad bin Abd al-Rahman bin Wahb, narrated by my uncle, on the authority of Abi Sakhr, with two chains of transmission separately. It was narrated by Yazid bin Khusaifa, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Qusayt, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, that he informed him, that he asked Zaid bin Thabit, and he claimed that he recited to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “And the Star” when it descended, but he did not prostrate. Narrated by Ali bin Hajar, narrated by Ismail bin Jafar, on the authority of Yazid bin Khusaifa"
"569","Narrated by Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Ala’, Sa’id ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Makhzoumi, and Ali ibn Khashram, and this is the hadith of al-Makhzoumi, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If the reader believes, then they believe. “The angels provide security, so whoever’s security coincides with the security of the angels, his previous sins will be forgiven.” Al-Makhzoumi once said: He said: I heard Al-Zuhri"
"570","I am Ahmad ibn Abdah al-Dhabi. Abd al-Aziz, meaning Ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi, informed us, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If the imam believes, then they believe, then whoever’s words agree with the words of the angels, his previous deeds will be forgiven.” \His sin.\"" Abu Bakr said regarding the saying of the Prophet"
"571","We are Muhammad bin Yahya, we are Ishaq bin Ibrahim, who is the son of Al-Ala’ Al-Zubaidi, Amr bin Al-Harith narrated to me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Salem, On the authority of Al-Zubaidi, he said: Al-Zuhri told me, on the authority of Abu Salamah, and Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was When he finished reciting the Mother of the Qur’an, he raised his voice and said: “Amen.”"
"572","Muhammad ibn Yahya told me, Abu Sa`id al-Ju’fi told me, Ibn Wahb told me, Osama, who is Ibn Zayd, told me on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, “When he was with the imam reciting the Mother of the Qur’an, the people believed. Ibn Omar believed, and saw that Sunnah.”"
"573","Muhammad ibn Hassan al-Azraq narrated to us a strange news, if he preserved the connection of the chain of transmission. Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Bilal, that he said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Do not precede me with an Amen.” Abu Bakr said: This is how Muhammad bin Hassan dictated this hadith to us from its origin.. Al-Thawri, on the authority of Asim, and he said: On the authority of Bilal, The narrators only say in this chain of transmission, on the authority of Abu Uthman: that Bilal said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace:"
"574","From Abu Bishr Al-Wasiti, from Khaled, meaning Ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Suhail, who is Ibn Abi Saleh, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, She said: A Jew entered the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: May peace be upon you, Muhammad. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “And upon you,” so she said Aisha: Then I decided to speak, but I knew that I hated the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, for that reason, so I remained silent, then another man came in and said: May peace be upon you, so he said: “On you.” I was about to speak, and I knew how much he hated the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, for that. Then the third person entered and said: “May peace be upon you,” so I was not even patient. I said: And upon you is the poison and the wrath and curse of God, brothers of apes and pigs. Will you greet the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with something that God did not greet him with? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God does not like indecency or indecency.” They said something, and we responded to them. Indeed, the Jews are an envious people. They do not envy us for anything as they envy us for peace and Amen.” Abu Bakr said: Ibn Abi Mulaika reported on the authority of Aisha about this story. I narrated it in the book of Al-Kabir."
"575","Muhammad bin Abd al-Ala al-San’ani and Amr bin Ali told us, they said: Yazid told us, and he is Ibn Zurai’, I am Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyib, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “When the imam says: ‘Not those with anger nor those who go astray’, Surah Al-Fatihah, verse 7, So say: Amen, for the angels say: Amen, and the imam says: Amen. So whoever’s assurance coincides with the assurance of the angels, his previous deeds will be forgiven. \His sin.\"" This is the hadith of Al-Sana’ani"""
"576","I am Ahmad bin Mani`, I am the soul of Ibn Juraij. H Al-Hasan bin Muhammad told us, a spirit told us, Ibn Jurayj told us. H Al-Hasan Al-Zaafrani also told us, Hajjaj bin Muhammad, he said: Ibn Juraij said, Amr bin Yahya told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya Ibn Hayyan, on the authority of his uncle Wasi Ibn Hayyan, that he asked Ibn Umar about the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “God is greater whenever He lowered, God is greater the more He raised.” This is the wording of the hadith of Al-Hasan bin Muhammad, and Ibn Mani’ said: On the authority of Ibn Omar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: “God “The Greatest” whenever he raises and lowers, and increases, then he says: “Peace and God’s mercy be upon you, on his right,” “Peace and God’s mercy be upon you, on his left.” Abu Bakr said: The companions of Amr bin Yahya disagreed regarding this chain of transmission, so he said: He asked Abdullah bin Zayd bin Asim, I included it in The big book"
"577","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi told us, Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: I saw a man at the shrine, saying “Allahu Akbar” at every turn. Raising and lowering, so I came to Ibn Abbas and said: “I saw a man praying and saying “Allahu Akbar” in every raising and lowering position, so he said: Isn’t that the prayer of the Messenger of God? May God bless him and grant him peace, do you not have a mother?”"
"578","This is Muhammad bin Rafi’, this is Abd al-Razzaq, I am Ibn Jurayj, Ibn Shihab told me, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abd al-Rahman, that he heard Abu Kitten, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he stood up to pray, he would say “Allahu Akbar” when he stood up, then he would say “Allahu Akbar” when he bowed, then he would say: “Allah has heard.” To the one who praises Him when he raises his back from the rak’ah, he says while standing: Our Lord, and to You be praise, then he says “Allahu Akbar” when he descends prostrating, then he says “Allahu Akbar” when he rises his head, then he says takbeer when he prostrates, then he says takbeer when he raises his head, then he does the same for the entire prayer until he completes it, and he says takbeer when He stands up from the bend after sitting.” Then Abu Hurairah says: I am most like you in prayer to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"579","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, he said: Abu Hurairah was “He leads us in prayer, saying “Allahu Akbar” when he stands, when he bows, and when he wants to prostrate, and after he rises from bowing, and when he wants to prostrate after He does not rise from prostration, and when he sits, and when he wants to stand in the two rak’ahs, he says “Allahu Akbar” and he pronounces “Allahu Akbar” in the same way in the other two rak’ahs. He said: “By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I am the closest of you in resemblance to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, meaning his prayer. This continued his prayer until He left the world\""
580"""
"580","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us: Abu 'Amir narrated to us: Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us: from Sa'id ibn al-Harith, who said: Abu Hurayrah fell ill, or was absent, so Abu Sa'id al-Khudri led us in prayer. He raised his voice with the takbir when he opened the prayer, when he bowed, when he said: ""Allah hears whoever praises Him,"" when he raised his head from prostration, when he prostrated, when he raised his head, and when he stood up from the two rak'ahs, until he completed his prayer in that manner. It was said to him: ""The people have differed concerning your prayer."" So he went out and stood on the pulpit and said: ""O people, by Allah, I do not care whether your prayer differs or not; this is how I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray."" Abu Bakr said: His statement ""and when he said: Allah hears whoever praises Him"" means only that when he said ""Allah hears whoever praises Him,"" he intended the movement toward prostration, he said the takbir; not that he said the takbir when he raised his head from bowing. And likewise he intended in the report of 'Imran ibn Husayn when he mentioned his prayer behind 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, and said: ""And when he rose from bowing he said the takbir,"" he meant only that he rose from bowing, intending the movement toward prostration, he said the takbir."
"581","The evidence for the correctness of what I have interpreted is that Harun bin Ishaq Al-Hamdani narrated to us, saying: Abdah narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Khaled, meaning Al-Hudha’, on the authority of Ghaylan ibn Jarir, on the authority of Mutarrif ibn Abdullah ibn Al-Shakheer, who said: “I prayed behind Ali, and he used to say “Allahu Akbar” when he prostrated and when he rose. His head.” When he left, Imran bin Husayn said to me: “This man led us in prayer like the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” Abu Bakr said: And it is true This news does not indicate that the word that Hammad bin Zayd mentioned, on the authority of Ghaylan bin Jarir, in this news, and when he got up from bowing He said “Allahu Akbar”, but he wanted to say “Allahu Akbar”, and when he got up from bowing and wanted to prostrate, he said “Allahu Akbar”, according to what Al-Zuhri mentioned, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Al-Harith bin Hisham, then he says: God hears those who praise Him when he raises his back from the rak’ah, then he says while standing: Our Lord, to You is praise, then He says takbeer when he falls prostrating, and likewise the narration of Abu Amir, on the authority of Fulayh, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Sa’id al-Khudri, he mentioned takbeer when He said: God hears those who praise Him, that is, He says “Allahu Akbar” when raising the head from bowing. He mentioned another “Allahu Akbar” when one desires to prostrate, so when he mentioned Takbeer when raising the head from prostration after saying Takbeer, when he said: God hears whoever praises Him, it is proven that he only wanted to say Takbeer, when He said: God hears whoever praises Him, when he desires to prompt prostration, and likewise in the narration of Abu Salamah from Abu Hurairah, he said: And when he bows, And if he wanted to prostrate after he had risen from bowing, this indicates that he was saying “Allahu Akbar” when he raised his head from bowing, and he wanted to prostrate without He used to say “Allahu Akbar” when raising his head from bowing, and if we allowed the praying person to say “Allahu Akbar” at every lowering and raising of his head, he would have to say “Allahu Akbar” if He raised his head from bowing, then he would say “Allahu Akbar” upon desire to prostrate, so the number of “Allahu Akbar” in four rak’ahs would be twenty-six, not two. And twenty takbirs, and in the narration of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, it was proven that the number of takbirs in four rak’ahs is twenty-two. A takbeer, nothing more"
"582","He said: Tell us the news of Ikrimah Nasr bin Ali Al-Jahdhami. He said: Abdul-Ala told us, Saeed told us. H Abu Musa, Ibn Abi Adi, told us on the authority of Saeed. H And Ali bin Khashram told us, Isa, meaning Ibn Yunus, told us, both of them on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: I told Ibn Abbas: I prayed the noon prayer with Batha’ behind a foolish sheikh, and he said “Allahu Akbar” twenty-two times when he prostrated, when he bowed, and when he rose. His head, and Ibn Abbas said: “That is the Sunnah of Abu Al-Qasim, may God bless him and grant him peace.” This is the wording of the hadith of Abu Musa. Ibn Khashram said: “That is the Sunnah of Abu Al-Qasim, or the prayer of Abu Al-Qasim, may God bless him and grant him peace.” Saeed doubted. Nasr said: “That is the prayer of Abu al-Qasim,” and he had no doubt. Bundar told us, Muadh bin Hisham told us, my father told me, on the authority of Qatada, with this chain of transmission similar to it."
"583","Narrated by Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala Al-Attar, narrated by Sufyan, who said: I heard Al-Zuhri saying: I heard Salim telling, on the authority of his father. H. Ali bin Hajar Al-Saadi, Ali bin Khashram, Saeed bin Abdul Rahman Al-Makhzoumi, and Utba bin Abdullah told us. Al-Yahmadi, Al-Hasan bin Muhammad, Yunus bin Abdul-Ala Al-Sadafi, Muhammad bin Rafi’, Ali bin Al-Azhar, and others said: Na Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, raising his hands when he began the prayer so that he would be in line with his shoulders, and when he wants to bow, and after he rises from bowing, and he does not rise between the two prostrations.” This is the wording of Ibn Rafi’. I heard Al-Makhzoumi saying: Which chain of narration is more authentic than this. He said: I heard Muhammad bin Yahya narrating on the authority of Ali bin Abdullah. He said: Sufyan said: This chain of transmission is like this cylinder."
"584","Al-Rabi’ bin Suleiman Al-Muradi and Bahr bin Nasr Al-Khawlani told us, they said: Ibn Wahb told us, Ibn Abi Al-Zanad told me. H Muhammad bin Yahya and Muhammad bin Rafi’ narrated to us, saying: Sulaiman bin Dawud Al-Hashimi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman bin Abi narrated to me. Al-Zanad, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Fadl Al-Hashimi, Abdul Rahman Al-Araj informed us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Rafi’, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that “when he stood up to perform the obligatory prayer, he would say “Allahu Akbar” and raise his hands He does the same when he finishes his recitation and wants to bow, and he does it when he rises from bowing, and he does not raise his hands in Part of his prayer while he was sitting, and when he stood up from the two prostrations, he raised his hands in the same way and said “Allahu Akbar.”"
"585","From Abu Bishr al-Wasiti, from Khaled, meaning Ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Khaled, who is the shoe, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, that he saw Malik ibn Al-Huwaithir: “When he prays, he says “Allahu Akbar” and raises his hands, and when he wants to bow down, he raises his hands, and when he raises his head from bowing, he raises his hands, and it happened that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray like this.”"
"586","Bundar and Yahya bin Hakim told us, they said: Abd al-Wahhab, who is al-Thaqafi, told us. Ayyub told me, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, Malik told us. Ibn Al-Huwaith, he said: We came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when we were young, close together, and we stayed with him for twenty nights. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was merciful and gentle. When he thought that we had longed for our families and were longing for us, he asked about what we had left behind. So we informed him, and he said: “Go back to your families and stay among them, teach them, and teach them,” and he mentioned things that I remember and things that I do not remember. And pray as you have seen me praying. When the time for prayer comes, let one of you call the call to prayer and let the eldest of you lead in prayer.” This is the wording of the hadith of Bundar. Abu Bakr said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered Malik bin Al-Huwaith and the young men who were with him to pray as they saw the Prophet praying. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and Malik bin Al-Huwayrith knew that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to raise his hands when he said the takbir in prayer, and when He bowed, and if he raised his head from bowing, this indicates that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded the hands to be raised, if the worshiper wanted Bowing, and when he raises his head from bowing, and every word narrated in this section, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to raise his hands when He bowed, so he is of the type that I learned that the Arabs may apply the active participle to the one who wanted to do the action before he did it, as God says: O Those who believe, when you stand for prayer, wash your faces. Surat Al-Ma’idah, verse 6. God Almighty only commanded the washing of the parts of ablution when He wanted a person to stand up for prayer, not after standing for it, so the meaning of his saying: when you stand for prayer: that is, if you want to stand for it, This is also the meaning of his saying: He raises his hands when he bows, that is, if he wants to bow, as reported by Ali bin Abi Talib and Ibn Omar, who mentioned him, And if he wanted to bow, we included these reports in their entirety in the Book of Al-Kabir, as well as his saying: “So when you enter houses, salute “On yourselves”: He only commanded to greet each other when he wanted to enter, not after entering the house. This word, if gathered from the Qur’an and Sunnah, is long. The book by examining it"
"587","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan told us, Abd al-Hamid bin Jaafar told us, Muhammad bin Ata’, who is Muhammad bin Amr ibn Ata’ traces his lineage back to his grandfather, on the authority of Abu Humaid al-Sa’idi, who said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up to pray, he would stand up straight for prayer. He stood up, mentioned some of the hadith, and said: Then he said: “Allahu Akbar,” and he bowed down, then he straightened up and neither tilted his head nor was he persuaded, and he placed his hands on His knees, then he said: “God hears whoever praises Him,” and he raised his hands and straightened, until every bone returned to its right place, then he descended to He prostrated himself on the ground, then he said: “Allahu Akbar,” then he moved his upper arms away from his armpits, opened his toes, then bent his left leg and sat. On it, then he straightened up until every bone returned to its straight place, then he descended, prostrating, then said: “Allahu Akbar,” then he bent his leg. He sat down and straightened up until every bone returned to its place, then he got up, then in the second rak’ah he did something like that, so that when he got up from The two prostrations, he said “Allahu Akbar” and raised his hands so that he would align them with his shoulders, as he did when he opened the prayer, then he did likewise, and even if it was the rak’ah that At the end of the prayer, he put his left leg behind him and sat on his side, bowing, then said the salaam. Abu Bakr said: Muhammad ibn Ata’ is Muhammad ibn Amr. Ibn Ataa"
"588","Our name is Abdul Rahman bin Bishr bin Al-Hakam, I am Yahya bin Saeed, and this is how he said: On the authority of Muhammad bin Ata. Bundar, Muhammad bin Yahya, and Ahmad bin Saeed al-Darimi told us, they said: Abu Asim told us, Abd al-Hamid bin Jaafar told us, Muhammad bin Amr bin Ata’ told me, saying: I heard Abu Humayd al-Sa’idi among ten of the companions of the Messenger of God, one of whom was Abu Qatada. He said: “I inform you of the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” They mentioned the length of the hadith, and they said at the end of the hadith: “You have spoken the truth, this is how it was.” The Prophet prays\""
589"""
"589","Bundar narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us: al-'Abbas ibn Sahl al-Sa'idi narrated to me, saying: A group of the Ansar gathered, among them Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi, Abu Humayd al-Sa'idi, and Abu Usayd al-Sa'idi. They mentioned the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Abu Humayd said: ""Let me tell you, for I am the most knowledgeable of you concerning this."" They said: ""Then tell us."" He said: ""I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform wudu excellently, then he entered the prayer and said the takbir, raising his hands level with his shoulders. Then he bowed, placing his hands on his knees as if grasping them, neither lowering his head nor raising it up, and he kept his arms away from his sides. Then he raised his head, standing straight until every bone returned to its place."" Then Bundar mentioned the rest of the hadith, and said at its end: ""All the people said: Thus was the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."" I heard Muhammad ibn Yahya say: ""Whoever hears this hadith, then does not raise his hands — meaning when he bows and when he raises his head from bowing — his prayer is deficient."""
"590","Bundar, Ahmad bin Abdah, Yahya bin Hakim, and Abd al-Rahman bin Bishr, and this is the hadith of Bundar, Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Saeed ibn Abi Saeed al-Maqbari, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He entered the mosque, and a man entered and prayed. Then he greeted the Prophet, and he responded to him. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Go back and pray, for you have not prayed.” Until he did that three times, then the man said: By the One who has sent you with the truth, I do not know anything other than this. He said: So he said: “When you stand up to pray, say “Allahu Akbar”, then say “Allahu Akbar.” Recite whatever is easy for you from the Qur’an, then bow until you are at ease in your bowing, then rise until you are standing upright, then prostrate until you are at ease in your prostration. Then rise until you are sitting upright, and do that throughout your entire prayer.” Ahmed bin Abdah said: On the authority of Saeed. Abu Bakr said: The news of Ali bin Yahya bin Khallad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Rifa’ah bin Rafi’, I narrated in the book of Al-Kabir. Abu Bakr said: No one narrated this news on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of his father other than Yahya ibn Saeed. They said: On the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Abu Hurairah."
"591","We are Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi, we are Abu Muawiyah, we are Al-Amash. And we are Harun bin Ishaq Al-Hamdani, I am Ibn Fudayl, on the authority of Al-Amash. H, Salam bin Junada told us, Waki` told us, Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Amara bin Umayr, on the authority of Abu Muammar, on the authority of Abu Masoud, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “The prayer of one who does not straighten his head when bowing and prostrating is not sufficient.”"
"592","On the authority of Bundar, on the authority of Ibn Abi Adi, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Sulayman, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abu Muammar, on the authority of Abu Masoud, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “A prayer is not sufficient for anyone or for a man who does not straighten his head when bowing or prostrating.” From Bishr bin Khaled Al-Askari, from Muhammad, meaning Ibn Jafar, on the authority of Shu’bah, who said: I heard Suleiman, who said: I heard Amara bin Umair, With this chain of transmission, the same, and he said: “In bowing and prostrating.”"
"593","Abu Musa Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna and Ahmad bin Al-Miqdam told us, they said: Mulazim bin Amr told us, my grandfather Abdullah bin Badr told me, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Ali bin Shayban, on the authority of his father Ali bin Shayban, who was one of the delegation, said: We prayed behind the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, Then he gestured with the back of his eyes to a man who did not straighten his back when bowing or prostrating. When the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, finished the prayer, he said: “O people! Muslims, there is no prayer for one who does not straighten his back while bowing and prostrating.” This is the hadith of Ahmad bin Al-Miqdam"
"594","Musa bin Harun bin Abdullah Al-Bazzaz told us, Abu Al-Hasan Al-Harith bin Abdullah Al-Hamdani, known as Ibn Al-Khazen, told us. Hushaym, on the authority of Asim ibn Kulayb, on the authority of Alqamah ibn Wa’il, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “when he bowed, he would be relieved.” \His fingers\"""""
"595","We are Muhammad bin Aban, we are Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Azdi, Abu Bakr said: He is Ibn Idris bin Yazid Al-Azdi, named after his grandfather. He said, Asim bin Kulayb told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al Aswad, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught us He said the prayer and said: “So he said ‘Allahu Akbar’, and when he wanted to bow, he placed his hands between his knees and bowed.” This reached Sa’d, and he said: He is right, my brother. We were We do this, then we were ordered to do this, meaning to hold on to the knees."
"596","Narrated by Salam bin Junada, narrated by Waki’, on the authority of Ibn Abi Khaled, and he is Ismail. H Yusuf bin Musa, Waki’, and Abu Usama narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Adiy, on the authority of Mus’ab Ibn Saad, he said: “When I bowed, I put my hands between my knees, and Abu Saad saw me, and he forbade me, and said: We were doing it, then we were forbidden, then We were commanded to raise them to the knees.”"
"597","Narrated to me by Muammal bin Hisham Al-Yashkari, narrated to me by Ismail, meaning Ibn Ulayya, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, narrated to me by Ali bin Yahya bin Khallad bin Rafi’ al-Ansari, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his uncle Rifa’ah ibn Rafi’: That a man entered the mosque, prayed, and mentioned the length of the hadith, and said: So he said The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Then when you kneel, place your hands firmly on your knees until every bone in you is at ease.”"
"598","Yusuf bin Musa narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Salim Al-Barrad, who said: We came to Uqba bin Amr Abu Masoud, and we said: He told us about the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “So he stood up in front of us in the mosque, and said the takbir, and when he bowed, he said the takbir, and placed his palms on the His knees, and he placed his fingers lower than that, then he touched his elbows, then he said: This is how we saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying.”"
"599","We are Ali bin Hajar Al-Saadi, we are Ismail bin Jafar, and Sufyan bin Uyaynah. H. Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala’ and Sa’id bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Makhzoumi told us, saying: Sufyan told us, all of them, on the authority of Sulayman bin Suhaim, On the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Ma’abad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “As for bowing, be great in it.” \Lord\"""""
"600","We are Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna, we are Abdullah bin Zaid, we are Musa bin Ayyub, he said: I heard my uncle Iyas bin Amir, saying: I heard Uqba bin Amir He says: When it was revealed, “Glorify in the name of your Lord the Great,” Surah Al-Waqi’ah, verse 74, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to us: “Put it in your bowing.”"
"601","From us Muhammad bin Issa, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Musa bin Ayyub, on the authority of his uncle, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, with the same"
"602","Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, Ibrahim Ibn Abdullah Ibn Ma’abad informed me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: That the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, removed the curtain and saw the people standing behind Abu Bakr praying, so he said: “O God, have I conveyed the message that there is no longer any of the bearers of prophethood remaining.” Except for the good dream that a Muslim sees for himself or for himself, and I am forbidden to recite while bowing or prostrating, so as for bowing, magnify the Lord in it. As for prostration, supplicate frequently, for it is certain that you will be answered.” Muhammad bin Yahya told us: Abu Asim once said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, raised the veil while the people were standing and praying behind Abu Bakr. The narration of Ismail and Ibn Uyaynah is not exactly this, and I summarized it."
"603","Muammal bin Hisham Al-Yashkari and Salam bin Junada Al-Qurashi told us, they said: Abu Muawiyah, I am Al-Amash, narrated to us, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Al-Mustarid bin Al-Ahnaf, on the authority of Silah, on the authority of Hudhayfah, said: I prayed with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, one night, and his bowing was like When he stood up, he said while bowing: “Glory be to my Lord, the Great.” Salam said: On the authority of Al-A’mash. Abu Musa and Ya’qub bin Ibrahim told us, they said: Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, with this chain of transmission, he said: I prayed with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, one night, and he used to say while bowing: “Glory be to my Lord, the Great.” From Bundar, from Yahya, from Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi, from Ibn Abi Adi, from Shu’bah. Bishr bin Khalid Al-Askari, Muhammad bin Jaafar, Shu’bah, narrated to us something similar."
"604","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi, Muhammad bin Aban, and Salam bin Junada told us, they said: Hafs bin Ghayath told us, Ibn Abi told us Layla, on the authority of Al-Shabi, on the authority of Silah, on the authority of Hudhayfah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say while bowing: “Glory be to my Lord the Great” three times."
"605","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi and Yusuf bin Musa told us, they said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Al-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha. She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to often say in his bowing and prostration: “Glory be to You, O God, our Lord, and with Your praise, O God.” Forgive me, he interprets the Qur’an.” Salam bin Junada narrated to us, Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, with this, and he said: Which is often said, to say: “Glory be to You, O God, and with Your praise.”"
"606","Al-Sana'ani Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, Khaled told us, meaning Ibn Al-Harith, Shu'bah told us, he said: Qatada told me, on the authority of Mutarrif, On the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say while bowing: “Glory be to the Holy One, Lord of the angels and the spirit.” Abu Bakr said: This difference of opinion regarding bowing is a permissible difference, so it is permissible for the praying person to say while bowing everything that we have narrated, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: In his bowing"
"607","Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Muhammad and Abu Yahya Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim, who said: Narrated to us Rawḥ ibn 'Ubadah, who said: Narrated to me Ibn Jurayj, who informed me Musa ibn 'Uqbah, from 'Abdullah ibn al-Faḍl, from 'Abd al-Raḥman al-A'raj, from 'Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi', from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib (RA), that the Prophet (ﷺ) when he would bow in rukū', would say:\n\n*\Allāhumma laka rakʿahtu"
"608","We have Bundar, we have Abu Dawud, we have Falih bin Sulaiman, Al-Abbas bin Sahl Al-Saadi told me, he said: Some people from the Ansar gathered, including Sahl. Ibn Saad Al-Sa’idi, Abu Humaid Al-Sa’idi, and Abu Usayd Al-Sa’idi, they mentioned the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Abu Humaid said: Let me narrate to you, for I inform you of this. They said: So he narrated. He said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He performed ablution well, then he entered. prayer, and he said “Allahu Akbar” and raised his hands to the level of his shoulders, then he bowed and placed his hands on his knees like one holding them, so he did not touch his head or To convince him, he moved his hands away from his sides, then raised his head and stood upright until every bone in it returned to its place. Then he mentioned the rest. Hadith, and all the people said: This is the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"609","Ahmad bin Abdah al-Dhabi told us, Hammad bin Zaid told us, Thabit al-Bunani told us. Ahmad bin Al-Miqdam, narrated to us Hammad bin Zaid, on the authority of Thabit, said: Anas bin Malik said to us: “I do not hesitate to lead you in prayer.” Just as I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying.” Thabit said: Anas was doing something that I do not see you doing. Whenever he raised his head from bowing, he stood up, so much so that we say he forgot."
"610","We are Muhammad bin Bashar Bandar, we are Muhammad bin Jaafar, Shu`bah told us. H. Salam bin Junada narrated to us, on the authority of Waki’, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Azib He said: “The bowing of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and raising his head after bowing and prostration, and his sitting between the two prostrations were close to the same.” . This is a sufficient hadith, from Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam, from Yazid, meaning Ibn Zurayi, from Shu`bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam ibn Utaiba, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman. Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Al-Baraa Ibn Aazib, said: “The bowing of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and when he raised his head from bowing, And his prostration, and what is between the two prostrations is close to being equal.”"
"611","This is Muhammad bin Rafi’, I am Abd al-Razzaq, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Ibn Shihab informed me, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abd al-Rahman, that He heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to say: God hears those who praise Him” when he raised his cross from bowing, then he said And he said: “Our Lord, to You be praise.”"
"612","We are Muhammad bin Yahya, we are Hajjaj bin Abi Minhal, and Abu Salih, all on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Abdullah bin Abi Salamah. H Muhammad bin Rafi’ narrated to us, I am Hujain bin Al-Muthanna Abu Omar, Abd al-Aziz bin Abi Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of his uncle Al-Majishun bin Abi Salamah, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Rafi’, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: That when he opened the prayer, he said “Allahu Akbar.” They mentioned some of the hadith, and said: When he raised his head, meaning from bowing, he said: “God hears those who praise Him. Our Lord, to You belongs all praise, filling the heavens, filling the earth, and filling whatever you wish after that.”"
"613","Zakaria bin Yahya bin Aban and Ahmad bin Yazid bin Alil al-Muqri’an told us, they said: Abdullah bin Yusuf told us, Sa’id, meaning Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Atiya bin Qais, on the authority of Qaza bin Yahya, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, When he said: “God hears those who praise Him,” he would say: “O God, our Lord, to You belongs all praise, filling the heavens, filling the earth, and filling whatever You wish after that.” “Those who deserve praise and glory are more deserving,” said the servant, “and we are all your servants. There is no objection to what you have given, and the grandfather is of no use to you.” One word, except that Ahmed said: “Our Lord, praise be to You.” Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abu Mushar told us, Saeed bin Abdul Aziz told us about this, and he added, and said: “And there is no giver of what you withhold.” Bahr bin Nasr also narrated to us, Bishr bin Bakr narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed bin Abdul Aziz, with this"
"614","It is narrated by Issa bin Ibrahim Al-Ghafiqi, it is Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nu’aym bin Abdullah, that Ali bin Yahya Al-Zarqi narrated to him. H Yunus bin Abdul-Ala al-Sadfi told us, Ibn Wahb told us that Malik told him, on the authority of Nu’aym bin Abdullah bin al-Mujmar, On the authority of Ali bin Yahya Al-Zarqi. H Al-Hasan bin Muhammad narrated to us, I am Ruh bin Ubadah, narrated to us by Malik, on the authority of Nu’aym bin Abdullah, that Ali bin Yahya Al-Zarqi told him, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Rifa’ah ibn Rafi’, that he said: One day we were praying behind the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he raised his head from Bowing down, he said: “God hears whoever praises Him,” and a man behind him said: Our Lord, praise be to You, much, good and blessed praise. When the Messenger of God departed, May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: “Who spoke above?” A man said: “I.” The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “I saw thirty-four \They will issue it hastily"
"615","On the authority of Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: Al-Zuhri did not tell us, except on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He prayed In the morning, when he raised his head from the second rak’ah. H Ahmad bin Abdah and Saeed bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, raised his head from the last rak’ah, he said: “O God, save Al-Walid bin Al-Walid and Salama bin Hisham. And Ayyash ibn Abi Rabi’ah, and the oppressed in Mecca.” Ahmad added: “from the Muslims,” and they said: Oh God, intensify your influence on Mudar, and make it difficult for them. Years like the years of Joseph.” Abu Bakr said: I have included this chapter in its entirety in the Book of Prayer, the Book of the Great."
"616","On the authority of Bundar, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Jaafar, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, who said: I heard Ibn Abi Laila, he said: I heard Al-Baraa ibn Azib, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to perform Qunoot in the sunset and the morning prayers.”"
"617","This is Ahmad bin Abdah, this is Abu Dawud, Hisham told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the afterlife, he would raise his head from bowing and say: “God hears those who praise Him,” he recited a Qunoot, and he said: Oh God, save Ayyash bin Abi Rabi’ah, Oh God, save Salama bin Hisham, Oh God, save Al-Walid bin Al-Walid, Oh God, save the oppressed from The believers from the people of Mecca, O God, intensify your burden on Mudar, O God, make it years for them like the years of Joseph.”"
"618","Muhammad bin Yahya told us, I am Abu Al-Numan, I am Thabit bin Yazid Abu Zaid Al-Ahwal, Hilal bin Khabbab told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: You recited the Qunoot of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, for a successive month in the noon, afternoon, sunset, evening, and morning prayers in the afternoon. Every prayer, when he says: “God hears him who praises Him,” in the last rak’ah, he supplicates for a neighborhood of Banu Salim who is well-behaved, of good standing, and of disobedience, and he believes Behind him.” He said: He sent to them inviting them to Islam, and they killed them. Ikrimah said: This is the key to Qunoot."
"619","Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abu Dawud told us, Ibrahim bin Saad told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed, and Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was not obliged except to supplicate for someone, or to supplicate against someone, and whenever he said: “God hears those who praise Him,” He said: “Our Lord, praise be to You, O God, save me,” and he mentioned the hadith."
"620","Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Marzuq Al-Bahili told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Ansari told us, Saeed bin Abi Arouba told us, on the authority of Qatada, On the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “would not recite Qunoun unless he supplicated for a people, or supplicated against a people.”"
"621","Ali bin Sahl Al-Ramli told us, Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, Abu Amr Al-Awza’i told me, on the authority of Yahya, Abu Salamah told us, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited the Qunoot during a month’s prayer, saying in his Qunot: “O God, save Al-Walid bin Al-Walid, O God, save Salama bin Hisham, O God, save Ayyash bin Abi Rabi’ah, O God, save the oppressed among the believers, O God, intensify your burden on Mudar, O God, grant them years like the years of Joseph.” Abu Hurairah said: Then one day the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not pray for them, so I mentioned that to him, and he said: “Or what? Do you think they have come?"
"622","Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, And peace be upon him, he said in the Fajr prayer when he raised his head from bowing: “Our Lord, and to You be praise” in the last rak’ah, then he said: “O God, curse so-and-so and so-and-so,” he prayed On some of the hypocrites, then God, Blessed and Most High, revealed: You have nothing to do with the matter. Whether He turns to them or punishes them, for they are wrongdoers. Surat Al Imran Verse 128"
"623","It was narrated to us by Yaḥyā ibn Ḥabīb al-Ḥāriṯī:\n> Narrated to us Khālid ibn al-Ḥāriṯ, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān, from Nāfiʿ, from ʿAbd Allāh (RA) that the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) used to supplicate against four individuals. Thereupon Allāh, the Exalted, revealed:\n*\Not for you [O Muḥammad] is the decision; whether He turns to them in mercy or punishes them—for they are wrongdoers.\""*\n[Sūrah Āl ʿImrān 3:128]\n\nHe (RA) said: \""So Allāh guided them to Islām.\""\n\nAbū Bakr (RA) said: \""This is also a strange (gharīb) narration.\""\n\nIt was narrated to us by Aḥmad ibn al-Miqdām al-ʿIjlī:\n> Narrated to us Khālid ibn al-Ḥāriṯ"
"624","This is Muhammad bin Rafi’, I am Abd al-Razzaq, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Ibn Shihab informed me, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abd al-Rahman, that He heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to “say “Allahu Akbar” when he fell prostrating.”"
"625","We were told by Bundar, Muhammad bin Yahya, and Ahmad bin Saeed al-Darimi, and this is the wording of Bundar. He said: Abu Asim told us, Abd told us. Al-Hamid bin Jaafar, alias Muhammad bin Amr bin Ata, said: I heard Abu Humayd Al-Saadi among ten of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, Among them is Abu Qatada. Abu Humaid said: I inform you of the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Indeed, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was If he stood up to pray, he mentioned some of the hadith, and said: Then he says: “Allahu Akbar,” then he falls to the ground, keeping his hands away from his sides. Muhammad bin Yahya said: He descends to the ground, spreading his hands away from his sides. Muhammad bin Yahya added: Then he prostrates, and they all said: They said: You are right, this is how the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray."
"626","Ali bin Muslim, Ahmad bin Sinan, Muhammad bin Yahya, and Raja bin Muhammad Al-Adhari told us: Yazid bin Harun told us, Sharik bin Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Wael bin Hajar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He used to place his knees before his hands when he prostrated.” Ahmad said, with hope: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he prostrated, placing his knees before his hands."
"627","Muhammad bin Amr bin Tammam Al-Masry told us, Asbagh Ibn Al-Faraj told us, Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Omar, On the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he used to “put his hands before his knees, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to do that.”"
"628","Our father, Ibrahim bin Ismail bin Yahya bin Salamah bin Kuhayl, told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Salamah, on the authority of Musab bin Saad, on the authority of Saad, he said: “We used to put the hands before the knees, so we were commanded to put the knees before the hands.”"
"629","Muhammad bin Yahya, Ahmad bin Sinan, Raja bin Muhammad Al-Adhari, and Ali bin Muslim told us, they said: Sahl bin Harun told us, Sharik bin Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Wael bin Hajar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was “He places his knees before his hands, and raises his hands before his knees when he rises.”"
"630","Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Ashjaj, Ziyad bin Ayyub, and Ma’mal bin Hisham narrated to us, they said: Ismail narrated to us, I am Ayoub, and Al-Ma’mal said: On the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he narrated it, saying: “The hands prostrate as the face prostrates, so when one of you puts his face down, Let him lower his hands, and when he raises them, let him raise them.”"
"631","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, Abdullah bin Yusuf told us, Al-Layth told us, Ibn Al-Had told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Amer bin Saad bin Abi Waqqas, on the authority of Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib, that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “When he prostrated The servant prostrated with him on seven sides: his face, his hands, his knees, and his feet.”"
"632","We are Bishr bin Muadh Al-Aqdi, I am Abu Awanah, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “I was commanded to prostrate on seven sides, and not to tie my hair or my clothes.”"
"633","Ahmad bin Al-Miqdam Al-Ajli told us, Yazid bin Zurayi told us, Shu’bah and Ruh bin Al-Qasim told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “I was commanded to prostrate on seven bones, and not to cover my hair or my clothes.”"
"634","Saeed bin Abdul Rahman Al Makhzoumi narrated, Sufyan narrated, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “He should prostrate on seven things: on his face, his hands, his knees, and his feet, and he forbade using a shawl of hair or clothing.”"
"635","Al-Makhzoumi narrated, Sufyan narrated, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, the same, except that he said: “Or he shrouds his clothes or... His hair,” and Ibn Tawus was passing his hand over his forehead and nose, saying: It is one."
"636","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Ibn Jurayj told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I was commanded to prostrate on all seven sides, and not to cover my hair or clothes, the forehead or the nose. And the hands, and the knees, and the feet.”"
"637","Muhammad bin Bashar Bandar told us, Abu Dawud told us, Fulayh bin Sulayman told us, Al-Abbas bin Sahl Al-Saadi told me, he said: People from The Ansar, including Sahl bin Saad al-Sa’idi, Abu Humaid al-Sa’idi, and Abu Usayd al-Sa’idi, so they mentioned the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him. Then Abu Humaid said: Let me speak to you, for I inform you of this. They said: Then he narrated. He said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He performed ablution well, then he entered the prayer, and mentioned some of the hadith, and said: “Then he prostrated, and raised his forehead and nose from the ground, and kept his hands away from His sides, then he raised his head, and all the people said: This is the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"638","It is narrated to me by Muammal bin Hisham, I am Ismail, meaning Ibn Ulayya, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, Ali bin Yahya bin Khallad narrated to me, on the authority of his father, On the authority of his uncle Rifa’ah, in a long hadith, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to the man who prayed and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered him to repeat Prayer, he said: “Then when you prostrate, keep your face and hands steady until every bone in you is secure in its place.”"
"639","We are Abdul-Rahman bin Bishr bin Al-Hakam, we are Ali, meaning Ibn Al-Hussein bin Waqid, my father told me, Abu Ishaq told me, he said: I heard Al-Baraa said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to “prostrate on the palms of the hand.”"
"640","We are Bundar, we are Abu Amer, I am Falih bin Suleiman Al-Madani, Abbas bin Sahl Al-Saadi told me, he said: Abu Humaid Al-Saadi met, And Abu Usayd al-Saadi, Sahl bin Saad, and Muhammad bin Maslamah, and Abu Humaid said: I inform you of the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said the salaam, so he stood up and said “Allahu Akbar”, and he mentioned some of the hadith, and said: “Then he prostrated, turning his nose and forehead, and moved his hands away from his sides, and placed He placed his palms in line with his shoulders, then raised his head until every bone was back in its place, until he was done.”"
"641","Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Ashjaj told us, Ibn Idris told us, Asim bin Kulayb told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Wael bin Hajar, he said: I came Medina, so I said: Let us look at the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I saw him. When he opened the prayer he said “Allahu Akbar” and raised his hands, so I saw “His thumbs were close to his ears.” He mentioned some of the hadith, and said: “Then he went down and prostrated, and his head was between his hands for a distance when he began the prayer.”"
"642","Musa bin Harun bin Abdullah Al-Bazzaz told us, Al-Harith bin Abdullah Al-Hamdani, known as Ibn Al-Khazen, told me, Hushaym told us, On the authority of Asim ibn Kulayb, on the authority of Alqamah ibn Wa’il, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “when he prostrated, he would intertwine his fingers.”"
"643","Issa bin Ibrahim Al-Ghafiqi Al-Misri told us, Ibn Wahb told us, on the authority of Al-Layth bin Saad, on the authority of Yazid bin Muhammad Al-Qurashi, and more Bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr bin Halhalah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr bin Ata, that he was sitting with a group of the Prophet’s companions May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. They mentioned the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Abu Humaid al-Sa’idi said: I used to remember the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, I saw him saying, “When he says takbeer, he places his hands on the shoes of his shoulders, and when he bows, he extends his hands from his knees, then shouts.” his back, and when he raises his head, he sits level, until every backbone returns to its place. And when he prostrates, he places his hands, neither spreading them nor clenching them, and facing with the tips of his fingers towards the Qiblah. Then, when he sits in the two rak’ahs, he sits on his left leg. If he sits in the last rak’ah, he puts his foot forward left, and sat on his seat.”"
"644","Muhammad bin Al-Ala bin Kurayb and Al-Ashjaj told us, they said: Abu Khaled told us. H, Harun bin Ishaq told us, Ibn Fudayl told us. H. Abdullah bin Al-Hakam bin Abi Ziyad Al-Qatwani, Ibn Numayr, told us. H. Salam bin Junada al-Qurashi told us, Waki` told us. H Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Jarir and Wakee’ narrated to us, all of them on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “When one of you prostrates, let him stand upright, and not spread his arms like the seven.”"
"645","Ubayd Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim told us: My uncle, my father, told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, Mas’ar bin Kadam al-Hilali told me, on the authority of Adam Ibn Ali Al-Bakri, on the authority of Ibn Umar, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not spread your arms like the seven feet, and support the your palms, and cover your toes, for if you do that, every part of you will prostrate.”"
"646","Ali bin Hajar told us, a partner told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: Al-Bara’ bin Aazib described prostration to us, “So he put his hands on the ground, and raised His old woman,” and he said: “This is what I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, doing.”"
"647","Ahmad ibn Sa`id al-Darimi, Ahmad ibn Mansour, and al-Yusri ibn Mazyd told us: Al-Nadr narrated to us, and he is ibn Shumayl, he informed us Yunus bin Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Baraa bin Aazib, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “when he prayed he would be humble.” He said: I heard Al-Yusri saying: Al-Nadr said: The one who does not stretch when bowing or prostrating. He said: I heard Ahmad bin Mansour Al-Marwazi saying: Al-Nadr said: And the Arabs say: It is Jakh."
"648","Muhammad and Saad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam, the two Egyptians, told us: My father told us, Bakr bin Mudar told us, on the authority of Ja’far, and he Ibn Rabi’ah, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Hurmuz, on the authority of Abdullah bin Malik bin Buhayna, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was “ When he prays, he spreads his hands so that his armpits are visible.”"
"649","Muhammad bin Yahya, Muhammad bin Rafi’, and Abd al-Rahman bin Bishr told us, they said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, Muammar told us, about Mansour, on the authority of Salem bin Abi Al-Jaad, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “when he prostrated, he would stand still until he could see \the whites of his armpits\"""""
"650","Yahya bin Habib Al-Harithi told us, Al-Mughirah told us, he said: This is what I read about Al-Fudayl, on the authority of Abu Hariz, and Abu Hariz told me Hariz, that Qais bin Abi Hazim narrated to him, that Adi bin Amira Al-Hadrami, narrated to him, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “when he prostrated, he would see The whites of his armpits.” Narrated by Muhammad bin Abd al-Ala al-San’ani, narrated by al-Mu’tamir, who said: I read from al-Fudayl, on the authority of Abu Hariz, something similar, and he said: “He sees white \His armpit\"""""
"651","Bundar told us, Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan told us dictation, Abd al-Hamid bin Jaafar told us, Muhammad bin Ata told me, on the authority of Abu Hamid Al-Sa’idi, he said: I heard it about ten of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, one of them was Abu Qatada bin Rabi’i, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “When he stands up to pray, he stands up straight,” and he mentioned some of the hadith, and said: “Then he descended to the ground, prostrating, then said: Allah is the Greatest, Then he pulled his upper arms away from his armpits, and opened his toes.”"
"652","Abu Zuhair Abd al-Majid bin Ibrahim al-Masry told us, Shuaib told us, meaning Ibn Yahya al-Tajibi, Yahya bin Ayyub told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr bin Halahla, narrated to him, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr bin Ata, that he was sitting with a group of people. Among the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, they mentioned the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Humaid al-Sa’idi said: I was protecting you. For the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I saw him, “When he says takbir, he makes his hands the shoes of his shoulders, and when he bows, he extends his hands from his knees, Then he arched his back, and when he raised his head, he stood until each part of him returned to its place. And when he prostrated, he placed his hands without spreading or spreading his head. He held them together and faced the qiblah with his toes.”"
"653","Saeed bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, my father told us, Al-Layth bin Saad told us, on the authority of Darraj Abi Al-Samh, on the authority of Ibn Hujayrah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When one of you prostrates, he should not spread his hands like a dog, and let him join \His thighs\"""""
"654","Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahim Al-Barqi and Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Kufi, who lived in Fustat, told us: Ibn Abi told us Maryam, Yahya bin Ayyub told us, Amara bin Ghaziyah told me, he said: I heard Abu Al-Nadr, saying: I heard Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, He says: Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, said: I lost the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was with me on my bed, and I found him prostrating with his heels crossed. Facing the Qiblah with the tips of his fingers, I heard him say: “I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your anger, in Your pardon from Your punishment, and in Your protection from You. I praise you but I do not convey everything that is in you.” So when he left, he said: “O Aisha, has your devil taken you?” She said: “Do you not have a devil?” He said: “There is no human being who does not have a devil.” So I said: And you, O Messenger of God? He said: “So do I, but I prayed to God for him and he became Muslim.”"
"655","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawrqi and Ali bin Shuaib told us, they said: Abu Usama told us, Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban. On the authority of Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I lost the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, one night in The bed, so I started to seek him with my hand, and my hand fell on the soles of his feet while they were upright, and I heard him say: “O God, I seek refuge in Your satisfaction from... I seek refuge in You from Your anger, and I seek refuge in You from Your punishment, and I seek refuge in You from You. I do not count Your praise, nor do I praise You, You are as You praised Yourself.”"
"656","Muhammad bin Abi Safwan Al-Thaqafi told us, Abdul Rahman, meaning Ibn Mahdi, told us, Ubayd Allah bin Iyad bin Laqit told us, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Al-Baraa bin Azib, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When you prostrate, put your palms down and raise your elbows.”"
"657","Saeed bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Makhzoumi and Omar bin Hafs Al-Shaybani told us, they said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, my nephew Yazid bin Al-Asam, on the authority of his uncle, on the authority of his paternal aunt, Maimunah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “when he prostrated, he would She wanted to pass under his hand, so she passed.” Omar Ibn Hafs said, he said: Ubayd Allah Ibn Abdullah Ibn Al-Asam told us, and he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “when he prostrated, he was dry.” His hands, even if an effort wanted to pass under them, it passed.”"
"658","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Mahdi, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salem, who is Ibn Abi al-Ja’d, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is not one of you except that his companion from the jinn has been appointed over him. And his companion is among the angels.” They said: And you, O Messenger of God? He said: “And me, but God helped me until I converted to Islam, so He does not command me to do anything but good.”"
"659","We are Bundar, we are Muhammad, meaning Ibn Jafar, Shu`bah told us. H. Salam bin Junada narrated to us, Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Single, he said: “The bowing of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his raising of his head after bowing, and his prostration and sitting between the two prostrations were close to \Alright\"""""
"660","Mu’mal bin Hisham Al-Yashkari and Salam bin Junada Al-Qurashi told us, they said: Abu Muawiyah told us, Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah. On the authority of Al-Mustawirad ibn Al-Ahnaf, on the authority of Silah, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: “I prayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, one night, and he mentioned The hadith, and he mentioned that he recited Al-Baqarah and Al-Nisa in the rak’ah, then he bowed, and his bowing was like his standing, then he prostrated, and his prostration was Like his bowing.”"
"661","Ubaidah bin Abdullah Al-Khuza’i told us, Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Utaiba, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abu Laila, on the authority of Al-Baraa bin Aazib, said: “The Prophet’s standing, bowing, prostration, and sitting were such that it was not known which “I prefer.” Abu Bakr said: He meant better: longer."
"662","It was narrated by Bundar, narrated by Yahya, and Abu Asim, who said: Abd al-Hamid bin Jaafar narrated to us, my father narrated to me, on the authority of Tamim bin Mahmoud, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Shibl. H. Salam bin Junada narrated to us, Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid bin Ja’far, with this chain of transmission. He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade And Salam bin Junada said about the crow’s peck. Salam bin Junada said: Concerning the obligatory duties, and they all said: And the sleeping of the beasts, and for the man to settle in the place, as he settles it. \The camel\"""""
"663","We are told by Abu Yahya Muhammad bin Abdul Rahim Al-Bazzaz, we are told by Al-Hakam bin Musa Abu Salih, Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, On the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Worse People are a thief who steals his prayers. They said: O Messenger of God, how could he steal his prayers? He said: “It does not complete its bowing or prostration.”"
"664","Muhammad bin Al-Ala bin Kurayb told us, Abu Khalid told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led us in the afternoon prayer, and he saw a man praying, and he said: “O so-and-so, fear God, pray well. Do you see that I do not see you? I see behind me as I see in front of me. Pray well and complete your bowing and prostration.”"
"665","Ismail bin Ishaq told us, Safwan bin Salih told us, Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, Shaybah bin Al-Ahnaf Al-Awza’i told us, Abu Salam Al-Aswad, narrated by Abu Salih Al-Ash’ari, on the authority of Abu Abdullah Al-Ash’ari, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led his Companions in prayer, Then he sat in a group of them, and a man entered, and he stood up to pray, and began to bow and tap in his prostration, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do you see this? Whoever dies in this state, dies in a religion other than that of Muhammad. He drips his prayers just as a crow drips blood. Rather, it is like one who kneels and drips in his prostration. Like a hungry person who only eats one date or two dates. What can you do with that? Perform ablution well. Woe to the heels of the Fire. Complete your bowing. And prostration.” Abu Salih said: So I said to Abu Abdullah Al-Ash’ari: Who told you this hadith? He said: The commanders of the soldiers: Amr ibn al-Aas, Khalid ibn al-Walid, Yazid ibn Abi Sufyan, and Shurahbil ibn Hasanah, all of them. They heard it from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"666","We are Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Ashjaj, we are Ibn Idris, and Muhammad bin Fudayl. H. Salam bin Junada told us, Waki’ told us. H. Harun bin Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us all, on the authority of Al-A’mash. H. Saeed bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Makhzoumi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash. H Al-Dawrqi told us, Abu Muawiyah, I Al-Amash, on the authority of Amara bin Umair, on the authority of Abu Muammar, on the authority of Abu Masoud, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “A prayer in which a man does not straighten his head in bowing and prostrating is not sufficient.”"
"667","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna and Ahmad bin Al-Miqdam told us, they said: Mulazim bin Amr told us, my grandfather Abdullah bin Badr told me, on the authority of Abdul Al-Rahman bin Ali, on the authority of his father, Ali bin Shayban, who was one of the delegation, said: I prayed behind the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he hinted at someone from behind He looked at a man who did not straighten his back while bowing and prostrating. When the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, finished the prayer, he said: “O community of Muslims, he does not A prayer for one who does not straighten his back when bowing and prostrating.” This is the hadith of Ahmad bin Al-Miqdam"
"668","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim, Muhammad bin Aban, and Salam bin Junada told us, they said: Hafs told us, and he is Ibn Ghayath, Ibn Abi told us. Layla, on the authority of Al-Shabi, on the authority of Silah, on the authority of Hudhayfah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say in his bowing: “Glory be to my Lord the Great” three times, and in His prostration: “Glory be to my Lord, the Most High” three times."
"669","Muammal bin Hisham and Salam bin Junada told us, they said: Abu Muawiyah told us, Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of the importer. Ibn Al-Ahnaf, on the authority of Silah Ibn Zufar, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: I prayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he mentioned the hadith and said: Then he prostrated, He said in his prostration: “Glory be to my Lord, the Most High.” Salam bin Junada said: On the authority of Al-A’mash"
"670","We are Abu Musa, we are Abdullah bin Zaid, we are Musa bin Ayoub, he said: I heard my uncle Iyas bin Amir, saying: I heard Uqba bin Amer, saying: When “Glorify the name of your Lord Most High” was revealed, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to us: “Put it in your prostration.” Muhammad ibn Isa, on the authority of Ibn al-Mubarak, on the authority of Musa ibn Ayyub, on the authority of his uncle, on the authority of Uqba ibn Amir, forbade him with something similar, and he did not say: \for us\"""""
"671","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim and Ali bin Shuaib told us, they said: Abu Usama told us, Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hayyan, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of Aisha, who said: I lost the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, one night in bed. So I started to ask for him with my hand, and my hand fell on the soles of his feet while they were upright, and I heard him say: “O God, I seek refuge in Your satisfaction from Your anger. I seek refuge in Your pardon from Your punishment, I seek refuge in You from You, I do not praise You, You are as You have praised Yourself.” This is the hadith of Al-Dawraqi, and Ali bin Shuaib said: On the authority of Ubayd Allah, and he said: “I cannot count your praise or praise.”"
"672","I am Yunus bin Abdul-Ala, I am Ibn Wahb, Yahya bin Ayyub narrated to me, on the authority of Amara bin Ghaziyah, on the authority of Sumayy, the client of Abu Bakr, On the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to say during his prostration: “O God, forgive me all my sins, fine.” His glory, His beginning and His end, His openness and His secret.”"
"673","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman and Bahr bin Nasr told us, they said: Ibn Wahb told us, Ibn Abi Al-Zannad told us, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Al-Fadl, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Araj, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Rafi’, on the authority of Ali, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was When he stood up to perform the obligatory prayer, he said takbeer, mentioned the hadith, and said: Then when he prostrated, he said in his prostration: “O God, to You I have prostrated, and in You I have believed, and to You I submitted to Islam, and you are my Lord. My face prostrated itself before the One who created it, and its hearing and sight were severed. Blessed be God, the Best of Creators.”"
"674","We are Ali bin Hajar, we are Ismail bin Jafar, and Sufyan bin Uyaynah. H. Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala’ and Sa’id bin Abdul-Rahman narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Sulayman bin Suhaim, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Ma’abad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, revealed the curtain while the people were in rows behind my father. Bakr, and he said: “As for prostration, strive hard in your supplication, for it will surely be answered.”"
"675","Yaqoub Al-Dawrqi and Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala narrated to us, they said: Bishr bin Mufaddal narrated to us, Ghaleb Al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of Bakr bin Abdullah, on the authority of Anas He said: “We used to pray with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the intense heat. If one of us wanted to prostrate, he would spread out his garment because of the intense heat.” Al-Hurr, and he prostrated over him.” Al-Sana’ani said: “If one of us is not able to raise his face from the ground, he spreads out his garment and prostrates over it.”"
"676","Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-San’ani told us, Sa’id bin Abi Maryam told us, Ibrahim bin Ismail bin Abi Habiba told us, Ibn Abd told me Al-Rahman bin Thabit bin Samit, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “prayed in the Mosque of Bani Abd al-Ashhal, And he has a cloak wrapped around him, and he places his hands. The cloak protects him from the cold of the pebbles.”"
"677","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, Abd al-Malik bin al-Sabbah al-Masma’i told us, Abd al-Hamid bin Ja’far al-Madani told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr ibn Ata’ said: I heard Abu Humaid al-Sa’idi among ten of the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: I teach you about prayer. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. They said: We were not the first to accompany him, nor did we take the longest to follow him. He said: Yes. They said: So turn away. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say, “When he stood up to pray, he would raise his hands until they were in line with his shoulders, then he would say “Allahu Akbar” and straighten up, standing, until everyone said “Allahu Akbar.” A bone in its upright position. Then he recites, then raises his hands, says “Allahu Akbar,” and kneels and places his palms on his knees, and does not tilt his head, nor He convinces him, then says: “God hears whoever praises Him,” and raises his hands until he aligns them with his shoulders and is balanced, until every bone stays in its place. upright, then he says “Allahu Akbar” and prostrates, facing his sides, then he raises his head, bends his left leg, and sits on it, opening his toes his right leg, then he gets up and does the same in the other rak’ah, then he gets up from the two prostrations and does the same as he did when he opened \prayer\"""""
"678","Abu Kurayb and Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Ashjaj told us, they said: I am Abu Khalid, Harun bin Ishaq told us, Ibn Fudayl told us. H. Salam bin Junada, narrated by Waki’, narrated to us on the authority of Sufyan, all of them, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, who said: I heard Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, saying: Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Omar told us, on the authority of his father, Abdullah bin Omar, who said: “It is part of the Sunnah in prayer to lie with your left leg. And the right position should be erected when you are sitting during prayer.” This is the hadith of Ibn Fudayl. The others said: On the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of his father"
"679","On the authority of Saeed bin Abdul Rahman Al Makhzoumi, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah Ibn Omar, on the authority of his father, said: “Part of the Sunnah of prayer is that you lie down with your left leg, and erect your right foot.” He said: And when the Prophet sat in prayer, he would lie down The left accusative and the right accusative.” Abu Bakr said: I do not consider this addition in the report of Ibn Uyaynah to be preserved. I mean his saying: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was When he sits in prayer, he lays the left side down and places the right side upright."
"680","We told Muhammad bin Yahya, we told Abdul Razzaq, Ibn Jurayj told us, Abu Al-Zubair told me, he heard Tawus, saying: We told Ibn Abbas said about sitting on the feet, and he said: “It is the Sunnah.” So we said: We see it as an arrogance toward the man. He said: Rather, it is the Sunnah of your Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"681","Ahmad bin Al-Azhar narrated to us, and I wrote it from its origin, I was Ya’qub bin Ibrahim bin Saad, narrated by my father, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: He narrated to me on the authority of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in his prayer, when Abbas bin Sahl bin Saad bin Malik bin Sa’id prostrated, he said: I sat in the market of Medina. In the afternoon with Abu Usayd Malik bin Rabi’ah, and with Abu Humayd, the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they were from his group from the Banu Sa`idah, and with Abu Qatada was Al-Harith bin Rabi’i, and they said to each other while I was listening: I know about the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. The two of you greeted each other saying it to his friend, so they said to one of them: “Then stand and lead us so that we may see whether the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is carried out or not.” No?” Then one of them got up and faced the Qiblah, then he said “Allahu Akbar,” then he read some of the Qur’an, then he bowed down and placed his hands on his knees until everyone was at ease. A bone of it, then he raised his head and straightened until every bone of his body returned, then he said: “God hears whoever praises Him,” then he fell, prostrating on his forehead. And his palms, his knees, and the tops of his feet, walking with his hands until I saw the whites of his armpits and what was under his shoulders, then he remained firm until every bone was secure. Then he raised his head and leaned on his heels and the tops of his feet, until every bone returned to its place. Then he went back to the same way. He said: Then he got up and bowed another like it. He said: Then he saluted. So he went to his two companions and said to them: How did you see? They said to him: The prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was correct. This is how he used to pray."
"682","Ahmad bin Abdah told us, Hammad bin Zaid told us, Thabit Al-Bunani told us, he said: Anas bin Malik told us: I do not hesitate to pray. With you, just as I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying with us. Thabit said: Anas was doing something that I did not see you doing. “When he raised After prostrating, his head remained between the two prostrations, until he said: He who said: He forgot.”"
"683","From Muhammad bin Bashar, from Abu Ahmad, meaning Al-Zubayri, from Mas’ar, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Single, he said: “The prostration of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his bowing, and his sitting between the two prostrations, were close to the same.”"
"684","On the authority of Salam ibn Junada, on the authority of Hafs ibn Ghayath, on the authority of Al-Alaa ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, on the authority of Talha ibn Yazid, on the authority of Hudhayfah, And Al-Amash, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Al-Mustarid bin Al-Ahnaf, on the authority of Silah bin Zufar, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, rose May God bless him and grant him peace, he had been praying at night, so I came and stood beside him, and he opened the cow, and I said: He wants the hundred, so he passed it, and I said: He wants The two hundred, so he passed it, and I said: He should conclude, so he concluded, then he opened an-Nisa’, so he recited it, then he recited Al Imran, then he kneeled close to what he recited, then He rose and said: “God hears whoever praises Him. Our Lord, praise be to You,” close to what he bowed down, then he prostrated in a manner similar to what he raised, then he rose and said: “Lord, forgive me.” In a way that he prostrated, then he prostrated in a way that he raised, then he stood up the second time.” Al-A’mash said: He would not pass by any sign of intimidation unless he sought refuge or sought protection. There is not a sign of mercy except that he asks, and there is not a sign that means exaltation but that he glorifies it."
"685","On the authority of Bundar, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid bin Jaafar, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ata, on the authority of Abu Humaid al-Sa’idi, he said: I heard him in Ten of the companions of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, one of them was Abu Qatada. He said: When the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “stood up to pray, he would stand upright.” He stood up, mentioned some of the hadith, and said: Then he descended to the ground, prostrating, then said: “Allahu Akbar,” then he distanced his upper arms from his armpits, and opened His toes, then he bent his left leg, sat on it, and straightened up until every bone in it returned to its place, then he fell prostrating, He said: “Allahu Akbar,” then he bent his leg and sat and straightened, until every bone returned to its place, then he got up."
"686","Ali bin Hajar narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid Al-Hadha’, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Malik bin Al-Huwayrith, that he saw the Prophet praying May God bless him and grant him peace: “He prays, but if he is in the Witr prayer of his prayer, he does not get up until he is completely seated.”"
"687","Muhammad bin Bashar and Abu Musa told us, they said: Abdul Wahhab told us, Khaled told us, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, he said: Malik bin Al-Huwayrith was What is between us, so he says: Shall I not tell you about the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace?” So he prayed at a time other than the time for prayer, so when he raised his head from the prostration The second: In the first rak’ah, he stood upright sitting, then stood up and leaned on the ground.” Abu Bakr said: Ayyub’s information on the authority of Abu Qilaba, which I narrated in the book of Al-Kabir."
"688","Ahmad bin Abdul Rahman bin Wahb told us, my uncle told us, Haywa told us, Khaled bin Yazid told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Hilal, On the authority of Naeem Al-Mujmar, he said: I prayed behind Abu Hurairah, and he said: “In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, Surah Al-Fatihah, verse 1.” Then he recited the Mother of the Qur’an, until he reached Nor those who go astray. Surah Al-Fatihah, verse 7. Then he said: Amen. Then the people said: Amen. Then when he bowed, he said: God is the Greatest. Then when he raised his head, he said: God hears those who praise Him. Then He said: Allah is the greatest, then he prostrated, and when he rose, he said: Allah is the greatest, and when he prostrated, he said: Allah is the greatest, then he stood up and said the takbeer, so when he rose Of the two, he said: “Allah is the greatest.” Then when he greeted him, he said: “By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I resemble you in prayer with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"689","We were told by Bundar, and Muhammad bin Rafi’, and this is the hadith of Bundar, Abu Amir told us, I am Fulayh bin Suleiman Al-Madani, Abbas bin told me Sahl al-Saadi, he said: Abu Humaid al-Saadi, Abu Usayd al-Saadi, Sahl bin Saad, and Muhammad bin Maslamah gathered, and Abu Humaid said: I inform you of the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He mentioned the hadith in its length, and said: “He sat, spread out his left leg, and approached the chest of He placed his right hand on his qiblah, and placed his right hand on his right knee and his left hand on his left knee, and pointed with his finger. \index finger\"""""
"690","On the authority of Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Ibn Idris, on the authority of Asim ibn Kulayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Wa’il ibn Hajar, he said: I came to Medina, So I said: Let us look at the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He mentioned the hadith and said: “He bent his left leg and put his right leg upright.”"
"691","Al-Makhzoumi narrated it. Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Wael bin Hajar, who said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. “When he sat in prayer, he spread his left leg and placed his right leg,” he said."
"692","Muhammad bin Sahl bin Askar and Al-Hussein bin Mahdi told us, they said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, Muammar told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah. On the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade, when a man sits during prayer, that he should rely on his left hand.” Al-Hussein bin Mahdi said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade a man to rely on his hands during prayer.”"
"693","Al-Sana'ani, I am Al-Mu'tamir, told us: I heard Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said, “He would raise his hands when he entered into prayer, and when he wanted to bow, and when he raised his head from bowing, and when he stood up from the two rak’ahs. He raises his hands in all of this, at the level of his shoulders.”"
"694","We are Abu Zuhayr Abd al-Majid bin Ibrahim al-Masry, we are Shuaib, meaning Ibn Yahya al-Tajibi, Yahya bin Ayyub told us, about Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, that he heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of God was May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “When he begins the prayer, he says ‘Allahu Akbar’, then places his hands equal to his shoulders, and when he bows, he does the same, and when he prostrates, he does the same.” That, and he does not do it when he raises his head from prostration, and when he gets up from the two rak’ahs he does the same.”"
"695","It was narrated by Othman bin Al-Hakam Al-Jadhami, who said: I am Ibn Jurayj, and that Ibn Shihab told him this chain of transmission like him, and he said: “He said greatness and raised “His hands are as high as his shoulders.” It was narrated to me by Abu Al-Yaman Yasin bin Abi Zurarah Al-Masri Al-Qabbani, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Hakam Al-Jadhami. Abu Bakr said: I heard Yunus saying: The first to come to Egypt, with the knowledge of Ibn Jurayj, or with the knowledge of Malik, was Uthman ibn al-Hakam al-Jadami. Abu Bakr said: I heard Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahim Al-Barqi saying: Ibn Abi Maryam told us, Othman bin Al-Hakam al-Jami’ah, and it was one of the people’s favorites."
"696","Yusuf bin Musa Al-Qattan told us, Al-Alaa bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad told us, Othman bin Hakim told us, Amer bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubair told me, on the authority of his father, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “when he sat during prayer, he would place his foot He placed his left hand between his thigh and his leg, and he placed his left hand on his left knee, and he placed his right hand on his right thigh, and pointed With his finger.” Abdul Wahid pointed with his index finger"
"697","On the authority of Bundar, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Jaafar, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Asim ibn Kulayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Wa’il ibn Hajar, he said: “I prayed with the Prophet, he prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. So he said “Allahu Akbar” when he entered into the prayer and raised his hands, and when he wanted to bow, he raised his hands, and when he raised his head from bowing, he raised his hands and placed He raised his palms together, meaning in prostration, and spread out his left thigh, and pointed with his index finger, meaning when sitting in tashahhud.” Abu Bakr said: His saying: And he spread his left thigh, means to the right one. Abu Bakr spread his left thigh, to place his right thigh on the left. Like the story of Adam ibn Abi Iyas: He placed his right thigh on the left."
"698","On the authority of Muhammad ibn Yahya, on the authority of Wahb ibn Jarir, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Asim ibn Kulayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Wa’il ibn Hajr al-Hadrami, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “raised his hands when he said the greatest, and when he bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing, and he said when he prostrated: Thus, and he crossed his hands.” From his armpits, and placed his right thigh on his left thigh, and said: Thus, and he placed Wahb with his index finger and crossed it with the middle one. Muhammad bin Yahya also pointed with his index finger and circled it with the middle and thumb, and knotted it with the middle one. Abu Bakr said: His saying: He placed his right thigh on his left thigh meant in the tashahhud."
"699","Ahmad bin Abdah told us, Yazid bin Zurayi told us, Husayn Al-Mu’allim told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Maysarah, on the authority of Abu Al-Jawza’, On the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “would say the greeting during the two rak’ahs, and he would spread his left foot under his right.”"
"700","We were told by Bundar, we were told by Yahya bin Saeed, we were told by Abd al-Hamid bin Jaafar, we were told by Muhammad bin Ata, on the authority of Abu Hamid al-Sa’idi, he said: I heard it about ten of the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. One of them was Abu Qatada. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was It was the rak’ah in which the prayer ended. He put his left leg behind him, sat on his side, bowing, then said the salaam.” According to the report of Abu Asim: He lowered his left leg and sat on his left side, hunched over. And in the news of Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Halhalah, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata’: If he sat on the fourth day, he would put his legs behind him and sit on his hip. This is in the narration of Yahya bin Ayyub, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, and Al-Layth said in his narration: On the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ibn Abi Hilal, on the authority of Yazid. Ibn Abi Habib, and Yazid Ibn Muhammad: When he sits in the last rak’ah, he puts his left leg forward and places the other, and sits on his seat. Abu Bakr said: I mentioned these reports in a section other than this."
"701","On the authority of Ibrahim bin Saad Al-Jawhari, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Ibrahim bin Saad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Al-Aswad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to “sit on his left hip at the end of his prayer.”"
"702","Al-Quta’i Muhammad bin Yahya narrates, Abdul-Ala narrates, Muhammad bin Ishaq narrates, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of his father, I am Abdullah Ibn Masoud, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught him the Tashahhud in prayer. He said: We used to memorize it, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Masoud, as We memorize the letters of the Qur’an, the waw and the alif, so when he sits on his left hip, he says: “Greetings are to Allah, and the prayers and the good deeds. Peace be upon you, O The Prophet, God’s mercy and blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God. I bear witness that there is no god but God and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. Then he supplicates for himself, then greets and departs.”"
"703","Bundar told us, and Yahya bin Hakim told us: Yahya told us, Al-Amash told us, Shaqiq told us, Abdullah told us. H Muhammad bin Al-Ala bin Kurayb, Abu Usama, told us. H and Harun bin Ishaq, Ibn Fudayl told us. H. Salam bin Junada, Waki’, and Ibn Idris narrated to us, all of them on the authority of Al-A’mash. H, Abu Musa told us, Abu Muawiyah told us. H Abu Husayn bin Ahmad bin Yunus narrated to us, Abtar narrated to us, Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: We were When we sat with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the tashahhud, we said: Peace be upon God from His servants, peace be upon so-and-so and so-and-so, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “Do not say peace be upon God, for God is peace, but when one of you sits, let him say: Greetings and prayers are to God.” And the good things, and peace be upon you, O Prophet, and God’s mercy and blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God. If you say that It has befallen every righteous servant in heaven and earth. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. Then let one of you choose. Of the supplication he likes, let him pray with it.” This is the wording of the hadith of Bundar, and the hadith of Ibn Fudayl, Abtar, and Ibn Idris ended when he said: And his messenger, and they did not say: Then Let each one of you have the choice of one supplication to the end of it."
"704","Abu Husayn told us, Abthar told us, Husayn told us. Salam bin Junada told us, Ibn Idris told us, Husayn told us. H Yusuf bin Musa told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour. H Yusuf bin Musa narrated to us, Jarir also narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Mughirah, all of them on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. In the tashahhud, and the hadith of Al-A’mash, he gave his statement: And his Messenger, and he added in the hadith of Mansour: Then he can make whatever choice he wants in the matter."
"705","Al-Rabi’ bin Salman narrated to us, Shuaib narrated to us, meaning Ibn Al-Layth, Al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, and Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to teach us the Tashahhud just as he taught us the Qur’an, and he used to say: “Blessed greetings The good prayers are for God. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and God’s mercy and blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God. I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God.”"
"706","On the authority of Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Yunus bin Bukayr, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: “It is Sunnah to conceal the tashahhud.”"
"707","Narrated by Salam bin Junada, on the authority of Hafs, meaning Ibn Ghayath, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “This was revealed The verse in the Tashahhud: “And do not say your prayer loudly, nor be silent therein.” Surah Al-Isra, verse 110."
"708","Ahmad bin Al-Azhar narrated to us, and I wrote it down from its origin. My father narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: He narrated to me about the Messenger of God bearing witness in the midst of The prayer and at the end of it, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad ibn Yazid al-Nakha’i, on the authority of his father, who said: And we used to memorize it, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Masoud, Just as we memorize the letters of the Qur’an when we were told that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught them to him. He said: He used to say when he sat in the middle of prayer: And at the end of it on his left hip: “Greetings are to God and prayers and good things. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and God’s mercy and blessings. Peace be upon us.” And upon the righteous servants of God, I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger.” He said: Then, if he was in the middle of the prayer, he got up when He finishes his tashahhud, and if at the end of it he supplicates after reciting the tashahhud, whatever God wills, he should supplicate, then he says the salutation. Abu Bakr said: His saying: And at the end of it on his left hip, he used to sit it at the end of his prayer, not in the middle of his prayer, and at the end of it as It was narrated by Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, and Ibrahim bin Saeed Al-Jawhari, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Ibrahim"
"709","Ahmad bin Abdul Rahman bin Wahb Al-Qurashi told us, my uncle told us, Abu Hani told me, that Abu Ali Al-Janabi told him, that He heard Fadalah bin Ubaid say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard a man calling in prayer. He did not thank God and did not send blessings upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “You hasten, O praying person.” Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, taught them, and he heard a man He sends blessings upon the Prophet, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O one who prays, call and you will be answered, ask and it will be given to you.”"
"710","On the authority of Bakr ibn Idris ibn al-Hajjaj ibn Harun al-Muqri, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman al-Muqri, on the authority of Abu Hani, on the authority of Abu Ali Amr Ibn Malik al-Janabi, on the authority of Fadalah Ibn Ubaid al-Ansari, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw a man praying who did not thank God and did not He glorified him, but he did not pray for the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he left. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “This hastened.” So he called him and said to him. And for others: “When one of you prays, let him begin by glorifying his Lord and praising Him, and send blessings upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and then supplicate with whatever he wishes.”"
"711","Abu Al-Azhar narrated it, and I wrote it from its original, narrated by Ya’qub, narrated by my father, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: He spoke to me about praying for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him. When a Muslim person prayed for him in his prayers, Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Zayd bin Abdul Rabbo, On the authority of Abu Masoud Uqba bin Amr, he said: A man came and sat in front of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while we were with him, and he said: Oh Messenger of God, as for peace, we have known it, so how can we pray for you if we prayed in our prayers, may God’s prayers be upon you? He said: He remained silent until we liked that the man did not ask him. Then he said: “If you pray for me, say: O God, bless Muhammad, the unlettered Prophet. And upon the family of Muhammad, as You sent blessings upon Abraham and upon the family of Abraham, and bless Muhammad the unlettered Prophet, and upon the family of Muhammad, as You bestowed blessing upon Abraham and upon his family. Abraham, you are Praiseworthy and Glorious.”"
"712","We are Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala, we are Sufyan, Yahya bin Saeed told me, on the authority of Muslim, then I met Muslim, so Muslim bin Abi told me Maryam, Ali bin Abd al-Rahman al-Mu’awi told me, he said: I prayed the noon prayer alongside Ibn Umar. H Abu Musa, Yahya bin Hakim, and Saeed bin Abdul Rahman Al Makhzoumi told us, they said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Muslim bin Abi Maryam, on the authority of Ali bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Mu’awi, and Yahya bin Hakim said: I heard Ali bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Ansari say: I prayed Next to Ibn Umar, I turned over the pebbles, and he said: Do not turn over the pebbles, but do as I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, doing. I said: How did you see him doing? He said: Thus, “he put his left hand on his left thigh, and his right hand on his right thigh, and raised his index finger.” This is the hadith of Yahya bin Hakim, and Yahya also added: He said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed narrated this hadith to us. On the authority of Muslim bin Abi Maryam, I met Muslim and asked him, so he told me about it. Al-Makhzoumi said in his hadith: So he placed his right hand on His right thigh, and he held two fingers, and circled the middle, and pointed with the one next to the thumb, and placed his left hand on his left thigh."
"713","This is Harun bin Ishaq, this is Ibn Fudayl. Al-Ashjaj, Ibn Idris, narrated to us. H Ali bin Khashram told us, Abdullah, meaning Ibn Idris, told us. H Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala’ and Sa’id bin Abdul-Rahman narrated to us, saying: All of them narrated to us, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Wael bin Hajar, and this is the wording of the hadith of Ibn Fudayl. He said: I was among those who came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I said: Let us look at the prayer. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, how does he pray? “When he sat down, he spread his left leg, then placed his left hand on his left thigh, then placed the edge of his right elbow on his right thigh, Then he tied the knot, meaning two seconds, then he flew, and made a sign of the rosary, making supplication.” Ibn Khashram said: He circled the middle and the thumb and raised the place between them to pray with it, meaning the rosary."
"714","Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Muawiyah bin Amr told us, Zaida told us, Asim bin Kulayb Al-Jarmi told us, my father told me that Wael bin Hajar He told him, he said: I said: Let us look at the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. How does he pray? He said: So I looked at him praying, so he said “Allahu Akbar” and mentioned some of the hadith, and said: “Then he sat, spread out his left leg, and placed his left palm on His left thigh and knee, and he placed the edge of his right elbow on his right thigh, then he closed two of his fingers and circled, then raised his finger, and I saw him move it and say supplication with it.” Abu Bakr said: There is nothing in the news that is “moved” except in this news plus the mention of it."
"715","Harun bin Ishaq told us, Ibn Bahz told us, on the authority of Issam bin Qudamah, on the authority of Malik Al-Khuza’i, on the authority of his father, he said: I saw the Prophet praying May God bless him and grant him peace in prayer, “putting his right hand on his right thigh, and pointing with his finger.” Muhammad bin Rafi’ narrated it. Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Issam, and he mentioned the hadith."
"716","We are Abd al-A'la bin Wasil bin Abd al-A'la, we are Al-Fadl, we are Issam bin Qudamah al-Jadli, Malik bin Numayr al-Khuza'i told me from The people of Basra said that his father told him that he saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “sitting in prayer, placing his right arm on So his right thigh, raising his index finger, bent it slightly, while he was supplicating.”"
"717","Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, Muammar told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace “When he sat in prayer, he would place his hands on his knees, and raise his right finger that is next to the thumb, and he would supplicate with it, and his left hand would On his knee, spreading it out on him.”"
"718","It is narrated by Bundar, it is narrated by Yahya bin Saeed, it is narrated by Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Amir bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He said: “When he testified, he placed his left hand on his left thigh, and placed his right hand on his right thigh, and pointed with his finger.” index finger, his gaze should not go beyond his point.”"
"719","On the authority of Ali ibn Hajar, on the authority of Ismail, meaning Ibn Jafar, on the authority of Muslim ibn Abi Maryam, on the authority of Ali ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Muawiyah, on the authority of Abd Allah ibn Umar said that he saw a man moving a pebble with his hand while he was praying. When he left, Abdullah said to him: “Do not move the pebble while you are praying. For that is from Satan, but do as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to do. He said: Then he placed his right hand on his thigh. He pointed with his finger next to the thumb to the Qiblah, and looked at it or towards it, then he said: This is how I saw the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him.”"
"720","On the authority of Bundar, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Jaafar, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: I heard Abu Al-Ahwas, speaking, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Masoud said: Indeed, we did not know what to say in every two rak’ahs, except to glorify God, glorify God, and praise our Lord, and that Muhammad taught the conquests. Goodness and its components, so he said: “When you sit in every two rak’ahs, say: Greetings are to God and good prayers. May peace and mercy be upon you, O Prophet. God and His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God. I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, then “If one of you chooses a supplication that he likes, let him pray with it.”"
"721","Ali bin Khashram told us, Isa told us, meaning Ibn Yunus. H Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Ahmasi informed us, Waki’ informed us. H, Harun bin Ishaq, Mukhlid bin Yazid Al-Harrani, narrated to us all, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Hassan bin Atiya, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abu Aisha, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When one of you bears witness, let him seek refuge with God from four, He says: O God, I seek refuge in You from the torment of Hell, from the torment of the grave, from the evil of the temptation of the Antichrist, and from the evil of the temptation of life. And deaths.” This is a comprehensive hadith. And in the hadith of Jesus: I heard Abu Hurairah. On the authority of Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Ahmasi, on the authority of Waki’, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, similarly"
"722","We are Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Zaafrani, we are a soul, we are Ibn Jurayj, Ibn Tawus told me, on the authority of his father, that he used to say after the tashahhud Words that he used to esteem very highly: Did you say both of them in the double? He said: Rather, in the last double after the tashahhud, I said: What is it? He said: “I seek refuge in God from the torment of the grave, and I seek refuge in God from the torment of Hell, and I seek refuge in God from the evil of the Antichrist, and I seek refuge in In God from the torment of the grave, and I seek refuge in God from the temptation of life and death. He said: He used to venerate them.” Ibn Jurayj said: He told me, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"723","On the authority of Bahr ibn Nasr, on the authority of Yahya, meaning ibn Hassan, on the authority of Yusuf ibn Yaqoub al-Majishun, on the authority of his father, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Ubayy Rafi’, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was one of the last things he would say between the tashahhud and the salutation: “O God, forgive me for what I have done.” I have presented and what I have delayed, and I have not concealed and what I have declared, and I have not been extravagant and you have no knowledge of it than me. You are the one who brings forward and you are the one who delays. There is no god but \You\"""""
"724","Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Husayn al-Mu’allim narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, Hanzalah bin Ali narrated to me, that Muhjan bin Al-Adra’ told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered the mosque and saw a man who had completed his prayer while he was He bears witness and says: O God, I ask you by God, the One and Eternal, who neither begot nor was born, and to whom there is no one equal, to forgive me. My sins, indeed, You are the Forgiving, the Merciful. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “They have been forgiven, they have been forgiven,” three times."
"725","On the authority of Yusuf bin Musa, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to a man: What do you say in prayer?” He said: “Shall I recite the tashahhud?” Then I say: “O God, I ask you for Paradise and I seek refuge in You from Hell.” By God, how good your crooning is. Nor did Muadh sing, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “We will hum around them.” Abu Bakr said: humming words that are not understood."
"726","On the authority of Bundar, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Jafar al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ismail bin Muhammad, on the authority of Amer bin Saad, on the authority of His father, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to “sallam on his right until the white of his cheek could be seen, and on his left until the white of his cheek could be seen.”"
"727","Utba bin Abdullah Al-Hammadi told us, Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, Musab bin Thabit told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Muhammad On the authority of Amer bin Saad bin Abi Waqqas, on the authority of his father, he said: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “saluting to his right and to his left until he could be seen.” \The whiteness of his cheek.\"" Al-Zuhri said: We did not hear this from the hadith of the Messenger of God"
"728","We are Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Habib bin Al-Shahid, and Ziyad bin Ayyub. Ishaq said: Omar told us, and Ziyad said: Omar bin Ubaid told me. Al-Tanafisi, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to salute on his right Until the white of his cheek is visible, may God’s peace, mercy, and blessings be upon you, and to his left until the white of his cheek is visible, may God’s peace, mercy, and blessings be upon you. And His blessings.”"
"729","Muhammad bin Yahya, Muhammad bin Khalaf al-Asqalani, and Muhammad bin Mahdi al-Attar told us, they said: Amr bin Abi Salama told us, on the authority of Zuhair Ibn Muhammad al-Makki, on the authority of Hisham Ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to “salut a salutation during prayer.” One side facing his face, leaning slightly toward the right side.” Ibn Mahdi said: He said: I am Zuhayr bin Muhammad Al-Makki"
"730","Narrated to us Muhammad bin Yahya, narrated to us by Mu’alla bin Asad Al-Ammi, narrated to us by Wahib, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with him. About her saying that she used to “salom one greeting in front of her face, peace be upon you.”"
"731","Narrated by Muhammad, narrated by Mu’alla, narrated by Wahib, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, that he used to “salutate one time: Peace be upon you.”"
"732","Na Na Bundar, Na Yahya, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Al-Qasim, he said: I saw Aisha: “Salamizing one person.” Na Bundar, Na Abdul Wahhab, Na Ubaid Allah, Na Ubaid Allah, with this like it, and added: And it does not turn to its right or to its left."
"733","Bundar and Al-Hasan bin Muhammad told us, they said: Yazid bin Harun told us, he said: Mas’ar told us. H and us Ali bin Khashram, Issa, meaning Ibn Yunus, told us on the authority of Mis’ar bin Kadam. H Al-Hasan bin Muhammad also narrated to us, Muhammad bin Ubaid Al-Tanafisi narrated to us, Mas’ar narrated to us. H Salam bin Junada narrated to us, Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Al-Qibtiyya, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra, who said: We were When we prayed behind the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, we said with our hands, “Peace be upon you,” right and left. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “What do I see? Your hands are like the tails of sun-kissed horses, so let each one of you remain still in prayer.” This is the hadith of Bundar, and others said: “Is it not enough for one of you to place his hand on his thigh and then salute, to his right and to his left?” However, Ibn Khashram said in his hadith: Then he should greet those on his right and those on his left, and in the hadith of Waki’: It is upon his brother who is on his right and who is on his side. To its north, Al-Hasan bin Muhammad said in the hadith of Yazid: When we prayed behind the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, we would say: Peace be upon God, peace be upon Gabriel, peace be upon Mikael, and Abu Khaled, meaning Yazid bin Harun, pointed with his hand and threw it right and left. Al-Hasan bin Muhammad said: Then he mentioned something similar to it, meaning something similar to the hadith of Muhammad bin Ubaid."
"734","Amr bin Ali Al-Sayrifi narrated to us, Muhammad bin Yusuf Al-Faryabi narrated to us, Al-Awza’i narrated to us, on the authority of Qurra bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Deleting the greeting is a sunnah.”"
"735","We told him, Ali bin Sahl al-Ramli told us, Amara bin Bishr al-Masisi told us, on the authority of al-Awza’i with this chain of transmission, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: “Deleting the greeting is a sunnah.” Abu Bakr said: It was narrated by Issa bin Yunus, Ibn Al-Mubarak, and Muhammad bin Yahya, on the authority of Al-Faryabi. They all said, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: Deleting the greeting is Sunnah.” Abu Ammar told us, Issa bin Yunus told us. H And Muhammad bin Abi Safwan Al-Thaqafi told us, Abd al-Rahman told us. H Yahya bin Hakim told us, Harami bin Amara told us, they said: Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak H, and Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Muhammad bin. Yusuf, all of them on the authority of Al-Awza’i"
"736","Narrated by Yaqoub Al-Durqi, narrated by Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Asim Al-Ahwal, on the authority of Awsaja bin Al-Rammah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Hudhayl, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say the salaam during prayer, he would not sit for more than an amount of time, saying: “Oh God, you Peace, and peace from you. Blessed are you, O Possessor of majesty and honor.”"
"737","Muhammad bin Miskin Al-Yamimi and Al-Hasan bin Isra’il Al-Lu’ali Al-Ramli told us, they said: Bishr bin Bakr narrated to us, Al-Lu’ali said: He told me, and Al-Yamami told me, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, he said: Abu Ammar told me, Abu Asma Al-Rahbi told me, Thawban told me A servant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wanted to finish his prayer, he would ask forgiveness three times. Several times, then he said: “O God, You are peace, and from You is peace. Blessed are You, O Possessor of majesty and honor.” Ahmad bin Yazid bin Alil Al-Anizi Al-Misri narrated to us, they said: Amr bin Abi Salamah narrated to me, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, with this chain of narration and something like it. Whether. Amr bin Hisham Al-Beiruti narrated, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, and he said: He mentioned this supplication before the greeting of peace."
"738","Narrated by Muhammad bin Maymun Al-Makki, narrated by Amr bin Hashim Al-Biruti, Al-Awza’i narrated to me, Abu Ammar narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Asma’ Al-Rahbi, On the authority of Thawban, the servant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wanted to say salaam from prayer, he would ask forgiveness Three times, then he said: “O God, You are peace, and from You is peace. Blessed are You, O Possessor of majesty and honor.” Then he greeted. Abu Bakr said: Even if Amr bin Hashim, or Muhammad bin Maymun, did not make a mistake in this wording, I mean his saying: before greeting, This section refers to the supplication before the greeting of peace."
"739","Muhammad bin Yahya told us, I am Abu Al-Numan, I am Thabit bin Yazid Abu Zaid Al-Ahwal, Hilal bin Khabbab told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: You recited the Qunoot of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, for a successive month in the noon, afternoon, sunset, evening, and morning prayers in the afternoon. Every prayer, when he said:"
"740","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi told us, Ismail bin Aliya told me, Al-Hajjaj bin Abi Uthman told me, Abu Al-Zubayr told us, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, delivering a sermon on this pulpit, and he says: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said the salaam at the end of prayer, he would say: There is no god but God, we worship none but Him, the people of grace, favour, and good praise. There is no god but God, sincere in religion to Him, even if the disbelievers hate it.”"
"741","We are Muhammad bin Khalaf Al-Asqalani, we are Adam, meaning Ibn Abi Iyas, we are Abu Omar Al-San’ani, who is Hafs bin Maysarah, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, On the authority of Abu al-Zubayr al-Makki, on the authority of Abdullah bin al-Zubayr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say when his prayer ended before To establish: “There is no god but God alone, with no partner, to Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise, and He is capable of all things. There is no power but in God, and we worship none but To Him belongs grace, favor, and good praise. There is no god but Allah, sincere in religion to Him, even if the disbelievers hate it.”"
"742","It is narrated by Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Zuhri, narrated by Sufyan, who said: I heard it from Abdah, meaning Ibn Abi Lubana, I heard it from Warad Kateb. Al-Mughira, he said: Muawiyah wrote to Al-Mughira: Tell me something you heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was May God bless him and grant him peace when he completes the prayer. H Al-Hasan bin Muhammad narrated to us, Asbat bin Muhammad narrated to us, Abd al-Malik bin Umair narrated to us. H Abu Musa and Yahya bin Hakim narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman, narrated to us Sufyan, narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik. H. Ziyad bin Ayyub told us, Hushaym told us, Abd al-Malik told us, he said: I heard Ward, speaking, and in the hadith of Asbat And Sufyan, on the authority of Warad, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say at the end of the prayer: “There is no god but God He alone has no partner, to Him belongs the dominion, and to Him is praise, and He is capable of all things. O God, there is no hinderer of what You have given, no giver of what You have withheld, and none is of benefit. Very serious about you.” In the hadith of Abd al-Rahman, he said: Al-Mughirah ibn Shu’bah dictated to me, and I wrote to Muawiyah that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had He says at the end of every obligatory prayer. As for Abu Hashim, he told us, with the hadith of Hushaym, following the news of Mughirah and Mujahid, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, On the authority of Warad: Muawiyah wrote to Al-Mughirah: Write to me about something I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: So he wrote to him. Al-Mughirah: I heard him say when he finished praying: “There is no god but God alone, He has no partner. To Him belongs the dominion, and to Him is praise, and He is over everything.” “Qadir” three times, he said: “And it was” He forbids gossip, asking too many questions, wasting money, withholding insults, being disobedient to mothers, and infanticide. “Girls.” Al-Dawrqi and Abu Hisham told us this news. They said: Hushaym told us. More than one of them told us: Al-Mugheerah, Mujalid, and a man. A third also, all of them on the authority of Al-Shaabi. Then Abu Hashim told us following this news, Hushaym told us, Abd al-Malik bin Umair told us, he said: I heard a ward, speaking This hadith is on the authority of Al-Mughirah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"743","Muhammad bin Yahya narrated, Hajjaj bin Minhal narrated, and Abu Salih Kateb, all on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Abdullah bin Abi Salamah, on the authority of His uncle Al-Majishun bin Abi Salamah, on the authority of Al-Araj, who is Abdul-Rahman bin Hurmuz, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Rafi’, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that when he finished his prayer and said the salaam, he would say: “O God, forgive me for what I have done and what I have delayed. “And I have not concealed nor declared, nor have I been extravagant, nor have You been more knowledgeable of it than I. You are the one who brings forward and the one who comes back. There is no god but You.” Abu Saleh said: I have no god but You."
"744","We are Muhammad bin Abbad bin Adam Al-Basri, I am Marwan bin Muawiyah Al-Fazari, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of his father, he said: We used to go out in the morning To the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the man comes and the woman comes, and he says: O Messenger of God, what should I say when I pray? He said: “Say: O God, forgive me, have mercy on me, guide me, protect me, and provide for me, for He has combined your world and the hereafter for you.”"
"745","Yunus bin Abd al-Ala al-Sadafi told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Hafs bin Maysarah told me, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Ata bin Abu Marwan, on the authority of his father, that Ka’b swore to him by the one who parted the sea to Moses. We find in the Torah that when David, the Prophet of God, departed from During his prayer, he said: “O God, set right for me my religion which You have made for me a protection, and set right for me my world in which You have made my livelihood. Oh God, I seek refuge in Your satisfaction from Your anger, and I seek refuge in Your forgiveness from Your vengeance, and I seek refuge in You from You. O God, there is no one who prevents what You have given, and there is no giver of what You withhold, and there is no benefit to the grandfather. How serious you are.” He said: Ka'b told me that Suhayb, the companion of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, told him that Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say them when... His departure from his prayer"
"746","On the authority of Muhammad bin Othman Al-Ijli, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Musa, on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of Abdul-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Musab bin Saad, and Amr Ibn Maymun Al-Azdi, they said: Saad used to teach his sons these words just as a clerk teaches boys. He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He used to seek refuge in them after the prayer: “O God, I seek refuge in You from stinginess, I seek refuge in You from cowardice, and I seek refuge in You from being returned to I despise life, and I seek refuge in You from the temptation of this world, and I seek refuge in You from the torment of the grave.”"
"747","It is narrated by Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Ahmasi, on the authority of Wakee’, on the authority of Uthman Al-Shaham, on the authority of Muslim bin Abi Bakra, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he used to say after the prayer: “O God, I seek refuge in You from disbelief, poverty, and the torment of the grave.”"
"748","On the authority of Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Ala, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Bishr ibn Asim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Dharr, he said: O Messenger of God, the people of Money is mixed with wages. They say as you say, and they spend but we do not. He said: “Shall I not tell you of a deed that if you do it, you will realize it before you?” And did you tell anyone after you except those who said something similar to what you said? At the end of every prayer, you say “Tasbih” thirty-three times, and you praise and “Allahu Akbar” like that, and behold, \You went to bed.\"""""
"749","Narrated by Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-Sana'ani, narrated by al-Mu'tamir, who said: I heard Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Sumayy, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that He said: The poor came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they said: The people of wealth have gone to high degrees and lasting bliss. They pray as we pray, and they fast as we fast, and they have gifts with which they perform Hajj and Umrah and perform jihad and give in charity. So he said: “Shall I not inform you? By a command, if you adhere to it, you will overtake those who came before you, and no one will overtake you after you, and you will be the best of those who completed it before him, except for one. “A deed similar to your deeds. You glorify, praise and exalt God thirty-three times after every prayer.” He said: So we disagreed among us, and some of us said: We glorify God thirty-three times, and we praise God thirty-three times, and we say “Allahu Akbar” thirty-four times. So I returned to him, and he said: She says, Glory be to God, and praise be to God, and God is great, until she completes thirty-three of them all.”"
"750","From Abu Bishr, from Khalid, meaning Ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of Abu Ubaid, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Yazid al-Laythi, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Whoever says Subhani Allah thirty-three times at the end of every prayer, and glorifies God thirty-three times, and praises God thirty-three times, That is ninety-nine, then the hundredth said: There is no god but God alone, with no partner. To Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise, and He is capable of all things. His sins are forgiven him, even if they are like the foam of the sea.”"
"751","Muhammad bin Mahdi Al-Attar narrated to us, Al-Muqri narrated to us, Haywa narrated to us, on the authority of Uqba bin Muslim, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman Al-Hubali, on the authority of Al-Sanabihi, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, that he said: One day the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took my hand and said to me: “O Muadh, by God, I To love you.” I said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, and by God, I love you. He said: “O Muadh, I advise you, do not neglect to say after every prayer: O God, help me.” For remembering You, thanking You, and worshiping You well.” Muadh al-Sanabihi recommended this, Al-Sanabihi recommended it to Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubali, and Abu Abd al-Rahman Uqba bin Muslim"
"752","Abu Qudamah Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, Othman bin Omar told us, Hisham bin Hassan told us. H Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan narrated to us, Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Kathir bin Aflah, on the authority of Zaid bin Thabit, because he said: “We were commanded to say ‘Tasbih’ Allah thirty-three times after every prayer, and ‘thank Him’ thirty-three times, and ‘Allahu Akbar’ thirty-four times.’ So it came. A man from the Ansar was in his sleep and it was said to him: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded you to say “Tasbih” at the end of every such-and-such prayer. He said: Yes, he said: “So make it twenty-five, and put in it the Tahlil,” so when the morning came, he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and informed him, and the Messenger of God said God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “So do it.” This is the hadith of Al-Thaqafi, and Abu Qudamah said: A man came in his dream, and it was said to him: Muhammad commanded you. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Do you exalt God thirty-three times after every prayer, praise Him thirty-three times, and say “Allahu Akbar” thirty-four times? He said: Yes, and he mentioned The rest of the conversation"
"753","We are Yahya bin Hakim, we are Sufyan bin Uyaynah. H. Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala’, narrated to us Sufyan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul-Rahman, who is the client of the family of Talha, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Juwayriyah bint Al-Harith said, and her name was Barrah, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, changed her name and called her Juwayriyah, and he hated To be said: He came out from a land. It said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, left while I was in my prayer place. He came back when daylight came and I was in it, and he said: “No.” Have you been praying since I left?” I said: Yes. He said: “I have said four words three times. If they were weighed according to what you said, they would be equal to them: Glory be to God. And with His praise, according to the number of His creation, the satisfaction of Himself, the weight of His Throne, and the ink of His words.” This is the hadith of Yahya bin Hakim, and Abdul Jabbar said: On the authority of Ibn Abbas, that when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to the morning prayer Juwayriyah was sitting in the mosque, so he mentioned the hadith but did not mention what had been said before this."
"754","Ali bin Abdul Rahman bin Al-Mughirah Al-Misri told us, Ibn Abi Maryam told us, Yahya bin Ayyub told us, Ibn Ajlan told me On the authority of Al-Mus’ab bin Muhammad bin Shurahbil, on the authority of Muhammad bin Saad bin Zurarah, on the authority of Abu Umamah Al-Bahili, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, passed by him while he was moving his lips, and he said: “What do you say, Abu Umamah?” He said: I remember my Lord. He said: “Shall I not tell you more or Is it better than your remembrance of the night with the day, and the day with the night, to say: Glory be to God, the number of what He created, and Glory be to God, the fullness of what He created, and Glory be to God. God is the number of what is in the earth and the sky, and Glory be to God is the fullness of what is in the earth and the sky, and Glory be to God is the number of what His Book has enumerated, and Glory be to God is the number of all Something, and Glory be to God fills everything, and you say praise like that.”"
"755","He said: I read to Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam, and he told me that his father told them. He said: Al-Layth told us. H Al-Hasan bin Muhammad narrated to us, Asim, meaning Ibn Ali, narrated to us, Laith narrated to us, on the authority of Hunayn bin Abi Hakim, on the authority of Ali bin Rabah, and in Hadith of Ibn Abd al-Hakam: On the authority of Ali Ibn Rabah, on the authority of Uqba, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “Recite the Mu’awwidhaat in Complete every prayer.” Al-Hasan bin Muhammad did not say: for me"
"756","Harun bin Ishaq told us, Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq. H And Issa bin Ibrahim narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, on the authority of Hafs bin Maysarah, both of them on the authority of Al-Alaa bin Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “If one of you prays and then sits in the place in which he prayed, you will still The angels pray over him: O God, forgive him, O God, have mercy on him, unless it happens.” This is the hadith of Ibn Fudayl, and in the report of Ibn Wahb, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If a Muslim prays, then sits in his place of prayer, he does not The angels pray for him: O God, forgive him, O God, have mercy on him, as long as it does not happen or arise.”"
"757","We are Bundar, we are Muhammad bin Jafar. H and Abu Musa told us, Abd al-Rahman told us, they said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Simak, that he asked Jabir bin Samra: How was the Messenger of God? What does he, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, do when he performs the Fajr prayer? He said: “He would sit in his place of prayer when he prayed the morning prayer until the sun rose.” This is the wording of the hadith of Bundar"
"758","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala and Sa’id bin Abdul-Rahman told us, they said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: A man stood up to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Should one of us pray in one garment? Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do you all have a garment?” . Abu Hurairah said to the one who asked him: Do you know Abu Hurairah? He prays in one garment, and his clothes are placed on the stand. This is the hadith of Saeed bin Abdul Rahman"
"759","Na Na Bundar, Yahya bin Saeed told us, Yazid bin Kaysan told us, Abu Hazim told me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “By the same one as my father A kitten in his hand. I saw that while I was looking in the mosque, I could hardly see a man praying in two garments, and today you are praying in \two and three\"""""
"760","Issa bin Ibrahim Al-Ghafiqi narrates, Ibn Wahb narrates, on the authority of Makhramah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, and he was asked about the man who prays in One shirt and he did not have his garment on, so he said: “There is nothing wrong with that if he hides it.” Amr bin Shuaib said that, and Bukayr said, and Saeed bin Al-Musayyab said: Ibn Masoud said: “We used to pray in one garment until God brought us clothes, and said: “Do not pray except in two clothes.” Ubayy bin Ka’b said: “There is nothing in this. We used to pray during the era of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, in one garment, and for us we have two garments.” Then it was said to Omar ibn al-Khattab, may God Almighty be pleased with him: “Don’t you make a judgement between these two when he is With them, he said: I am with me"
"761","Ahmad bin Abdah told us, Hammad told us, meaning Ibn Zaid. H. Bundar and Yahya bin Hakim told us, saying: Yahya bin Saeed told us. H. Abu Kurayb told us, Abu Usama told us. H. Salam bin Junada, Waki’ told us, all of them on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa. H Yahya bin Hakim told us, Al-Hasan bin Habib, meaning Ibn Nadbah, Hisham told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Omar bin Abi Salamah, He said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying in Umm Salamah’s house in a single garment with two ends separated."
"762","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me, and Usama bin Zaid Al-Laythi told me, on the authority of my father Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, that he saw the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “praying in one garment, with its two ends separated on the his shoulders, and his clothes on the stand.”"
"763","Abu Qudamah narrated to me, Yahya narrated to me, on the authority of Sufyan, Abu Hazim narrated to me, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad, he said: “There were men who prayed with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him, tying their shoulders around their necks in the manner of boys. It will be said to the women: Do not raise your heads until the men are sitting level.” Similar to this is narrated by Salam bin Junada, narrated by Waki’, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Sa’d, and he added, he said: From the distress of people."
"764","Harun bin Ishaq Al-Hamdani told us, Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “I was in Seventy of the Companions of Suffah, not a single man of them wearing a robe, either a cloak or a cloak that they tied around their necks, some of which reached the length of the shin. And some of them reach the ankles, and he gathers them in his hand for fear that his private parts should be seen.” Abu Bakr said: Abu Hazim is a Madani whose name is Salama bin Dinar, who narrated on the authority of Sahl bin Saad, and who narrated on the authority of Abu Hurairah Salman. Al-Ashja'i"
"765","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala and Saeed bin Abdul-Rahman told us, they said: Sufyan told us. H. Ali bin Hajar told us, Ibn Abi Al-Zannad told us. H. Salam bin Junada told us, Waki` told us, on the authority of Sufyan, all of them on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “None of you should pray in one garment, with nothing of it on his shoulders.” However, Abdul Jabbar said: On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he was informed of it."
"766","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ told us, Abu Bahr Abd al-Rahman bin Uthman al-Bakrawi told us, Sa’id bin Abi Arouba told us, Ayoub told us, on the authority of Nafi’, he said: Ibn Umar saw me praying in one garment, so he said: Didn’t I give you two garments? He said: I said: Yes, he said: Have you seen that if I sent you on a need, would you go out in one garment? I said: No. He said: God is more deserving of you being beautified for him. Then he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “If none of you has anything but One garment, let him girdle his waist with it, and do not use it to cover the Jews.” Abu Bakr said: This report is also general and unexplained. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, meant this garment that he ordered to be tied around the waist. Tight clothing rather than loose clothing, and the explanation for these two reports."
"767","He said: This is what Muhammad bin Rafi’ narrated to us, Shurayh bin Al-Nu’man narrated to us, Falayh bin Sulayman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Harith, that Jabir bin Abdullah came, he and a group he named, and when we entered upon him, we found him praying in one garment, wrapped in it. He had differed between His two ends, and his robe was close to him. If he took it, he would reach it. He said: When he said the salutation, we asked him about his prayer in one garment, and he said: I will do this. Let fools like you see me and reveal to Jabir a concession granted by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Indeed, I went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. peace be upon him, during one of his travels, so I came to him one night regarding some matter of mine, and I found him praying while I was wearing one garment that I covered myself with, and I prayed until... beside him, and when he left, he said: “What is the secret, O Jabir?” So I informed him of my need, and when I finished, he said: “O Jabir, what is this inclusion that you saw?” So I said: It was one tight garment. He said: “If you pray with one garment on you, then if it is wide, wrap yourself around it, even if it is tight.” “Girdle yourselves with it.”"
"768","I am Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala, Sufyan told us, Abu Ishaq Al-Shaybani told us, he heard it from Abdullah bin Shaddad, on the authority of Maymunah, She said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to pray while I was wearing a cloak, some of it on me and some of it on him, and I was menstruating.” The overcoat is a covering made of wool"
"769","Muhammad bin Abi Safwan Al-Thaqafi told us, Sa’id bin Amir told us, Sa’id told us. H Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Zaafrani narrated to us, Abdul-Wahhab bin Ata narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you prays in one garment, let him tighten it around his loins, and do not cover them like a garment.” \The Jews.\"" This is the hadith of Ibn Abi Safwan"""
"770","On the authority of Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala Al-Attar, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Omar ibn Abi Salamah, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed Peace and blessings of God be upon him in the house of Umm Salama, wearing a garment covered with it.”"
"771","Muhammad bin Al-Ala bin Kurayb narrated to us, Abu Usama narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, that Omar bin Abi Salamah told him, he said: I saw the Prophet praying May God bless him and grant him peace: “He prays in a garment covered with it in Umm Salamah’s house, placing his two ends on his shoulders.”"
"772","On the authority of Muhammad bin Isa, on the authority of Abdullah, meaning Ibn Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Dhakwan, on the authority of Sulayman Al-Ahwal, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Huraira, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “forbade lowering one’s face during prayer, and for a man to cover his mouth.”"
"773","Omar bin Hafs Al-Shaybani told us, Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Abdul Hamid bin Jaafar, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Marthad bin Abdullah, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, on the authority of Omar, he said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying in a silk robe, then he did not remain To remove it.” This is how Al-Shaybani told us about it. He said: On the authority of Omar, and it is an illusion."
"774","He said: Bundar and Abu Musa told us about it, they said: On the authority of Uqba bin Amir, he said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they did not mention Omar, this is the correct one, and the mention of Omar in this news is an illusion, but the correct one is, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"775","Hisham bin Abdul-Malik Abu Al-Walid and Al-Hajjaj bin Al-Minhal narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, on the authority of Safiyya bint al-Harith, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God does not accept a woman’s prayer She has menstruated unless she wears a veil.” Bundar told us, Yahya told us, Humaid bin Abdullah told us, my mother told me, on the authority of Aisha, that she said: A woman should not You pray. Abu Bakr said: Humaid bin Abdullah is Al-Kharrat."
"776","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Amr, Ibn Lahi’ah, and Al-Layth bin Saad told me. H Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Hakam told us, my father and Shuaib told us, they said: Al-Layth bin Saad told us. H Yahya bin Hakim told us, Abu Al-Walid told us, Al-Layth bin Saad told us. Al-Fadl bin Yaqoub Al-Jazari narrated to us, Abd Al-Ala narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, all of them on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Suwayd bin Qais, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Khadij, said: I heard Muawiyah bin Abi Sufyan say: I asked Umm Habibah: Was the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He, peace and blessings be upon him, prays in the garment in which he has intercourse with her? She said: “Yes, as long as he does not see any harm in him.” Ibn al-Hakam, al-Fadl, and Yahya ibn Hakim said: On the authority of Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan. And in the hadith of Ibn Ishaq: In the garment in which he has intercourse with you?"
"777","Nasr bin Ali told us, Abd al-Aziz bin Muhammad al-Darawardi told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ibrahim, he said: I heard Salama bin al-Akwa’, saying: I said: O Messenger of God, I am hunting and you are attending prayer, and I am wearing a shirt. He said: “Tie it, even if it is with a thorn.”"
"778","Ahmad bin Abdah al-Dhabi told us, Abd al-Aziz bin Muhammad al-Madani told us, Musa bin Ibrahim told me, on the authority of Salama bin al-Akwa’, he said: I asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “Should I be hunting and only wear one shirt or robe, should I wear it?” He said: “Yes, even with a thorn.” He once said: “Prick it, even with a fork.” Abu Bakr said: This Musa bin Ibrahim is the son of Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Abi Rabi’ah. This is how Attaf bin Khaled, and I think he is the son of Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Muammar bin Abi Rabi’ah. His father Ibrahim is the one who Sharhabeel bin Saad mentioned that he and Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Muammar bin Abi Rabi’ah entered upon Jabir bin Abdullah mentioned in a long hadith"
"779","Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Safwan bin Salih al-Thaqafi told us, Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, Zuhair bin Muhammad told us, Zaid bin Aslam told us, He said: I saw Ibn Umar praying with his buttons loose, so I asked him about that, and he said: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, doing it."
"780","Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Sulayman bin Abdul Rahman told us, Al-Walid told us, like this, except that he did not say: So I asked him, and he said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying with his buttons unbuttoned."
"781","Muhammad bin Khalaf Al-Hadadi told us, Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, Shayban bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Abdul Rahman Ibn Thawban, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Amr, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God does not look at the prayer A man who drags his garment recklessly.” Abu Bakr said: They differed regarding this chain of transmission. Some of them said: On the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, I included this chapter in the book on clothing."
"782","Bishr bin Muadh Al-Aqdi told us, Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “I was commanded to prostrate on seven sides, and not to tie my hair or my clothes.”"
"783","Yahya bin Saeed, I am Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Amr bin Sulaym, on the authority of Ibn Abi Qatada, on the authority of Amer bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Amr ibn Sulaym, on the authority of Ibn Abi Qatada ibn Rabi’i, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was carrying Abi’s daughter. “The sinner is on his neck during prayer, so when he prostrates he places it, and when he stands he carries it.”"
"784","He said: Al-Dawrqi narrated to us with this chain of transmission. He said: “And he was carrying the daughter of Zainab on his neck and leading the people in prayer, so when he bowed, he placed her down. And when he stood up, he carried her.”"
"785","Bundar told us, Muhammad told us, meaning Ibn Ja`far, Shu`bah told us, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq talking, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: While the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was prostrating, and around him were people from the Quraysh, when Uqba ibn Abi Mu’it came to ask He was arrogant, so he threw it at the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, but he did not raise his head, so Fatima came and took him from his back, and prayed for those who He did so and said: “O God, upon you are the leaders of Quraysh, Abu Jahl bin Hisham, Utbah bin Rabi’ah, Shaybah bin Rabi’ah, and Uqba bin Abu Muayt, Umayyah bin Khalaf, or Ubayy bin Khalaf Shu’bah Al-Shak.” He said: I saw them killed on the Day of Badr, and thrown into a well, but either Umayyah or Ubayy had their limbs cut off, so they were not thrown into the well."
"786","Narrated to me Muhammad bin Aqeel, narrated to Hafs, Ibrahim narrated to me, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Naama, on the authority of Abu Nadra, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led us in prayer one day. He took off his shoes and placed them on his left. When the people saw that the Messenger of God God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had taken off his sandals. They had taken off their sandals, and when he had finished, he said to them: “What is the matter with you when you took off your sandals?” They said: O Messenger of God, we saw that you took off your sandals, so we took off our sandals. He said: “A person came to me and told me that there was something wrong with my sandals, so I took them off. “If one of you enters the mosque, let him look, and if he sees dirt on his sandals, let him wipe them with the ground, then pray in them.”"
"787","It was narrated by Abd al-Jabbar bin Al-Ala, it was narrated by Sufyan, h. Bundar and Abu Musa narrated to us, they said: Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, h. Sallam bin Junada, I am Waki’, narrated to us on the authority of Sufyan, all of them on the authority of Al-Amash, h. Sallam bin Junada, I am Abu Muawiyah, narrated to us on the authority of Al-A'mash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Dharr, said: I said, O Messenger of God: Which mosque was built on earth first? He said: “Touch the forbidden grandfather.” He said: I said: Then what? He said: “Al-Aqsa Mosque.” He said: I said: How much is there between them? He said: “Forty years, then wherever prayer leads you, pray, for that is a mosque.” This is the hadith of Abu Muawiyah, and the meaning of their entire hadith is the same. Abu Bakr said: The news of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “The entire earth has been made for us a mosque and a purification” from this chapter."
"788","Imran bin Musa Al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Abd Al-Warith narrated to us, Abu Al-Tayyah Al-Dhabi narrated to us, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: When he presented The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray wherever the prayer led him, and he would pray in the sheep pens, then he ordered the mosque. He said: So he sent To a group of Banu al-Najjar who came, and he said: “O Banu al-Najjar, give me an eighth with this wall of yours.” They said: No, by God, we do not ask for its price except from God. Anas said: In it were the graves of polytheists, and there were ruins in it and there were palm trees. He said: So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered graves to be made. The polytheists were dug up, the ruins were leveled, and the palm trees were cut down. He said: Arrange the palm trees facing the direction of the mosque, and he said: “Make its supports of stones.”"
"789","On the authority of Yusuf ibn Musa, on the authority of Hussein ibn Ali, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Asim ibn Abi al-Najjoud, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Indeed, among the worst people are those whom the Hour will overtake while they are still alive, and those who take graves as places of worship.”"
"790","I am Bundar, and Yahya bin Hakim said: Yahya told us, I am Hisham bin Urwa, and Bundar said, on the authority of Hisham, my father told me, On the authority of Aisha, that Umm Salamah and Umm Habiba mentioned a church they had seen in Abyssinia, which had pictures, so they mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Those, when there was a righteous man among them, they built a mosque over his grave, and placed those images in it, those are evil.” “Creation is with God.”"
"791","I am Al-Hussein bin Harith Abu Ammar, Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad Al-Darawardi told us, on the authority of Amr bin Yahya, H. Bishr bin Muaz told us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Amr ibn Yahya al-Ansari narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “The entire earth is a mosque, except for the bathroom and the cemetery.”"
"792","Bishr bin Muadh narrated to us, Bishr bin Al-Fadl narrated to us, Amara bin Ghaziyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Amara Al-Ansari, on the authority of Abu Saeed, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"793","Al-Hasan bin Harith narrated to us, Al-Walid bin Muslim narrated to us, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, saying: Busr bin Ubayd Allah, that he heard Wathilah bin Al-Asqa’ Al-Laythi saying: I heard Abu Marthad Al-Ghanawi saying: “Do not sit on graves, and do not pray.” \To her.\"" Abu Bakr said: Ibn al-Mubarak included between Busr ibn Ubayd Allah and Wathilah Abu Idris al-Khawlani in this news."""
"794","Bundar told us, Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us, Abdullah bin Al Mubarak told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Yazid, Busr bin Ubaid told me God, he said: I heard Abu Idris, he said: I heard Wathilah bin Al-Asqa’, saying: I heard Abu Al-Marthad Al-Ghanawi, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He says something similar"
"795","Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam al-Ijli narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray’i narrated to us, and Ismail ibn Bishr ibn Mansour al-Sulami narrated to us, he narrated to us Abd al-Ala, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Alaa ibn Kurayb, on the authority of Abu Khaled, on the authority of Hisham ibn Hassan, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Al-Ala, Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr, who is Ibn Ayyash, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “If you find nothing but sheep pens and camel pens, then pray in sheep pens, and do not pray in camel pens.” Muhammad bin Al-Alaa said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Do not pray in camel pens, and pray in sheep pens.”"
"796","On the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Ala, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Bakr, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"797","Muhammad bin Yahya told me, Ibrahim bin Al-Hakam bin Aban told me, my father told me, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet was May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “perhaps he prayed over the place where he had intercourse.”"
"798","We were told by Bundar, we were told by Yahya, we were told by Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Ashjaj, we were told by Uqba, meaning Ibn Khalid Al-Sakouni, we were told by Ubaid Allah, Nafi’ told me, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he “stacked the spear and prayed towards it,” and Al-Ashjaj said: “It was.” He focuses the spear between his hands,” and did nothing more than that."
"799","Al-Ashjaj told us, Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to focus on The spear, he prays with it on the day of Eid.”"
"800","Bundar told us, Abu Bakr, meaning the Hanafi, told us, Al-Dahhak bin Uthman told us, Sadaqah bin Yasar told me, he said: I heard Ibn Umar, He says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not pray except with a curtain, and do not let anyone pass in front of you. If he refuses, then you must fight him, for you are with him.” \Al-Qurain\"""""
"801","Muhammad bin Al-Ala told us, Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he greeted and prayed to his mount.” Nafi’ said: “And I saw Ibn Umar praying to his mount.”"
"802","Al-Ashjaj and Harun bin Ishaq told us about it, but they did not mention the vision. They said: On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he was praying. Aaron said: To his camel, and Abu Sa’id said: To his camel, and Ibn Omar used to do it."
"803","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala told us, Sufyan told us, Safwan bin Sulaym told us, Ahmad bin Mani’ and Ahmad bin Abdah told us, They said: Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Safwan bin Sulaym, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr bin Mut’im, on the authority of Sahl bin Abi Hathamah, Abd said: Al-Jabbar: And he conveyed it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Others said: A narration. He said: “When one of you prays, let him pray to the sutrah, and come close to it, not Satan breaks off his prayers.”"
"804","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, my father narrated to me, on the authority of Sahl bin Sa’d, he said: “There was a place in the prayer area of the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and between the wall there is as much space as a sheep’s path.”"
"805","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Habib bin Al-Shahid told us, Omar bin Ubaid Al-Tanafisi told us, on the authority of Samak bin Harb, on the authority of Musa bin Talha, on the authority of His father, he said: We were praying while the animals were passing in front of us, so we asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “It is like the end of a journey being in front of me.” “One of you, and what passes between his hands will not be harmed.”"
"806","Al-Dawrqi told us, Ibn Ulayya told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Humayd ibn Hilal, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Samit, on the authority of Abu Dharr, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When one of you stands to pray, he will cover it if it is in front of him, like the end of a saddle,” then he mentioned The hadith is given to us by Abu Al-Khattab. We are Bishr, meaning Ibn al-Mufaddal. Yunus told us something similar."
"807","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, Abd al-Razzaq told us, and Ahmad bin Sa’id al-Darimi told us, Abu Asim told us, both of them on the authority of Ibn Juraij. I said to Ata’: “How much The back of a saddlebag that covers the one who is praying. He said, “The length of an arm’s length.”"
"808","We are Muhammad bin Muammar Al-Qaisi, we are Muhammad bin Al-Qasim Abu Ibrahim Al-Asadi, we are Thawr bin Yazid, on the authority of Burayd bin Yazid bin Jabir, On the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Yazid ibn Jabir, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “It is part of the tunic like the back of The journey, even if it were just a hair's breadth.\ Abu Bakr said: I fear that it is Muhammad bin Al-Qasim"
"809","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Sulayman bin Bilal told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Anas bin Malik He said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying to her in the prayer place,” meaning the goat. Abu Bakr said: Concerning the command of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to cover oneself with the arrow during prayer, it has not been proven and proven that he, may God bless him and grant him peace, meant “By commanding to cover oneself like the end of a mount, in its length, not in its entire length and width.”"
"810","Abdullah bin Imran Al-Rabi’ Al-Abidi narrated to us with this news. Ibrahim, meaning Ibn Saad, narrated to me on the authority of Abd Al-Malik, who is Ibn Abd. Al-Aziz bin Sabra Al-Juhani, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Be concealed in your prayers, even if \with an arrow\"""""
"811","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala and Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Jawaz narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Abu Muhammad Ibn Amr Ibn Harith narrates to him, on the authority of his grandfather, I heard Abu Hurairah say: Abu Al-Qasim, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you prays Let him place something in his hands.” And he once said: “Something facing his face. If he does not find anything, let him set up a stick. If he does not find a stick, let him draw a line. Then what passed between his hands will not harm him.” The permissibility said: Let him place something facing his face, and the rest should be the same."
"812","A similar hadith of permissibility was narrated to us by Muhammad bin Abd al-Ala al-San’ani, Bishr bin al-Mufaddal narrated to us, Ismail bin Umayyah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Amr bin Harith, that he heard his grandfather speaking, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said. Abu Bakr said: What is correct is what Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal said, and so said Muammar and Al-Thawri, on the authority of Abu Amr bin Harith, except that they, They said on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. Muhammad ibn Rafi’ narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma’mar and al-Thawri narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail ibn Umayyah."
"813","Ali bin Khashram narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Salim bin Al-Nadr, on the authority of Busr bin Saeed, he said: Zayd bin Khalid sent me to Abu Juhaim, I ask him about what passes in front of the person praying. What should he do? He said: “If it were better for him to stand forty than for it to pass before him.”"
"814","Ahmad bin Mani’ told us, Abu Ahmad told us, Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman told us, my uncle told me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah On the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Rafi’, Ibn Abi Fudaik told us, Ubayd Allah told me, on the authority of his uncle, on the authority of my father Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you knew what is involved in walking in front of his brother objecting while he is conversing with his Lord, It was more beloved to him to stand in that place for a hundred years than to step.” This is the hadith of Ibn Mani’."
"815","On the authority of Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawrqi, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Kathir bin Kathir, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Muttalib Ibn Abi Wada'ah said: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he finished his circumambulation. The entourage of Al-Mataf came and prayed two rak'ahs, without \The circumambulators are one\"""""
"816","Ahmad bin Abdah told us, Abdul Aziz, meaning Ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi, told us Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Saeed. Al-Khudri, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you is praying, he should not let anyone pass in front of him. He refused, let him fight him, for he is a devil.”"
"817","Abdul-Warith bin Abdul-Samad told us, my father told us, Hammam told us, Zaid bin Aslam told us, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Abi Saeed. On the authority of his father, he was praying to a pole, and a man from the Umayyads passed by. He prevented him, so he went to come back and hit him. He was struck in the chest. He was a man from the Umayyads. He mentioned that to Marwan. Marwan met him and said: What made you hit your brother’s son? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you prays for something that he will cover, and someone passes in front of him, let him prevent him. He refused, let him fight him, for he is a devil, for you have struck the devil.”"
"818","Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad told me, my father told me, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Humaid ibn Hilal, on the authority of Abu Salih, he said: While Abu Sa`id Al-Khudri prays on Friday, so he mentioned the hadith like the hadith of Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah, which follows him in the second chapter, except that he added to it: And I forbade him, but he refused to stop. He said: And Marwan was in charge of Medina that day, so he complained to him, so Marwan mentioned that to Abu Sa’id, and Abu Sa’id said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “If something passes in front of one of you while he is praying, let him stop it twice, and if he refuses, let him fight it, for it is Satan.”"
"819","Yaqoub Al-Dawraqi told us, Hashim bin Al-Qasim told us, Sulayman bin Al-Mughirah told us, on the authority of Humaid bin Hilal, on the authority of Abu Salih, he said: While Abu Sa`id al-Khudri was praying on Friday for something that would protect him from the people, a young man from Banu Abi Mu’it came to him and wanted to pass between His hands, so he pushed it into his throat, and he looked and did not find any comfort except in the hands of Abu Saeed, so he returned and pushed it into his throat, harder than the first push. He said: So he appeared standing, then he got rid of Abu Sa’id, then he went out. He went to Marwan, and they complained to him about what he had received from Abu Sa’id. He said: And Abu Sa’id went in to Marwan, and he said: What do you have to do when your brother’s son came to complain about you? Abu Sa’id said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “When he prayed If one of you wants to pass in front of him, let him throw it into his throat. If he refuses, let him fight him, for he is a devil.”"
"820","Bundar told us, Abu Bakr told us, meaning the Hanafi, Al-Dahhak bin Uthman told us, Sadaqa bin Yasar told me, he said: I heard Ibn Umar, He says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not pray except with a curtain, and do not let anyone pass in front of you. If he refuses, then you must fight him, for you are with him.” \Al-Qurain\"""""
"821","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, Abdullah bin Yazid told us, Musa bin Ayyub Al-Ghafiqi told us, my uncle Iyas bin Amir told me, he said: I heard Ali bin Abi Talib say: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was praising God at night, and Aisha was standing between him and the qiblah.” . Abu Bakr said: His saying: “Tasbih” at night means he wants to perform voluntary prayers."
"822","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala and Saeed bin Abdul-Rahman told us, they said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “was praying his prayer at night, and I was standing between him and the qiblah, like standing in the way of a funeral.” Al-Makhzoumi added once: “If he wants to perform the witr prayer, he can force his foot behind me.”"
"823","Ahmad ibn Abdah informed us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, informed us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “he used to pray at night while I was asleep between him and the Qiblah, so if he performed Witr, he would wake me up.” Ahmad told us, Hammad told us, he said: Ayoub said, on the authority of Hisham, she said: “An objection like the objection of a funeral.”"
"824","Bundar told us, Yahya told us, Muhammad bin Al-Ala bin Kurayb told us, Ibn Bishr told us: Hisham told us, Salam bin Junada told us, Sallam bin Junada told us, Waki`, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, similar to the hadith of Hammad, on the authority of Hisham, except that in the hadith of Waki` and Ibn Bishr: “And I disagree between him.” And between the qiblah, if he wanted to perform the Witr prayer, he would wake me up and I would perform the Witr prayer.” And in the hadith of Bundar: “He prays at night while our bed is between him and the qiblah, so if he wants to pray the Witr prayer, he makes me stand still and pray the Witr prayer.”"
"825","Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Ashjaj told us, Hafs, meaning Ibn Ghayath, told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha; And Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Al-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was praying while I was interrupted between... His hands, so if I want to get up, I slip by my feet.”"
"826","Al-Dawrqi narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: Perhaps I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. “He prays at night in bed, and I am on the bed between him and the Qiblah. Whenever I have a need, I slip by my feet.” I hate the bed and face it.”"
"827","I am Abu Tahir, we are Al-Fadl bin Ya’qub Al-Rakhami, we are Al-Haytham bin Jamil, we are Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Ya’la bin Hakim, and Al-Zubayr bin Al-Kharait, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was “praying, and a sheep passed in front of him, so he led it towards the Qiblah.” until he pressed his stomach to the qiblah.”"
"828","Bundar told us, Ubaid Allah bin Abdul Majeed told us, Abdul Rahman bin Abi Al-Zannad told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of my father A kitten, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A kitten does not interrupt prayer, it is one of the household’s belongings.”"
"829","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman narrated it. Ibn Wahb told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Al-Zinad, with this hadith as a chain of transmission, not traceable. Abu Bakr said: Ibn Wahb is more knowledgeable about the hadith of the people of Medina than Ubayd Allah bin Abdul Majeed."
"830","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi told us, Ibn Ulayya told us, on the authority of Yunus, H. Abu Al-Khattab Ziyad bin Yahya told us, Bishr told us I mean, Ibn al-Mufaddal, Yunus, h. Ahmad bin Mani’ told us, Hushaym told us, Yunus, and Mansour, who is Ibn Zazan, told us, Bundar narrated to us, Muhammad bin Ja’far narrated to us, Shu’bah, H, and Hilal bin Bishr narrated to us, Salem bin Nuh narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman bin Amer, H. Nasr bin Marzuq told us, Asad, meaning Ibn Musa, told us, Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ayyub, Yunus bin Ubaid, and Habib. Ibn Al-Shahid, and Al-Dawrqi told us, Al-Mu’tamir Ibn Sulaiman, on the authority of Salem, who is Ibn Al-Zinad, all of them on the authority of Humaid Ibn Hilal, he told us Abu Al-Khattab Ziyad bin Yahya told us Sahl bin Aslam, meaning Al-Adawi, Humaid bin Hilal told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Samit, On the authority of Abu Dharr, and this is the hadith of Abu Al-Khattab, on the authority of Sahl bin Aslam, Abu Dharr said: The donkey, the woman, and the dog interrupt the prayer. Black, I said: O Abu Dharr: What is the matter with a dog that is black from white, from yellow, from red? He said: O my nephew, I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, as you asked me, and he said: “The black dog is a devil.”"
"831","On the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Walid, on the authority of Abdul-A’la bin Abdul-A’la Al-Shami, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Humaid bin Hilal, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Samit, On the authority of Abu Dhar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Prayer is repeated in the passage of the donkey, the woman, and the black dog.” I said: What is the matter with the black ones? From the yellow dog, from the red dog, and he said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, just as you asked me, and he said: “The black dog is a devil.”"
"832","Abdullah bin Hashim told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Jabir bin Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “A dog interrupts prayer, and a menstruating woman”"
"833","Abu Musa Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna, Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala’, and Sa’id bin Abdul-Rahman narrated it. They said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, On the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Al-Fadl and I came while we were on a donkey, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He led the people in prayer at Arafat, so we passed by some rows, then we got down from them and left them to graze, but he did not tell us. Abu Musa said: He meant something, and he said Abdul-Jabbar: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not forbid us. Al-Makhzoumi said: He did not say anything to us. Abu Bakr said: It was narrated by Muammar. And Malik, they said: He leads the people in prayer in Mina."
"834","Abu Musa told us, Abd al-A’la told me, Muammar told us, Yunus ibn Abd al-A’la told us, Ibn Wahb told us that Malik told him, he told us Yaqub Al-Dawraqi, Abdul-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Malik, in the report of Muammar, “The donkey passed in front of the people, but he did not interrupt their prayer.” And in Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Malik: “I was riding a donkey, so I left him in the middle of the row and began to pray, but he did not blame me.” Abu Bakr said: This report does not contain the fact that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw the donkeys passing by, and not cowering in front of the lines, nor that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He, peace and blessings be upon him, was aware of that, so he did not order the one before whom the donkey passed to repeat the prayer, and the report is established and authentic on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. “The black dog, the menstruating woman, and the donkey interrupt the prayer,” and unless there is proven information from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, against This does not permit speech or fatwa contrary to what has been proven from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"835","Shu`bah narrated, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Yahya bin Al-Jazzar, on the authority of Suhaib, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: I and a boy from Banu Hashim came to A donkey, or two donkeys, so I passed in front of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was praying, but he did not leave, and two female slaves from Banu Abd came. Al-Muttalib, so they took the knees of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he separated - or separated - them, and did not move away. Abu Bakr said: And not in This news is that the donkey passed through the hands of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he only said: So I passed through the hands of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, This word indicates that Ibn Abbas passed in front of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, after he got off the donkey, because he said: So I passed between The hands of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, as he prayed"
"836","However, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated it on the authority of Shu`bah, who said: So we passed in front of him, then we descended and entered with him in prayer. Muhammad ibn Uthman forbade him. Al-Ijli, Ubayd Allah told us, and the ruling for Ubayd Allah ibn Musa on Muhammad ibn Ja`far is impossible, especially in the hadith of Shu`bah, even if he disagreed with Muhammad ibn Ja`far. A number like Ubayd Allah, according to the hadith of Shu`bah, would have been ruled by Muhammad ibn Ja`far. This news was narrated by Mansour bin Al-Mu’tamir, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Yahya bin Al-Jazzar, on the authority of Abu Al-Sahba’, who was Suhaib, who said: We were With Ibn Abbas, we mentioned what interrupts the prayer, and they said: The donkey and the woman. Ibn Abbas said: I and a boy from Banu Abbas have come. Abdul Muttalib, riding a donkey, while the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was leading the people in prayer in an empty land, so we left the donkey in their hands, then We came until we entered into their hands, so what happened to that? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was praying, then two female slaves from Banu Abd came. Al-Muttalib and they fought, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, took them and separated one of them from the other, so what did that matter?"
"837","I am Abu Tahir, narrated by Abu Bakr, narrated by Yusuf bin Musa, narrated by Jarir, on the authority of Mansour, Abu Bakr said: This narration appears to be narration. Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the donkey only passed in front of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, after he got off the donkey; Because he said: So I passed in front of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was praying, except that Ubayd Allah bin Musa narrated it on the authority of Shu’bah, and he said: So we passed In front of him, then we descended and entered with him in prayer. Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Ijli forbade him, Ubayd Allah lent us, and the ruling belonged to Ubayd Allah ibn Musa upon Muhammad ibn Ja'far is impossible, especially in the hadith of Shu'bah, and if Muhammad ibn Ja'far had disagreed with a number like Ubayd Allah regarding the hadith of Shu'bah, the ruling would have been for Muhammad ibn Jafar is upon them. This news was narrated by Mansour bin Al-Mu’tamir, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Yahya bin Al-Jazzar, on the authority of Abu Al-Sahba’, who is Suhaib, who said: We were With Ibn Abbas, we mentioned what interrupts the prayer, and they said: The donkey and the woman. Ibn Abbas said: I and a boy from Banu Abbas have come. Abdul Muttalib, riding a donkey, while the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was leading the people in prayer in an empty land, so we left the donkey in their hands, then We came until we entered into their hands, so what happened to that? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was praying, then two female slaves from Banu Abd came. Al-Muttalib and they fought, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, took them and separated one of them from the other, and that did not matter. Yusuf bin Musa forbade him, then Jarir, on the authority of Mansour, Abu Bakr said: This news appears to be the same as the news of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the donkey It passed between the hands of the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, not between the hands of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and it does not include that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, knew about that. It was reported that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, knew that the donkey had passed through the hands of some of those who were behind him, so it is permissible for it to be the jacket of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. It was a cover for those behind him, as the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to cover himself with a spear when he prayed in the prayer place, even if his cover was not It will be a cover for those behind him, because every person who is being led in prayer needs to be covered with a spear, just as the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was covered with it. So he carried the goat for the Prophet. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he covers himself with it without ordering the followers to cover himself behind him, as an indication that the imam’s jacket is a cover for those behind him. \\""\\n[Commentary] 835 - Al-Azami said: Its chain of transmission is authentic"""
"838","Ibn Jurayj narrated, saying: Abd al-Karim told me that a mujahid told him on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: I and al-Fadl came riding on donkeys. So we passed in front of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at Arafat while he was praying the prescribed prayer. Nothing could cover him, come between us and him. “\\""\""\\n[Commentary] 838 - He said Al-Azami: Its chain of transmission is authentic"""
"839","Ibn Jurayj narrated, saying: Abd al-Karim told me that a mujahid told him, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: “I and al-Fadl Ali came to A donkey, so we passed in front of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at Arafat while he was praying the obligatory prayer. Nothing could cover him, come between us and him.” Abdullah bin Ishaq Al-Jawhari discouraged him, told us Abu Asim, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, Abu Bakr said: It is not permissible to use Abd as evidence. Al-Karim, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah, and this word was narrated on the authority of Ibn Abbas, contrary to this meaning."
"840","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Hakam bin Aban told us, my father told me, H, Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Hakam, narrated to us by my father, H., Saad bin Abdullah bin Abdullah Al-Hakam narrated to us, Hafs bin Omar Al-Muqri narrated to us, Al-Hakam bin Aban narrated to us. On the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “The goat was placed in front of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in Arafat, and he prayed with it. And the donkey is behind the goat.” Abu Bakr said: This news is the opposite of the news of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Mujahid. Because in this report, the donkey was behind the goat, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, centered the goat in his hands with Arafah, so he prayed. To it, and in the story of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: While he is praying the prescribed prayer, there is nothing that can cover him that will come between us and him, and the story of Abdul Al-Karim, and the news of Al-Hakam bin Aban is close in terms of transmission, because Abd Al-Karim has spoken of the people of knowledge regarding the hadith as evidence. With his experience, as well as the report of Al-Hakam bin Aban, except that the news of Al-Hakam bin Aban is supported by authentic reports from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. In terms of transmission, Abd al-Karim’s report on the authority of Mujahid is supported by authentic reports in terms of transmission on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and this The act that Abdul Karim mentioned, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, has been proven on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he discouraged something like This action is in the narration of Sahl bin Abi Hathamah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When one of you prays, let him pray to a sutrah, and let him From it, Satan does not interrupt his prayers.”"
"841","And in the news of Aoun bin Abi Juhayfah, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “set a goat and began praying to it, passing behind it.” The dog, the woman, and the donkey.” Al-Dawrqi narrated to us, Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abu Musa narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Awn bin Abi Juhayfah, and in Al-Rabi’ bin Sabra Al-Juhani reported on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Be concealed in your prayers, even if only with an arrow.” And in the report of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, on the authority of The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “When one of you prays, let him pray toward a sutrah and come close to it.” Abu Bakr said: All of these reports are authentic. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered the praying person to cover himself during his prayer. Abdul Karim claimed, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He prayed without a curtain, while he was in space. Because at Arafat there was no building at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, could cover with, and he, may God bless him and grant him peace, rebuked The person praying, peace and blessings of God be upon him, is not allowed to pray except with a sutrah. In the news of Sadaqa bin Yassar, I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not pray except with a covering.” And he, may God bless him and grant him peace, rebuked The person praying, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, is not to pray except with a sutrah, so how can he do what he, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, is forbidden from doing? And in the story of Musa bin Talha, on the authority of his father, there is evidence that if a donkey passes between the hands of a person praying and there is no curtain in his hands, then the donkey’s passing between them will harm him. His hands"
"842","On the authority of Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Habib ibn al-Shahid, on the authority of Omar ibn Ubaid al-Tanafisi, on the authority of Samak ibn Harb, on the authority of Musa ibn Talha, on the authority of His father, he said: We were praying while the animals were passing in front of us, so we asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “The example of the end of a journey is in front of me.” “One of you, let him not be harmed by what passed between his hands.”"
"843","Abu Musa told us, Abdul Rahman told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Musa bin Talha, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Let one of you place something like the back of a saddlebag before him, then what passed before him will not harm him.” Abu Bakr said: In his saying, may God bless him and grant him peace: “The likeness of the back of a saddlebag is in the hands of one of you, then what passes through his hands will not harm him.” A clear indication is that if it is not in his hands, such as the back of a saddlebag, it will be harmed by the passing of animals in his hands, and the animals that are harmed by passing in his hands are The animals that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, knew would interrupt prayer, which is the donkey and the black dog, according to what the Chosen One, may God bless him and grant him peace, knew. Peace and blessings be upon him, not any other animal that does not interrupt prayer."
"844","Abu Musa told us, Muhammad bin Ja’far told me, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, he said: I heard al-Qasim speaking, on the authority of Aisha had a garment on which there were pictures spread out, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was praying to it, so he said: “Delay it.” from me, so she took it and made it a pillow.”"
"845","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ubayy and Shuaib told us, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abu Al-Khair, On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him, that he said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Teach me a supplication that I may pray.” With him in my prayers.”"
"846","Yunus bin Abd al-Ala al-Sadafi told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Amr bin al-Harith and Ibn Lahi’ah told me, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abu Al-Khair, that he heard Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas saying: Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him, said to the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Teach me, O Messenger of God, a supplication that I may pray with in my prayers and in my house. He said: “Say: O God, I have wronged myself greatly, and do not He forgives sins except You, so grant me forgiveness from You, and have mercy on me. Indeed, You are the Forgiving, the Merciful.”"
"847","Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Ashjaj told us, Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, She said: When the revelation of God’s victory and conquest came to its end, I did not see the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying a prayer except that he said: “Glory be to You.” O God, and with Your praise, O God, forgive me.”"
"848","Muhammad bin Abbad bin Adam told us, Marwan bin Muawiyah Al-Fazari told us, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of his father, he said: We used to go out in the morning To the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the man comes, and the woman comes, and he says: O Messenger of God, how should I say when I pray? He said: “Say: O God, forgive me, have mercy on me, guide me, protect me, and provide for me, for He has given you this world and the hereafter.”"
"849","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawrqi told us, Ibn Ulayya told us, Mu’mal bin Hisham told us, Ismail told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, Abdul-Wahid bin Hamza bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr told me, on the authority of Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying during one of his prayers: “O God, give me a simple reckoning.” When he left, I said: O Messenger of God, what The easy reckoning. He said: “He looks at his book and ignores it. Indeed, whoever’s reckoning was discussed on that day, O Aisha, he perished, and all that “It afflicts a believer, and God pardons him for it, even a thorn that pricks him.” All of them have the same wording."
"850","Muhammad bin Aban narrated to us, Waki’ narrated to us, Ikrimah bin Ammar Al-Yamimi narrated to us, Abdullah bin Hashim narrated to us, Waki’ narrated to us, On the authority of Ikrimah bin Ammar, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: Umm Sulaym came to the Messenger of God God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and she said: O Messenger of God, teach me words to invoke in my prayer. He said: “Glorify God ten times, and praise Him ten times. And speak to him ten times, then ask him what you need, and he will say: Yes, yes.”"
"851","Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Ashjaj told us, Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I heard the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: “I have seen you being tried in the graves like the temptation of the Antichrist.” Amra said: Aisha said: So I was listening. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says in his prayer: “O God, I seek refuge in You from the torment of the Fire, and from the torment of the grave.”"
"852","Abu Abd al-Hakam told me that his father and Shuaib told them, saying: Al-Layth informed us, on the authority of Yazid ibn al-Had, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray in his prayers: “O God, I seek refuge in You from the torment of The grave, and I seek refuge in You from the temptation of the Antichrist, and I seek refuge in You from the temptation of life and death. Oh God, I seek refuge in You from sin and debt.” Aisha said: Someone said: How often do you seek refuge from debt, O Messenger of God? He said: “When a man is in debt, he tells a lie and makes a promise and breaks it.”"
"853","Ahmad bin Abdah al-Dhabi told us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, told us, Abu Hazim told us, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad al-Sa’idi, h and he told us Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi, Abd al-Aziz bin Abi Hazim told us, on the authority of his father, H. Ismail bin Bishr bin Mansour told us Al-Sulami, narrated to us Abdul-A’la, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, h. Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ narrated to us, Abdul-A’la narrated to us, Ubaid Allah narrated to us That is, Ibn Umar, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl ibn Saad, and this is the wording of the hadith of Hammad ibn Zayd. He said: There was a fight between the Banu Amr ibn Awf, and this reached the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he prayed the noon prayer, then he came to them to reconcile between them, then he said to Bilal: “O Bilal, if you come The afternoon prayer and I did not come, so he ordered Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. When the afternoon prayer came, Bilal called the call to prayer, then he remained iqama, then he said to Abu Bakr: Come forward. So Abu Bakr came forward and began the prayer, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and started to divide the people until he stood up behind Abu Bakr and said: He greeted the people, and when Abu Bakr entered the prayer he would not turn around. When Abu Bakr saw that the wailing was not being held back from him, he turned around and the Messenger of God motioned to him. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that is, let him go. When he said: Abu Bakr stayed for a while, thanking God for the saying of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Go ahead, then Abu Bakr al-Qahqari walked on his heels and delayed. When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw that, he came forward and led the people in prayer. He finished his prayer and said: “O Abu Bakr, what prevented you when I told you not to go?” He said: It was not for Ibn Abi Quhafa to lead the Messenger of God. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to the people: “If anything disturbs you in your prayer, let the men praise and the women praise.” And he said Ibn Abi Hazim in his hadith: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pointed to him like this, ordering him to pray, so Abu Bakr raised his hand. So he praised God, then the man who recited came back after him, and Abdul-Ala said in his hadith: “Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gestured to him, that is, as You.” Abu Bakr raised his hands and thanked God, and praised him for what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had said. Then the retreating man returned. Bakr: And some of them exceed others in hadith."
"854","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala told us, Sufyan told us, he said: I heard Abu Hazim, saying: Sahl bin Saad Al-Sa’idi, the companion of the Messenger of God, told us May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, Ali bin Khashram told us, Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, he heard it from Sahl bin Saad Al-Sa’idi, He says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever is disturbed by something in his prayer, let him say: Glory be to God, this is only for women” meaning applause. This is the hadith of Ali bin Khashram, and as for Abdul Jabbar, he narrated to us the hadith in its length regarding the departure of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to Bani Amr bin Awf, and at the end of it he said, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “What is the matter with you when something disturbs you during your prayer, you clasp? This is only for women. Something bothers him about his prayer, so let him say: Glory be to God. Abu Bakr said: Clapping and applause are the same."
"855","Yusuf bin Musa Al-Qattan narrated to us, Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, I am Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: We used to greet The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in prayer, and he responded to us. When we returned from the Negus, we greeted him, but he did not respond to us, so we said: O Messenger By God, we used to greet you during prayer and you would respond to us. Then he, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed there is a preoccupation in prayer.”"
"856","Bundar told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, and Yazid bin Harun told us, they said: Ismail, H and us, Abu Hashim told us Ziyad bin Ayyub. Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Shubail, on the authority of Abu Amr Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Zayd bin Arqam, He said: “The man beside him was speaking during the prayer, until it came down, and stand up to God in obedience, Surat Al-Baqarah, verse 238. He added in the hadith of Hushaym: So we were commanded to be silent. And we were forbidden from speaking.”"
"857","Yahya bin Hakim told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, Ismail bin Abi Khaled told us, similar to the hadith of Bundar, except that He said: “A man used to talk to his companion during prayer about a need, at the time of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, until the verse “And stand up to God in obedience” was revealed, Surah Al-Baqarah, verse 238. So we were commanded to remain silent.”"
"858","Abu Musa, on the authority of Yahya bin Hammad, on the authority of Abu Awanah, told us, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: We were greeting the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was praying similarly, and he said: He responded to us and said: “Indeed there is a preoccupation in prayer.” I said to Abraham: How do you greet? Are you? He said: I reply to myself"
"859","It was narrated by Bundar, it was narrated by Yahya, Al-Hajjaj, who is Al-Sawwaf, narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, H, and Abu Hashim Ziyad bin Ayyub narrated to us. Ismail bin Aliya told us, Al-Hajjaj bin Abi Uthman told me, Yahya bin Abi Kathir told me, and Muhammad bin Hisham told us, Ismail told us, Al-Hajjaj told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, H. Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Maimun told us, Al-Walid told us That is, Ibn Muslim, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya, and Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, Bishr, meaning Ibn Bakr, informed us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, Yahya narrated to me, on the authority of Hilal bin Abi Maimunah, Ata’ bin Yasar narrated to me, Muawiyah bin Al-Hakam Al-Sulami narrated to us, h. Ziyad bin Ayyub narrated to us, and Bishr, meaning Ibn Ismail Al-Halabi, narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, Hilal narrated to me Ibn Abi Maimunah, Ata’ Ibn Yasar narrated to me, Muawiyah Ibn Al-Hakam Al-Sulami narrated to me, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, we were talking about a covenant. During the pre-Islamic period, then God brought Islam, and some of us were practicing Islam. He said: “That is something they find in their chests, but it does not stop them.” He said: Oh Messenger of God, there are men who come to priests. He said: “Do not come to them.” He said: O Messenger of God, there are men among us who calligraphy. He said: “There was a prophet among the prophets.” He writes, and whoever agrees with his handwriting, that is it.” He said: While I was praying with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when a man from among the people sneezed, so I said To him: May God have mercy on you, so the people stared at me with their eyes, and I said: My mother is bereaved, why are you looking at me? He said: Then the people struck with their hands. On their thighs, when I saw them silence me, but I remained silent. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, left, he called for me, so he and my mother said, I have never seen a teacher before him or after him with better teaching than him, and by God, he never hit me, nor cursed me, nor cursed me, but he said: “Our prayer None of what people say is appropriate in this, rather it is the takbir, the glorification, and the recitation of the Qur’an.” This is the wording of the hadith of Maysara. Bandar said: While I was praying with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and so the rest said. Pindar said: When I saw them silence me, I remained silent. Abu Bakr said: I included in the major classification the hadith of the survivors following the similar hadith of Bundar, and I did not mention their words."
"860","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Abdul Wahhab, meaning Ibn Abdul Majeed Al-Thaqafi, told us, Ayoub told us, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He prayed The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, led us one of the evening prayers, and my greatest suspicion is that it was the noon prayer, two rak’ahs, so he came with a piece of wood in the direction of the qiblah. The mosque, so he placed his hands on her, one over the other, and the people quickly left, saying: The prayer has been shortened, and among the people were Abu Bakr and Omar. So they were afraid to speak to him, and a man with short or long hands is called: the one with two hands, so he said: Did you shorten the prayer or did you forget? He said: “You did not fall short, and I did not forget.” He said: “Rather, I forgot.” He said: “Did Dhu al-Yadayn speak the truth?” He said: Yes, so he prayed two rak’ahs, then he said the salaam, then he said “Allahu Akbar” and prostrated like his prostration or longer, then he rose.” Bundar mentioned the hadith. Abu said Bakr: I have covered this chapter in its entirety in the book of forgetfulness in prayer."
"861","Ahmad ibn al-Muqaddam al-Ijli told us, Yazid i.e. ibn Zurayi, Ruh ibn al-Qasim informed us, on the authority of al-Ala’ ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went out to Ubayy ibn Ka’b while he was praying, and Issa ibn Ibrahim Al-Ghafiqi, Ibn Wahb told us, on the authority of Hafs ibn Maysarah, on the authority of Al-Alaa ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, passed by Ubayy bin Ka’b while he was praying, and he called him. Ubayy turned and went to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Peace be upon him. He said: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of God. He said: Peace be upon you. What prevented you, my father, from not answering me when I called you? He said: O Messenger of God, I was in prayer. He said: “Do you not find in the Book of God that you respond to God and to the Messenger when he calls you when he revives you?” Surat Al-Anfal, a verse 24 “He said: Yes, my father and my mother. My father said: I will not come back, God willing.” This is the hadith of Ibn Wahb"
"862","Bundar told us, Yahya told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, Khubayb bin Abdul Rahman told me, on the authority of Hafs bin Asim, on the authority of Abu Sa’id bin Al-Mu’alla, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by me while I was in the mosque, so he called me, but I did not come to him, so he said: “What prevented you from coming to me?” I said: Indeed, I was praying. He said: Did not God Almighty say: O you who have believed, respond to God and to the Messenger when he calls you to give you life. Surat Al-Anfal, verse 24 Then he said: “Shall I not teach you the best surah in the Qur’an before I go out?” When he went to leave, I mentioned that to him. He said: “Praise be to God, Lord.” “The two worlds.” Surat Al-Fatihah, verse 2, “It is the Seven Repeated Surahs and the Great Qur’an that I have been given.”"
"863","Then Bundar told us from Shu’bah’s book, and Yahya and Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Khubayb, on the authority of Hafs bin Asim, on the authority of Abu Sa’id. Ibn Al-Mu'alla, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by me while I was praying, so he called me with something similar, except that he said: The greatest surah."
"864","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Salamah, that Abu Hurairah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, established the prayer, and we stood with him, and one of the Bedouins said during the prayer: O God, have mercy on me and Muhammad, and do not have mercy on anyone with us. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, greeted him, he said to the Bedouins: “You have become largely petrified,” seeking God’s mercy."
"865","Ibrahim bin Masoud bin Abdul Hamid told us, Al-Qasim, meaning Ibn Al-Hakam Al-Arni, told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Qaboos bin Abi Dhabyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed in Mina, and a word came out of him. He said: “So he heard it.” The hypocrites, and he said: They increased, so they said: He has two hearts. Do you not listen to his words and words in prayer? He has a heart with you, and a heart with His companions, so it was revealed: O Prophet, fear God and do not obey the disbelievers and hypocrites, to His saying: God has not made for a man two hearts within his belly. Surah Al-Ahzab, Verse 1 - 4\""
866"""
"866","Ahmad ibn 'Abdah narrated to us: Hammad — that is, ibn Zayd — informed us: al-Azraq ibn Qays narrated to us, saying: He saw Abu Barzah al-Aslami praying, and the reins of his mount were in his hand. When he bowed, the reins slipped from his hand, and the mount went off. Abu Barzah retreated on his heels, not turning around until he caught up with the mount, took it, then walked back as he was, then came to his place of prayer, completed his prayer, perfected it, then gave the salam. He said: ""I accompanied the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on many campaigns until he counted the campaigns. I saw his concessions and ease, and I adopted that. Had I left my mount until it reached the desert, then gone after it as an old man groping in darkness, that would have been harder on me."""
"867","Muhammad bin Aziz Al-Ayli told us that Salama told them, on the authority of Uqail, who said: Muhammad bin Muslim told me that Anas bin Malik Al-Ansari, He told him that while the Muslims were in the dawn prayer on Monday and Abu Bakr was praying with them, no one surprised them except the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He had uncovered the cover of Aisha’s room, and he looked at them as they were standing in rows in prayer, then he smiled and laughed: so Abu Bakr jumped on the He followed him to reach the row, and he thought that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, wanted to go out to pray, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, pointed to them. And he greeted you with his hand, “Complete your prayer.”"
"868","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala told us, Sufyan told us, Othman bin Abi Suleiman told us, and Ibn Ajlan told us, they heard Aamir bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubair, saying: I heard Amr bin Sulaym al-Zarqi, saying: I heard Abu Qatada, saying: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, leading the people, and on “His freedman is Umamah bint Zainab, so when he bows, he places it, and when he rises from prostration, he repeats it.”"
"869","Saeed bin Abdul Rahman Al Makhzoumi told us, Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Muammar, H. Muhammad bin Hisham told us, Yahya told us Ibn Al-Yaman, H. Abu Musa narrated to us, Abd Al-Ala narrated to us, H. Ya’qub Al-Dawrqi narrated to us, Ghandar narrated to us, H. Yahya bin narrated to us. Wise, Muhammad ibn Ja`far narrated to us, they said: Muammar narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of Dammam, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “ordered the killing of the two lions during prayer, the scorpion and the serpent,” and in the hadith of Ghandar, Muammar said, so I told him, He said: “The scorpion and the snake.” In the hadith of Abd al-Ala, Yahya said: He means the snake and the scorpion."
"870","Abu Bakr said: In the report of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad, Abu Bakr “did not turn around during his prayer, so when the people applauded a lot, he turned around,” Then, when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in the row, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pointed to him like this, ordering him to pray. I dictated it before it was too late"
"871","Al-Hussein bin Harith told us, Al-Fadl bin Musa told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Saeed, who is Ibn Abi Hind, on the authority of Thawr bin Yazid, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to turn right and left in his prayer, and would not twist his neck behind him. \His back\"""""
"872","Abu Musa Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna and Ahmad bin Al-Miqdam Al-Ijli told us, they said: Mulazim bin Amr told us, my grandfather Abdullah bin Zaid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ali bin Shayban, on the authority of his father Ali bin Shayban, who was one of the delegation, said: “I prayed behind the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he greeted, then he noticed with the back of his eye a man who did not straighten his head when bowing or prostrating.” Abu Bakr said: This news is not contrary to the news of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Indeed, I see from behind me as I see from in front of me, since the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sees May God bless him and grant him peace, and if he sees behind him during prayer, it may be permissible for him to look with the back of his eye at the one who is praying, so that he may inform his companions if They saw him doing this action because it is permissible for the praying person to do the same as what he did, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"873","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman Al-Muradi told us, Shuaib told us, Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, complained He greeted us, so we prayed behind him while he was sitting. He turned to us and saw us standing, so he pointed to us, so we sat.”"
"874","Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Ala’ narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Humaid ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Abu Sa’id al-Khudri, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw dirt in the direction of the mosque, so he rubbed it off with a pebble, and forbade the man from spitting in his hands. His right, and he said: “Let him spit from his left or under his left foot.”"
"875","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told me, He heard Abu Hurairah and Abu Sa`id al-Khudri say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw sputum in the qiblah, so he took it. A pebble, he rubbed it, then said: “None of you should spit on the qiblah or on his right, and let him spit on his left or under his feet.” \the left\"""""
"876","Bundar and Abu Musa told us: Yahya, who is Ibn Sa`id, told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Rab’i ibn Harash, on the authority of Tariq bin Abdullah Al-Muharbi said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you are in prayer, do not spit to your right, but Behind you, or facing your left, or under your left foot.” This is the hadith of Bundar, and Abu Musa said, Mansour told me, and he also said, he said, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: And he said: “And spit Behind you or facing your left if it is empty, otherwise so, under his left foot.”"
"877","Yusuf bin Musa told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Rabi’ bin Harash, on the authority of Tariq bin Abdullah Al-Muharbi, he said: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “When you are praying, do not spit in front of your hands, nor on your right, but spit where it faces your left. It should be empty, so open it under your left foot, then say it.” Mansour said: I mean, rub it with the ground."
"878","Bundar told us, Ishaq bin Yusuf told us, Al-Jariri told us, and Ya’qub bin Ibrahim Al-Duraqi told us, Ismail bin Aliya, on the authority of Al-Jariri, H. Al-Sana’ani narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, meaning Ibn Zurayi, Al-Jariri narrated to us, H. Abu Bishr Al-Wasiti narrated to us It is narrated by Khaled, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala’ ibn Al-Shakhir, on the authority of his father, “He prayed with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he soaked himself and rubbed it.” With his left shoe.” Khaled added more in his speech, and he was in a land of harsh conditions. Abu Bakr said: Abu Al-Ala is Yazid bin Abdullah bin Al-Shakheer, the brother of Mutarrif, whom they attributed to his grandfather. Abu Bakr said: This news was narrated by Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Al-Jariri, and he said: On the authority of Abu Al-Ala, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of his father"
"879","Yusuf bin Musa narrated to us, Al-Ala bin Abdul-Jabbar Al-Basri, and Al-Hajjaj bin Al-Minhal narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of his father, said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying, and spit under his feet. \The left one.\"" Al-Ala added: Then he rubbed it"""
"880","It was narrated by Yaqoub bin Ibrahim, it was narrated by Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, he said: It was narrated by Iyad bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, liked the fact that the pilgrims held them in his hand, so he entered the mosque one day, and in his hand was one. From it, he saw some scum in the direction of the mosque, so he ground them until he cleaned them out, then he turned to the people angrily, and said: “Would any of you like to A man meets him, and he spits in his face?! When one of you stands up to pray, he is only facing his Lord, and the Angel is on his right. He should spit between his hands, or on his right, and let him spit under his left foot, or on his left. If a gesture hastens him, let him say thus. At the edge of his garment, he joined some of it to another.” Al-Dawraqi said: Yahya showed us how he made it."
"881","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, Surayj told us, Falayh, who is Ibn Sulaiman, told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman In a long hadith he mentioned, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “If one of you is in his prayer, he should not spit In front of him, for his Lord is in front of him, and let him spit on his left, or under his feet, and if he does not find a spit, then on his clothes, or his sandals, until He will come out with it.”"
"882","Yusuf bin Musa told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Yahya bin Al-Jazzar, on the authority of Abu Al-Sahbaa, he said: We were at Ibn Abbas, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was leading the people in prayer, then two slave girls from Banu Abdul Muttalib came and fought. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took them and separated one from the other, and then he did not care about that.”"
"883","Abu Bakr said: I have previously dictated that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you is praying, he should not let anyone pass in front of him. He refused, let him fight him, for he is a devil.”"
"884","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, who was Ibn Dinar, who said: I heard Kurayb, the client of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: “I spent the night at my aunt Maimuna’s, and when part of the night had passed, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up to pray, and he mentioned some Hadith, and he said: Then I stood to his left and he turned me to his right. He said: Saeed bin Abdul Rahman Al Makhzoumi told us something similar, and he said: About Kurayb"
"885","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, Abd al-Razzaq told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas, who said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to point to \Prayer\"""""
"886","Abu Bakr said: I dictated the news of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir. “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, complained, so we prayed behind him while he was sitting. He pointed to us and we sat down.” Al-Rabi’ narrated to us, Shuaib narrated to us, Al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir"
"887","Muhammad bin Muammar bin Rabi’i Al-Qaisi told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, I am Ali bin Salih, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was praying, and when he prostrated, Al-Hasan jumped up, and Al-Hussein was on his back, and when they prevented them, he pointed at them. If they left them, then when he finished the prayer, he put them in his lap and said: “Whoever loves me must love these.”"
"888","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala told us, Sufyan told us, Zaid bin Aslam told us, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Omar, H. Ali bin Khashram told us. And Abu Ammar, Abu Ammar said, Sufyan told us, and Ali said: Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, he said: Ibn Umar said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered the Quba Mosque, and men from the Ansar entered to greet him, so I asked Suhayb: How did the Prophet do? May God bless him and grant him peace, if he was greeting him while he was praying? He said: “He was gesturing with his hand.” Abu Bakr said: This is the hadith of Abu Ammar. Abdul Jabbar added. Sufyan said: I said to Zaid: Did you hear this from Ibn Omar? He said: Yes"
"889","From Muhammad bin Al-Ala bin Kurayb, from Khallad Al-Jufi, meaning Ibn Yazid, on the authority of Zuhair bin Muawiyah, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me to the Banu al-Mustaliq. “So I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was riding a donkey of his. He was praying, so I was talking to him and he gestured to me with his hand.”"
"890","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, Ibn Wahb told us, he said: And Amr bin Al-Harith and Ibn Lahi’ah told me, on the authority of Yazid, and he Ibn Abi Habib, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman, who was the son of Shamasa, that he heard Uqba bin Amir say: We prayed with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. One day, he remained standing for a long time, then I saw him leaning down to eat something, and when he greeted him, he said: “There is nothing that you promised that has not been presented to me in my place.” This, until the fire was shown to me, and sparks from it came to me until this place came to me, so I feared that you would be overtaken.”"
"891","Issa bin Ibrahim Al-Ghafiqi narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, Rabi’ah bin Yazid narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Idris Al-Khawlani, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, that he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up to pray, then he extended his hand as if he was eating something, when He finished praying, we said: O Messenger of God, we saw you extending your hand. He said: “The enemy of God, Satan, came with a shooting star to put it in my face. So I said: I seek refuge in God from you, so he did not delay for three days, then I wanted to take him, and had it not been for the invitation of our brother Suleiman, peace be upon him, he would have become bound, playing Therein are the children of the people of Medina.”"
"892","Bahr bin Nasr bin Sabiq Al-Khawlani told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Muawiyah bin Saleh told me, on the authority of Issa bin Asim, on the authority of Zur bin Hubaysh On the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: We prayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the morning prayer. He said: While he was praying, he extended his hand, then He delayed it, and when he finished praying, we said: O Messenger of God, you did in this prayer of yours what you did not do in the prayer before it. He said: “Indeed, I saw Paradise.” It was presented to me, and I saw its clusters close by, its grains like bears, so I wanted to eat from it, so it was inspired to it to delay. So I delayed, then the Fire was presented to me, between me and you, until I saw my shadow and your shadow, so I motioned to you to delay, so I was inspired to Accept them, for you embraced Islam and they embraced Islam, and you emigrated and they emigrated, and you struggled and they struggled, but I did not see any superiority over you except through prophecy.”"
"893","Abu Bakr said: I dictated the news of Sahl bin Saad, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “If something bothers you in your prayer, let the men praise Him. And let the women forgive.”"
"894","We are Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala, Saeed bin Abdul-Rahman, Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Zuhri, and Ali bin Khashram. Ali said: He told me Ibn Uyaynah, the others said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Praise \For men"
"895","Al-San’ani Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, Khaled told us, meaning Ibn Al-Harith, Hisham told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, Muaqib told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was told about wiping in the mosque. He said: “If you \One subject\"""""
"896","Al-Dawraqi praised him, Ibn Ulayya told us about this, on the authority of Hisham, and said: On the authority of Mu’aqib"
"897","Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Sharhabeel bin Saad, on the authority of Jabir, who said: I asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about wiping pebbles in prayer, and he said: “One, and if you withhold it, it is better for you than a hundred she-camels, all of them black.”"
"898","On the authority of Bundar, on the authority of Salim ibn Nuh, on the authority of Yunus ibn Ubaid, on the authority of Zurara ibn Awfa, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, And he said: “God has transcended for my nation what they have told themselves about, something that cannot be spoken or acted upon.”"
"899","On the authority of Abdullah bin Hashim, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Harithah bin Mudharib, on the authority of Ali, he said: What There was a knight among us on the day of Badr other than Miqdad, and you saw us while there was nothing among us but asleep, except for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, under a tree praying. And he cried until the morning. Abu Bakr said: The story of Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God Almighty be pleased with him, when the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, commanded him to lead the people in prayer, so he was told: He is a gentle man who cries a lot when he recites the Qur’an, for that matter."
"900","Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad al-Anbari told me, my father told me, Hammad told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of his father, he said: I saw The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “prays while his chest buzzes like the buzzing of a boiler.”"
"901","Yusuf bin Musa told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: The sun was eclipsed one day. During the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up to pray, then he prostrated, and he could hardly raise his head. He blew and cried, and he mentioned the hadith, and said: Then he got up and thanked God, and praised Him, and said: “Fire was presented to me, so I started blowing on it, and I was afraid that \It deceives you\"""""
"902","Muhammad ibn Yahya and Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ubaid narrated to us, Shurahbil ibn Mudarik al-Ja’fi narrated to me, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Najiy Al-Hadrami, on the authority of his father, said, Ali said: “I had a status with the Messenger of God that no other creature had. I used to come to him So I greet him until he clears his throat and I go back to my family.” Abu Bakr said: They differed on this report from Abdullah bin Naji, so I do not remember anyone. He said: On the authority of his father other than Sharhabeel bin Aware. this"
"903","It was narrated by Amara bin Al-Qaqa’ and Mughirah bin Maqsim all together, on the authority of Al-Harith Al-Ukli, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah bin Amr bin Jarir, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Naji, on the authority of Ali. Jarir said: On the authority of Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Harith, and Amara, on the authority of Al-Harith: He says tasbih, and he said: Abu Bakr bin Ayyash, on the authority of Al-Mughirah: He clears his throat."
"904","Yusuf bin Musa narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, Al-Dawrqi narrated to us, Abu Bakr bin Ayyash narrated to us, both on the authority of Al-Mughirah, narrated to us Muhammad bin Yahya, narrated to us. Mu’alla bin Asad, Abdul Wahid told us, Amara bin Al-Qaqa’ informed us, with the words I mentioned."
"905","Imran bin Musa Al-Qazzaz told us, Abdul-Warith told us, Muhammad bin Jahadah told us, Abdul-Jabbar bin Wael told us, he said: I was As a boy, I cannot understand my father’s prayer. Alqamah ibn Wa’il told me, on the authority of Abu Wa’il ibn Hajar, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was He entered into prayer, raising his hands, then he said “Allahu Akbar,” then he said “tahf,” then he put his hands into his garment, then he took his left hand with his right.” Then he mentioned the hadith. Abu said Bakr: This is Alqamah bin Wa’il. There is no doubt about him. Perhaps Abd al-Warith, or someone below him, had doubts about his name. It was narrated by Hammam bin Yahya, Muhammad bin Hajarah narrated to us, Abdul-Jabbar bin Wael narrated to me, on the authority of Alqamah bin Wael, and Mawla To them, on the authority of his father Wael bin Hajar"
"906","Muhammad bin Yahya narrated to us, Affan bin Muslim narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, but it is not in the hadith of Affan, then he put his hands into his garment."
"907","We are Ali bin Khashram, I am Jesus, meaning Ibn Yunus, we are told by Abd al-Jabbar bin Al-Ala, we are Sufyan, we are Isa, Ibn Kurayb, we are Abu Usama, H., and Bishr bin Hilal, on the authority of Abdul-Warith, on the authority of Ayyub, all of them on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you sleeps during his prayer, let him lie down until sleep goes away from him, for one of you “If he prays while he is sleepy, perhaps he wants to ask for forgiveness and curses himself.” This is the wording of the hadith of Jesus. Abu Bakr said: There is evidence in the report that drowsiness does not interrupt prayer, because if drowsiness interrupted prayer, it would not have happened, according to what he, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said. And he said hello: He does not know, perhaps he will go and ask for forgiveness and curse himself, in a sense. He understood this saying that he only commanded us to depart from Prayer is the fear of cursing oneself when one wants to pray for it, not because it is not during prayer if one becomes sleepy."
"908","Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Ashjaj told us, Abu Khaled told us, H, Yusuf bin Musa told us, Jarir told us, H, and Ismail bin Bishr told us. Ibn Mansour Al-Sulaymi, Abdul-Ala told us all, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade May God bless him and grant him peace, that a man should pray briefly. And Ismail said in his hadith: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade shortening the prayer. \Prayer\"""""
"909","From us, Ali bin Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Mughirah Al-Misri, from Abu Salih Al-Harrani, from Issa bin Yunus, from Hisham, from Ibn Sirin, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Shortness in prayer is comfort for the people of Hell.”"
"910","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala and Issa bin Ibrahim Al-Ghafiqi told us, they said: Ibn Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me, and Issa said: On the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, that Bukayr narrated to him, that Kurayb, the client of Ibn Abbas, narrated to him, that Abdullah bin Abbas saw Abdullah bin Al-Harith was praying with his head tied behind it, so he stood up and began to loosen it, and the other one confirmed it for him. When he left, he went to Ibn Abbas and said: What’s wrong with you? And my head? He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Indeed, the likeness of this is the example of one who prays while he is folded.” Yunus said: And he He was crippled, so he stood up behind him, untied him, and made the other one stand up to him. Thus they all said: and the other agreed. Abu Bakr said: And the correct statement is confirmed"
"911","Abd al-Rahman bin Bishr bin al-Hakam told us, Hajjaj told us, Ibn Jurayj told us, Imran bin Musa told us, Saeed bin Abi Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of his father, that he saw Abu Rafi’, the client of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, passing by Hassan bin Ali, and Hassan He was praying, his two braids stuck into the back of his neck, so Abu Rafi’ untied them, then Hasan turned to him angrily, so Abu Rafi’ said: Accept your prayer, and do not Get angry, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “That is the grip of Satan,” saying: Satan’s seat means the place of his two plaits."
"912","Abu Bakr said: I dictated these reports."
"913","Narrated by Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala, narrated by Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: I heard Abu Al-Ahwas, saying: I heard Abu Dharr, saying: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Ali bin Khashram told us. Ibn Uyaynah told us. Al-Makhzoumi told us. Sufyan told us this. The chain of transmission, and they said in all of them: On the authority of: “When one of you stands for prayer, mercy faces him, so he should not wipe away the pebbles.” Abdul-Jabbar added, and Saad bin Ibrahim said to him: Who is Abu Al-Ahwas? He said: I saw the sheikh whom you described as such and such."
"914","Ahmad bin Al-Miqdam Al-Ijli told us, Yazid told us, meaning Ibn Zuray’, Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas Al-Laythi, On the authority of Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you stands for prayer, then mercy is facing him, so do not move the pebbles.”"
"915","Abu Bakr said: I previously dictated the story of Mu’aqib, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “If you are a doer, then one.”"
"916","Saeed bin Abi Yazid and Warraq Al-Faryabi told us in Ramla, Muhammad bin Yusuf told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abdullah bin Issa, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of Abu Dharr, who said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about everything. Until I asked him about wiping pebbles during prayer, and he said: “One or leave.”"
"917","Abu Bakr said: I dictated the hadith of Jabir before on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"918","Muhammad bin Isa told us, Abdullah, meaning Ibn Al-Mubarak, told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Dhakwan, on the authority of Sulayman Al-Ahwal, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “forbade prostrating during prayer, and for a man to cover his mouth.”"
"919","Ahmad bin Abdah told us, Abdul Aziz, meaning Al-Darawardi, told us, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Saeed Al-Khudri, On the authority of his father, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When one of you yawns, let him cover his mouth with his hand, for Satan will enter.”"
